scope: ledger
title: Category colours are eleven richer hues drawn as dots beside the name, and none of them is a flow colour
question: How are categories coloured, given docs/11's greyed eight and D-313's four flow colours?
answer: Eleven tokens --color-category-1..11 (light and lifted dark), names kept so stored colours keep meaning; count in domain/categoryColors.ts. A category is a dot beside its name, never a coloured background; none is a flow colour (flows are figures). Resolution per level (D-161) unchanged. docs/11 amended.
