title: Transactions is one page with By merchant and All rows, a row has one menu, Categories is a list and a panel, and a conversation can do all of it
question: How do Transactions and Categories follow the approved M28 U6 mockup?
answer: #/transactions (All rows, month-paged) and #/transactions/merchants (By merchant, replaces #/categorize) share a ViewSwitch. Filing a merchant ticks the rule by default; one Undo (undoCorrections + deleteRule); 1-6/drag into usual categories; session filings list. One ContextMenu per row (X leaves out, Space ticks); S2 pending card bills, S5 hint. Categories: tabs, list, panel, archive-unused. Tools set_excluded_from_totals, set_transaction_notes, set_card_payers, skip_merchants, edit_categories; parity ratchet 104 to 91.
