### D-316
date: 2026-10-02
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: A category on the Money moved tab is moved, not spent: inside saved, out of went out, and Home lists it
question: The author filed a transaction under Investments, on Categories' Money moved tab, and Home counted it as went out. What makes a transaction moved, and how does a wrong filing stay visible?
answer: The Money moved tab is every category whose kind is not EXPENSE and not INCOME (TRANSFER, SAVING, DEBT_PAYMENT); MOVED_KINDS in movedRepository.ts is the one list, read by the tab and by movedCondition. A transaction is moved when a declared format links it (D-309) or its category's kind is in MOVED_KINDS; one OR test so a row that is both counts once. Every total D-309 kept in step follows. Rows excluded from statistics (card bills) are never moved; moved is net (out minus back) so a withdrawal in a moved category nets against it. monthlyReport.moved lists the net per category and Home's Month shows 'Moved, not spent' under Where it went, so a wrong filing is seen. Amends D-309. Cost: loan payments (DEBT_PAYMENT) are now saved, and a lone Internal Transfer leg is saved; narrowing is a change to MOVED_KINDS and the tab follows.
state: amended

### D-317
date: 2026-10-02
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: A salary comes in once: the slip is the figure, the deposit that paid it proves it, and a gap is shown, never picked
question: Home counted a slip and the Salary-filed deposit that paid it as two incomes, and nothing asserted they agree. Which side is the figure, and how is agreement proved and a gap shown?
answer: The slip is the figure (its salary month); a deposit matched to a slip, exact or not, is in no income figure (salaryDepositCounts, coveredBySlip inside spendable; derived, never stored). A salary deposit is a BANK inflow whose text says salary or that is filed under a category named Salary. Exact nets claim slips first across all months, then the rest pair closest-first within a one-month lag. The ledger's own matchSalaries is the assertion, not an engine identity. Verdicts on the slip: AGREES (quiet), DIFFERS (gap, red), NO_DEPOSIT, UNCHECKED (no bank statement covers its pay month), and NO_SLIP on a deposit with none; shown on Home, Paychecks and in paychecks/month_summary in the same words (salaryBankWords). The 2,742 in question was two different months' slips: a month confusion. Amends D-078.
state: live

### D-318
date: 2026-10-02
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: A loan payment is spent, not moved: DEBT_PAYMENT leaves MOVED_KINDS, and its categories sit under Spending
question: Should a loan payment (DEBT_PAYMENT) count as moved, now that every kind on the Money moved tab does?
answer: No: part of a payment is interest, which is spent. MOVED_KINDS is TRANSFER and SAVING; the tab and the totals read that one list, so DEBT_PAYMENT categories show on the Spending tab and count as went out. TRANSFER stays moved, including a lone Internal Transfer leg. Amends D-316.
supersedes: D-316
