### D-319
date: 2026-10-03
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: Plan is one page: each fixed expense has its own say per plan, a divider trades between its neighbours, a bucket points at six things and wears the colour of what it points at
question: How do fixed expenses and the splitter become one screen, and what does a fixed expense do to a plan?
answer: #/plan is one page (#/plan/fixed and #/plan/splitter redirect). A plan_fixed_expense row per plan and expense says NET, SPLIT or IGNORE (no row = ignore; a payslip deduction is outside the choice, D-053); the two plan-wide settings are inert columns, converted to roles by installLedgerPack on open. A divider trades between its two neighbours (tradedAt, snap 50). A bucket points at goal, debt, category, fund, account or nothing (fund/account are FREE plus an optional link, since a held enum cannot widen) and is coloured by its target: category hue, saved green for goal/fund/account, neutral for debt/nothing. A remainder takes what is left after the in-split share. Tools: plans, plan_month, set_fixed_expense_roles, set_plan, edit_fixed_expenses.
state: live

### D-320
date: 2026-10-03
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: The plan's bar can turn into a ring: one set of outlines, two places for each point, and a preference that is the viewer's
question: How does Plan's bar become a ring without a second implementation?
answer: Bar/Ring switch; each segment is a sampled outline with a bar place and a ring place, t 0..1 slides points between them (ringGeometry.ts), PlanBar drives t by rAF 350ms and settles into the real bar or ring; reduced motion swaps. Dividers, drag (angle unwrapped across 12 o'clock), nudge, hover, ticks reused. Compare view keeps bars. Choice in localStorage fc-plan-view (D-115).
