### D-321
date: 2026-10-03
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: A change to a bucket flows only to the right, and a drag snaps to what the bucket is written in
question: How does a change to one plan bucket move the others, and what does a drag snap to?
answer: changedTo (splitter.ts): bucket k takes a value in its own unit; the difference comes from the buckets after it, next first then onward at zero, or goes to the next; a REMAINDER after it absorbs and ends the walk; locked are skipped; past the last the free money gives up to room (drag stops, typed overflows). tradedAt = changedTo + snap: fixed amount to 50 shekels, percent to whole percent (arrows 1%/10%). Typed figures keep precision; typed amounts commit on blur/Enter. Cause before: typing a percent went through redistribute (spreads over all other percents, left too), and a percent drag snapped in minor units.
supersedes: D-319
