question: How does Wealth match its approved mockup, where does an amount typed on Goals/Debts/Categories come from, and can the cushion count more than fixed expenses?
answer: Wealth's pages are built from src/ui/wealth/parts.tsx, a port of docs/mockups/m28-u8/wealth.html (headings, columns, order, prose as the mockup). Overview's In the bank = last statement balances + goal money held outside them. An amount typed anywhere but Plan (editGoalMonthly) is taken from Plan's what's-left bucket when there is one; Plan's own field keeps D-321. New buckets go before What's left in drawn order. Goals' Everything else = what's-left bucket of nothing + unassigned (everythingElse). split_bucket.in_cushion: a ticked CATEGORY/DEBT/FREE bucket (not What's left) adds its amount this month to the cushion's monthly figure; set on Overview, tool set_cushion buckets. New tool set_goal_amounts. Suggest goal amounts lives on Plan; remove-bucket confirm under its bucket; Points at is the mockup's tabbed popover and a new goal takes target, date, holding. createDebt/updateDebt run payment discovery.
