title: Columns move: the order is the declaration's, a header moves by its grip with a pointer or the arrows, and moving the first text column says the entries are called by another
question: How do a format's columns change order, and what happens to the naming column (the first text column) when one moves?
answer: The order is the declaration's columns list; a move changes no table and no entry. A header's grip (RowSheet onMove) drags, or takes Left/Right (mirrored in RTL) and Home/End; on an existing format it is a draft change saved from the panel (focus ORDER, sheet drawn by inDraftOrder), on a new format it reorders the draft. The naming column stays labelColumn (first text column): a move that changes it is said (orderChange) in the panel and in extend_format's dry run, not prevented - except on a pack's format, where declarationChangeRefusal refuses taking the naming from a pack column. A conversation passes extend_format `order` (every column once, new ones included; inOrder refuses a partial list).
