date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: Deleting a category moves whatever still uses it to a category of the same kind first, and is refused when there is none
question: What happens when a person deletes a category that rows, rules, budgets or children still use?
answer: deleteCategory(db, id, now, moveTo?) is the one write. In use (isCategoryInUse) = rows, a person's rules, subcategories, Plan buckets, fixed expenses (filed or matched), debts tracked by it, goals fed by it; corrections, re-apply undo, staged rows and built-in rules are history and are forgotten. Nothing uses it: deleted outright. In use: moveTo must be one of categoryDeleteTargets (live, non-system, same kind/tab, not itself or its child, top-level if it has children, not already feeding another goal); everything moves via merge's moveEverything (MANUAL stays MANUAL; debts and goals now follow in merge too), then it is removed. No target: refused, naming what uses it. System categories never delete. Screen: panel button, right-click menu, Delete key, with a DeletePanel picking the target; conversation: edit_categories delete:true + move_to, dry-run first.
