answer: A group belongs to a top-level category; a subcategory always takes its parent's (setCategoryGroup refuses a subcategory and carries children along; reparentCategory under a parent sets the parent's group; merged children take the survivor's). Groups are created (last in order) and renamed, names unique without case; no delete yet. Categories: group select with No group / New group… in the new-category form and the panel, heading pencil renames. Conversation: create_category `group` + `groups`; edit_categories `group` (null = none) + `groups` renames. Plan's inline new category has a Group field. Plan's bucket table derives headings (sectionBuckets): category buckets under their group in group order, goals under the group called Savings (own heading if none), the rest under Other, last; one section shows no heading; plan order stands within a heading and Move up/down swaps within it.
