### D-343
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: Add writes or says which row and cell stops it: the table is asked before the write, a column whose table drifted from its declaration is rebuilt while empty, and a refused foot row stays marked until written
question: Why did Add on a declared format do nothing at all, and how is a write that every check passed but SQLite refuses kept from being silent?
answer: A table checked start_hour/end_hour as dates while the declaration said time; SQLite refused the INSERT and the exception escaped mutate in a click handler. Now: tableRefusals (formatRowRepository) writes the batch in a rolled-back transaction and returns row+column refusals; stageRows and the entry page ask it, and FormatRows catches any write that still throws and says it on the page. Skipped on a query_only document (plugin dry run); the parity audit treats it as no write (TAKEN_BACK). The reconciler reads observe().sql and rebuilds an EMPTY column whose definition differs from what its declaration compiles to (on open and on adopt); a column holding data is left alone. The sheet's foot holds refused batches (FootState.held) and re-judges them every keystroke, so red clears when fixed and a later row's write never wipes an earlier refusal. Date, month and time open the native picker on click (NativePicker for text fields).
