### D-344
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A cell is read as it is typed and shows its reading while typed: 87, 87% and 0.87 are 87% and 1 is 1%, a time takes either clock, and the document keeps the currency a new amount starts in
question: How are a percent, a time and a currency typed into a cell, what does a person see while typing, and where does a default currency live?
answer: Percent cells go through readPercent (amends D-333): a % makes the figure the percent (0.5% is half a percent); a bare figure strictly between -1 and 1 and not zero is the fraction (0.87 is 87%, -0.2 is -20%); anything else is the percent, so 1 is 1% and the whole is written 100. Six places of a fraction (four of a percent), more refused. Bounds stay the percent figure (parsePercent). Sheet, entry page and record_format_rows share coerceValue, so a conversation gets the same answer. A percent slider writes its sign. Time: parseTime already took 14:30, 1430, 2:30pm, 2:30 PM; pinned in tests with the refusals. completion.ts (completionOf/settledText) is the engine's reading shown faint in the field's right padding while typing (87 -> %, 0.87 -> 87%, 230pm -> 14:30) and written into the field on blur; a refused text shows nothing. Currency: CurrencyField (ChoiceField with sign, code, name; search by any) on the sheet and entry page; signs bundled in domain/format/currency.ts; any 3-letter code still typed; a bare sign refused naming its codes; codes with unknown minor units (JOD, OMR) not listed. The document keeps a currency: document_setting (schema 57, key currency, CHECKed), settings.md in a text .emd when chosen; blankDraft offers it when no row above carries one. Asked on a money column's panel (ColumnQuestions), written on pick; record_units takes currency, formats prints it. A conversation's row still names its own currency (the engine does not assume it). Second exception to D-115's no settings in the document, asked for. Fixed on the way: a ChoiceField list inside a label reopened on pick.
state: live

### D-345
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A new format asks its name alone first; the sheet marks only the column the panel is open on; a saved column greys out *worked out* with the reason; and a format with no identity is created without a *Nothing does*
question: How should making a format read: what is asked first, how does the panel show which column it is about, why could a saved column not become worked out, and does the editor still need a 'Nothing does' step?
answer: NewFormat asks only the name (and the table name when it cannot be read off the title) until 'Add its columns' or Enter; a door's already-named draft skips it. RowSheet marks exactly one header (sheetMark in ui/formats/shape.ts): the column or derived column the panel is open on, or a placeholder header for one not on the sheet yet; surface + ink underline, not accent. A saved column's type tiles show 'worked out' disabled with 'Only a column not saved yet can be. Press + for a new one.' The editor no longer asks 'Nothing does': FormatDraft lost nothingMustHold and declarationOf writes nothingMustHold = no identities, so Create/Save with none is the saying; creationOf waits only on a name and a column; openingShape never opens on ADDS_UP for a missing answer. D-222 still holds for declare_format (nothing_must_hold) and .format.md (checks: none).
