### D-346
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: Worked out and must add up are offered side by side with one time example each; a formula field offers the format's names and marks the ones it knows in positive; a worked-out column is resized like any other and drawn on surface
question: How does a person tell a worked-out column from a must-add-up check, say hours = end − start as either, write a formula without guessing column names, and see and size a computed column in the grid?
answer: The What has to add up panel opens on two cards — Worked out (the app computes it; + A worked-out column adds a derived column and moves the panel to it) and Must add up (you type every figure, the app proves it; + A check opens a written-out identity) — both with the example hours = end − start. The per-column question asks 'has to add up from the other columns?' and its selects offer dates/times/instants: a point part takes off only a point of its kind and is never multiplied; with no figure to seed, it seeds the span of the first two points of one kind. Works out and Holds are one FormulaField (src/domain/format/formula.ts finds names; formulaNames offers own figures and points, one-hop link columns, totals): known names in positive (the app found it; accent stays for what can be pressed), unknown ones wavy-underlined negative once the cursor leaves the word; ↑↓ Enter/Tab completes, Escape closes the list not the panel. The grammar still decides meaning (D-224) and its own sentence is the only one shown; identity problems are not repeated under the panel. A check's name follows its first name until named. In RowSheet a derived column has the resize handle (width kept by name in format_column_view) and its header and cells are bg-surface.
state: live

### D-347
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A format sheet header's hidden controls take no width, so a narrow column shows its name; a timing assertion is held to the load it ran under, and a test's default budget is fifteen seconds
question: Why did a narrow format column show one letter of its name, and which test failed once in a full run?
answer: The header's move grip and Edit were opacity-0 but kept their width; now they are zero wide (still focusable) until a pointer or focus is on the header, the name is a truncating Bidi span, and the title gives the whole name then the note (RowSheet UNTIL_HOVER; headerControls.test.ts guards it). The flake: scale.test.ts held every read to 1s, and the monthly report takes ~0.69s quiet and 0.85s loaded; each read is now timed beside a summarizeTransactions pass and held to max(1s, 12 passes). Under triple load a plugin-tool test took 5.5s against vitest's 5s default, so testTimeout is 15s in vite.config.ts. Never retry a failed test.
state: live

### D-348
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: Groups and top-level categories are one tree, three levels deep: a heading is a top-level category, and a budget on any category counts everything under it
question: Groups and top-level categories both meant 'a heading that collects what is under it' (asked: don't they shadow the same thing?). Merge them, and what does a Plan bucket on a parent count?
answer: One category tree, three levels at most (src/domain/categoryTree.ts: placementProblem refuses a parent that is the category or under it, and a depth the category plus what it carries would take past three; a move needs the same kind; a system category takes no children). The seeded groups are seeded top-level categories (Health became 'Health & Fitness' since names are unique; Loan payments and the system categories stay at the top). A budget on any category counts it and everything under it (splitPlanRepository.spendUnder, used by bucketActuals and Home's budget lines); the breakdown rolls up at every level; 'with subcategories' descends two. Plan's headings are the top-level ancestor (sectionBuckets). Group select/New group/group rename are gone: the Categories panel's Under select and Move under reparent; create_category/edit_categories lose group/groups (refused with a pointer to parent_name/parent_id). Category.path is the whole path. category_group is in RETIRED_FORMATS: an older document keeps it as its own, and its category.group column, unread. No conversion of old documents.
supersedes: D-342
state: live

### D-349
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A total may fold a worked-out column, as each row shows it; a total of money carries its currency, and two currencies in one are no total
question: Can an aggregate fold a derived column of the rows it gathers, and what currency is a sum of money in?
answer: Yes: an aggregate's expression may name the source's derived columns (aggregateRejection via workedOutOf). The fold reads them out of the source view's SQL (derivedFiguresOf), so each row counts as shown, money rounded per row (D-333); a derived column naming such a total rounds per row in SQL too (workedFigure). AggregateValue carries currency for money (sums and latest/earliest); rows in two currencies are unchecked naming one row of each. inputsWithTotals hands the currency to every identity (sheet, entry page, staged header), so gross = total across currencies is unchecked. A money total prints as an amount (moneyText, aggregateSentence). The entry page's verdicts now fold totals and hops like the sheet's.
state: live

### D-350
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A link may be found by a date: written on a write while it is empty, stored as if picked, refused by name when no row or two match, and never over a person's link
question: How does a link fill itself from a date — work_day.paycheck from the slip of the day's month — without a read-time search or a guess?
answer: A link column may declare found_by: `date in period` (this row's date falls in the target's month; the target column is a month, or a date taken by its month) or `date on paid_on` (the same day). foundBy.ts owns the sentence and checks; the rule runs inside withRules on every generic write (stageRows, entry page, board move, record/update_format_rows, read_onto_format), before judging, and STORES the link. It fills only an empty link the writer did not change; no row or two refuses the write naming them; a link a person set or cleared is never moved; when the date changes and the link was the old date's own answer it is found again. Declaring it changes no existing row — an empty link is found when its row is next written. Schema 58 (format_column.found_by), language 18; in a .format.md it rides in the points-at cell (`paycheck, found by date in period`). Screen: Connections panel 'Found by'; header shows 'paycheck · found by date'. Tools: connect_formats found_by (alone adds it to an existing link), extend/declare_format columns found_by, formats prints it.
state: live

### D-351
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A fold is called a total wherever a person reads it, a total of money takes no unit, and the link-and-total gesture starts from either end
question: How does Connections make a total (an aggregate) read plainly enough that a person can make a paycheck's total of work days unaided?
answer: Every screen and refusal calls an aggregate 'a total' (port 'a total of…', 'X keeps a total of the Y rows whose z names it', 'The total x', 'A total needs a name'); the declaration word and connect_formats' key stay 'aggregate'. The total's line is the F5 FormulaField over foldNames (own figures and times, worked-out columns, one hop). foldType compiles the line as a derived column of the source: MONEY means no unit field and no unit written. NEW_LINK dropped on NEW_FIGURE is LINK_AND_FIGURE; a new link's panel has '…and T keeps a total of these rows'; an existing link's has '+ A total of these rows on T'. A folded pack says 'N formats inside — press to open' and 'Find a format…' opens the pack and centres the bubble. A format with no total points at Connections; a check's part that is a total reads 'a total of Y rows'.
state: live

### D-352
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: The connection window says what will be true in plain words: belongs to one… / has many…, one/many marks on the line, a headline built from the answers, and a total that opens on a suggested name
question: How should the window that opens after a drag on Connections say what a connection is?
answer: In the relationship, not the storage: ports read belongs to one… / has many…, a link column reads one Paycheck, the line has a fork at the many end and a bar at the one end. The window headline is built from the answers by headlineOf/edgeHeadline (Each work day belongs to one paycheck, and each paycheck counts its work days); questions are short (Which paycheck: I pick it / Match by date; Every work day must have one; Add up), the total is one sentence with blanks, name and note are folded. What will change is said (Adds a paycheck column to Work day), never a fmt_ table name; refusals get a plain headline per kind with the reconciler sentence verbatim under Exactly why. A new total opens as a count with a suggested name, and no refusal shows while a blank is empty. Delete asks foldsOver first. App menus, no <select>. The window caps at 55% height and the graph keeps its two formats in view.
state: live

### D-353
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A link found by a date is applied to the rows already there only when asked: apply_rules with link, and Apply beside Match by date, filling empty links and never a set one
question: How do rows entered before a link's found_by rule was set get linked?
answer: On demand only. planFoundLink/applyFoundLink (formatRuleRepository.ts, over foundBy.ts planFinds) fill every empty link of the format by its found_by; a set link is never touched or re-checked. A row with no target for its month/day, two targets, or no date stays empty and is named with why. A conversation uses apply_rules with `link` (format = the format the link is on; rule_set beside link is refused; a dry run with nothing to place invites no commit). On screen: the connection window shows 'N work days have no paycheck yet — Apply' beside Match by date while the saved rule is unchanged, Apply confirms with counts and reasons first, and saving a link that newly matches by date reopens the window on that question. Rejected: auto-apply on declare, a new tool, re-finding links already set.
state: live

### D-354
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A place links to an account, never merges with one: holding_place.account and the account's own cash holding made with it, and an account that holds things read as HOLDINGS beside a stored CASH
question: How does a money-map place relate to an account, where does that account's cash sit, and how is an account that holds things (a broker, a savings account) told apart when account.kind cannot grow a member?
answer: holding_place.account (optional, unique, never a card) names the account whose statements show the place's money; places without statements name none. setPlaceAccount makes the account's own cash holding (holding.account, unique; Cash/CASH/RECORDED/liquid) or adopts one picked in the place; relink keeps it, unlink clears the mark and keeps the holding; cashHoldingOf finds it. An account that holds things is model kind HOLDINGS, stored as kind CASH + holds_things=1 (D-216 forbids widening the enum), so every kind='BANK' query leaves it alone; accountBalances (In the bank) is BANK and CASH only. Merge re-points the place unless the survivor is named; delete unlinks. Screen: Money map place editor (Account, Its cash); tool: set_place_accounts; update_account takes HOLDINGS; savings shows Places and their accounts only when one is linked. No figure moves.
state: live

### D-355
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A row that names a holding is cash turning into it inside one account: transaction.holding and quantity, counted in no flow, and the holding's quantity a declared sum of its rows
question: How does a transaction say it bought or sold a holding inside its account, how do the totals treat it, and where does a holding's quantity come from?
answer: transaction and staged_row gain optional holding (link → holding) and quantity (decimal, 6 places; bought +, sold −; never money); a staged row's pair is carried by commit. heldCondition (movedRepository) puts such a row in no flow: statistics' spendable leaves it out, movedCondition is never true for it (not saved either), the filter total and monthlyTotals count it unsummed (TransactionSummary.held). holding declares aggregate quantity = sum of transaction.holding's quantity; holdingQuantity folds it via foldAggregate, unchecked when a naming row has no quantity. setTransactionHolding writes both or neither behind transactionHoldingProblem: holding at a place naming the row's account or naming none; never an account's own cash; quantity not zero. Screen: Transactions detail panel 'Bought or sold' (rows on an account a place names); tool: set_transaction_holdings. Older documents get the column and aggregate when the app opens them (the plugin never installs).
state: live

### D-356
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A transfer between two of your own accounts is one pair: matched by amount and date, suggested on every commit, answered once, and moved at the ordinary end and held at the end that holds things
question: How does a transfer between two of the person's own accounts (bank to broker, which carries no reference) stop counting as spending on one side and income on the other?
answer: A pack format transfer_pair (out_transaction, in_transaction — each unique — and user_decision PAIRED|NOT_PAIRED|PENDING). matchTransfers pairs a row leaving and a row arriving on two non-card accounts: same amount and currency, within 4 days, closest first, each row once; excluded, held, card-paying and already-paired rows are skipped, so a bonus with nothing leaving elsewhere stays unpaired. suggestTransfers runs after every commit (and on Accounts create/kind change) and writes PENDING; NOT_PAIRED is kept so neither row is suggested again. A PAIRED end on an ordinary account is moved (into saved); the end on a HOLDINGS account is held (heldCondition, no flow). Both read only where fmt_transfer_pair exists (keepsTransfers). Screen: Accounts queue, a notice, the detail panel's Transfer; tools: transfers, answer_transfers.
state: live

### D-357
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A goal is fed by one source: a Money moved category or the rows that name its holding, never both, and what a holding's rows put in is checked against a printed cost basis
question: Once a buy names a holding, how does a goal take its money without the transfer and the buys both counting?
answer: saving_goal gets fed_by_holding (optional boolean) beside deposit_category; setGoalFeed writes one and clears the other (goalFeedProblem judges: default holding needed, not an account's own cash, one goal per holding). syncGoalFeeds (was syncCategoryDeposits): a category feed reads its filed rows that are not held; a holding feed reads rows naming the holding (buy = deposit, sale = withdrawal), keyed by row; the bank transfer feeds neither. holdingPutIn/costBasisCheck: PROVED, FAILED by an amount, or UNCHECKED with reason — always unchecked until M30 U5 adds readings. Statistics' deposited now leaves out FROM_TRANSACTION deposits (their rows are already moved, or bought with moved cash) — fixes a double count in saved since D-324. GoalDetail select and set_goal_deposit_categories from_holding are the two halves; savings shows feed and check. The declared spending rollup is gross (moved and held lines included) and its note now says it is not Statistics' figure: a rollup filter cannot say not or is-empty.
state: live

### D-358
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A holding is worth its latest reading: a dated reading transcribed from a statement, growth derived from it and keyed by it, quantity × price a check only, and nothing on an account that holds things is income or spending
question: How does a goal fed by a holding know what it is worth now, and what do rows on an account that holds things count as?
answer: New pack format holding_reading (holding, as_of, value; optional quantity, cost_basis, price, statement, source, note; one a holding a day), written by record_holding_readings or the goal page's Record a reading via recordHoldingReading. Same figures again = UNCHANGED; other figures for that day refused unless correct:true (screen: Replace it). For a holding-fed goal, syncGoalFeeds keeps one GROWTH deposit per reading (source_key reading:<id>) = (reading − goal's put-in by its day) − previous, so the balance is the latest reading and can fall; goalWorth gives worth now and put in. Checks, never sources: cost basis vs rows put in by the reading's day (U4's check now proved/failed), quantity vs rows, quantity × price vs value (±1 unit or 0.1%; catches agorot), an account's own cash takes a value only and is checked exactly against the account's running balance. heldCondition now covers every row of a holds-things account: interest, bonus, rebate, fee are growth/loss of its cash, never income or spending. Separate fee rows are left for U6 to confirm on the real exports.
state: amended

### D-359
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A broker statement is read by the conversation and written in one batch: each row keyed by its value date, amount and the printed balance after it, the balances checked row by row, and the holdings table as readings
question: How does a broker's PDF statement get into the document, without an app reader, so an overlapping file does not duplicate rows and a misread figure is caught?
answer: A conversation reads the PDF and calls record_holdings_statement once per file (src/data/importer/holdingStatement.ts plans and writes through the screens' repositories): every movement in printed order with value date, signed amount (fees are inside it), the cash balance printed after it, and holding+quantity for a buy or sale; plus the holdings table and cash line as dated readings. It makes the holds-things account, links its place and makes missing holdings. Each printed balance must equal the previous plus the row, else the batch is refused at that row. natural_key = value date + amount + balance after (no description), so a half-year file over the months adds only what is new and the same file (by hash) reuses its statement. Amount-0 rows naming no holding are left out. The dry run shows cost/quantity/price/cash checks; failed checks are shown, not refused. Proved on copies of six real exports: every check proved; the broker puts the fee inside the buy.
state: live

### D-360
date: 2026-10-04
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: What is in the bank is the ticked accounts' latest statements, split between the goals saved there and the cushion as what is left; parts beyond the balance are a failed check, in the whole and per account, never clamped; the Emergency goal is no longer the cushion
question: How is what is in the bank split between the cushion and goals saved there, and what happens when the goals hold more than is there?
answer: in_cushion on a bank/cash account ticks it (Overview card, set_cushion accounts); a card or holds-things account never counts. In the bank = ticked accounts' latest statement balances; a ticked account with none leaves the split UNCHECKED. A goal's part = its deposits into a ticked account's own cash holding. Cushion = what is left, against months (ledger setting `cushion`) of fixed expenses plus ticked Plan buckets. Two checks: whole parts vs whole balance (failed -> cushion 'none', never clamped) and per account (names the short account; the cushion stands if the whole adds up). setCushionMonths makes no goal; an existing Emergency goal is an ordinary goal and counts as a part if saved in a ticked account. Code: src/domain/cushion.ts, src/data/repositories/cushionRepository.ts.
state: live

### D-361
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: In the bank leaves out what an account that holds things holds, and net worth keeps it; Home's Saved lists its three parts; the biggest charges are rows went out counts
question: Overview's In the bank counted goal money at a broker, Home's Saved could not say where its figure came from, and Home's biggest charges listed rows every total leaves out. What should each read?
answer: goalMoneyOutside splits liquid goal money into outside (added to the statements for In the bank, less set aside) and held (any holding whose account or whose place's account holds things); net worth adds held back so it does not move. Home's Moved, not spent becomes Saved: rows per moved category, per saving line off the month's slips (employee part), per goal deposit Saved counts, totalling summary.saved exactly (monthlyReport.savedFrom, same gates as payrollMonths and depositMonths); month_summary prints the same. largestCharges picks the month's biggest charges by spendable, so pays-a-card, moved and held rows are out.
state: live

### D-362
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: Every bank account and cash has its place, named as it, and its own Cash — made with the account and held on open; a place is not re-pointed between accounts in one step; a goal's money in a bank account's own Cash is inside its statement and counted once
question: A bank account read from a spreadsheet had no place and no Cash (only a broker statement made a place), so goal money could not be put in it; a place could be silently re-pointed from the broker to Everyday Bank; and once every bank account has its own Cash, goal money there would be counted twice in In the bank.
answer: createAccount gives a BANK or CASH account (not card, not holds-things, not archived) a place named as it (CHECKING/CASH) and its own Cash; ensureEveryOwnCash holds every document to it on open in the app (marks it unsaved) and after every plugin write, reusing a place already naming the account or an unnamed place with the same name. Naming the account from another place moves it and removes its place while that place is bare (isBarePlace). placeAccountProblem refuses re-pointing a place from one account to another: set it to none first; the Money map picker offers only the named account. goalMoneyOutside leaves a holding that is a bank account's own Cash out of outside, held and the set-aside subtraction while the account has a statement balance, so In the bank and Net worth equal the statement after a deposit there.
state: live

### D-363
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A goal asks one question, where is the money; the answer decides the rest — an account or a place kept by hand asks how much is already there, a holding bought by rows is followed; + New… makes a place in the same write; the category feed is the folded advanced choice; the goal form is one write both halves share
question: How does a goal say where its money is, and what follows from the answer?
answer: The goal form asks 'Where is the money?' over whereChoices (goalWhereRepository.ts): bank accounts by the account's name (their own Cash), each place that holds things with its holdings and cash, places kept by hand, each with its figure; a holding another goal follows cannot be picked. An account's Cash, a broker's cash, a by-hand or new place asks 'How much of it is already there?' (a Was already there deposit dated today, asked only when the place is new to the goal; more than the last statement warns). A holding in a place an account's statements show is followed by its rows (fed_by_holding) and typing into it is refused. '+ New…' makes a place and its one holding in the same write. saveGoalAnswer writes goal + place + deposit + feed in one transaction; the form, Plan's new goal and create_saving_goals (already_there, already_there_on) all use it; goalAnswerProblem is the shared judgement. The Money moved category is the folded advanced choice and replaces the answer's own way. GoalDetail has its own Edit (opens the same form via ?edit=, returns to the drawer), no feed menu, and says 'Where is the money? Not said yet' with Say where instead of hiding add buttons. The Emergency kind left the form; an old one keeps its months until a target is typed. Parity's without-a-screen ratchet rose to 5 (setGoalFeed, updateGoal reached through saveGoalAnswer).
state: live

### D-364
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A goal whose money is a bank account's own Cash can count the confirmed transfers into it: ticked under the account's answer, off by default; arriving is a deposit, leaving a withdrawal, after the latest Was already there; a third feed, one goal per account, and a pair it reads is no category's
question: How does a goal kept in a bank account count the transfers into that account without a Money moved category and a rule?
answer: saving_goal.fed_by_transfers is a third feed beside deposit_category and fed_by_holding (one per goal; setGoalFeed clears the others; transferFeedProblem refuses anything but a BANK/CASH account's own Cash, a broker's cash included, and a second goal on one account). syncGoalFeeds reads every PAIRED transfer_pair with an end on that account, counted in totals: the arriving end is a deposit, the leaving end a withdrawal, keyed by the row, dated after the goal's latest Was already there in that holding. Both ends of a pair it reads are claimed, so no category feed counts them too. The goal form shows 'Transfers into <account> are for this goal' under a bank account's answer, off by default, clearing and cleared by the fold's category; GoalAnswer.transfersIn; saveGoalAnswer writes the money already there before the feed. Tools: create_saving_goals and set_goal_deposit_categories take from_transfers; savings names the feed. The parity audit's ONE_WRITE_FORMS (saveGoalAnswer) lets a surface reaching a form's one write reach the writes it calls by name; allowance without a screen back to 3. Plan's new-goal form says 'Where is the money?' with whereChoices' names (F3's picker does not fit its popover).
state: live

### D-365
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A holding with a reading is worth its latest reading wherever it is shown, whether or not a goal follows it; growth is the reading less what went in by its day; the Money map's unseen figures go; an account's bare place goes with it
question: What is a holding with readings worth when no goal follows it, and where is that figure shown?
answer: Its latest reading on or before the day plus what moved after the reading at cost (holdingWorths in src/domain/holdingReadings.ts, loaded by holdingWorthInput/holdingWorthsOn), used as a D-186 valuation that replaces the holding's sum of deposits on the Money map, Overview, the savings tool, net worth (cut per month) and the unchecked-holdings list. Growth = reading minus the holding's rows put in by its day; an account's own cash has worth and no growth. Goals still hold their deposits; a goal fed by its holding agrees by construction. Overview's held (D-361) is these readings for accounts that hold things, counted once. The Money map's own figures, goal-by-place table and funds list are removed (only drawn outside Overview, where nothing rendered it). Deleting or merging a bank account removes its bare place (isBarePlace now lives in accountRepository). Amends D-358: no growth deposits for a holding no goal follows, but it has a worth and growth.
state: live

### D-366
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: Net worth is everything owned, each once: every holding not liquid and not inside a statement counts on Overview, as it already did in Home's net worth and the savings tool
question: Overview's Net worth left out a locked holding that is not a fund (a fixed deposit), while Home's net worth and the savings tool counted it. What should Net worth count?
answer: Everything owned, each once: statements + goal money outside them + held at accounts that hold things + every non-liquid holding not inside a statement (latest reading where it has one, deposits otherwise; unknown holdings counted locked as netWorthAt does) + funds, less debts. goalMoneyOutside gains `locked`; Overview's In the bank and Net worth come from one function, bankAndWorth in netWorthRepository.ts. In the bank is unchanged. Home's net worth reads no statement, so it agrees on every holding without equalling Overview's figure. Rejected: making netWorthAt read statements.
