### D-368
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: Read it keeps the reader, so a statement's columns are mapped once; a statement dropped on a document without the ledger is held and offered one; the empty window says which button keeps money; reader is the one word for reader / mapping / layout / template
question: How does a first statement get read in fewer steps, and what is the one word for the thing that reads a file's columns?
answer: The mapper has one filled button, Read it, and it keeps the reader: makes a new one under the name in the bar, repairs an edited or moved one in place (D-031), leaves an untouched exact match alone; the kept id goes into the sheet so Write teaches the reader its account and next month's file skips the mapper and the account question. Account kind stays guessKind pre-selected in a select (the confirm). A statement dropped or picked in a document with no ledger is held in App state and NoLedger offers 'Keep a ledger here and read it' / 'Not now'. The empty window gives New document and New ledger one line each; New ledger's says it is for money. On screen the word is reader (No reader yet, your reader); code keeps mapping; M31 U8 follows. First run: 5 steps by New ledger, 6 by New document (was 6 with Save, ~11 by New document).
