### D-369
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: 50/30/20 lands on the person's top-level categories, each share divided by what went out under them, asking only about headings it cannot place; with no payslip, take-home pay is the salary that came in; a budget set with no plan makes the plan
question: How does a first plan become a working budget for a document with statements and no payslip, in one step?
answer: Start with 50/30/20 makes one CATEGORY bucket per top-level category (domain/starterPlan.ts): needs 5000bp, wants 3000bp, saving 2000bp, each divided among its headings by outflow under them (subtree) over the last 3 ledger months, via distribute; zero-spend headings beside spending ones get none; no spending -> even; a share with no heading -> one unpointed bucket in its own name; existing bucket on a category is reused. Seeded ids living/transport/health/family/obligations=needs, lifestyle=wants, savings=saving; SAVING kind=saving, DEBT_PAYMENT=needs; income/transfer/system out. Only person-made top-level expense headings are asked, in one 'Which are these?' list on Plan's empty state (Needs/Wants/Saving/Leave out), no default. resolveBasis falls back to salaryLanded (salary deposits by month) when a slip basis is unavailable and the document has no slips: newest month for last paycheck, average of N for average; Plan says 'No payslip yet — the salary that came in, <month>'. setCategoryBudget with no plan creates the default plan (screen and edit_categories); clearing makes nothing.
state: live

### D-370
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: A month's plan is a row, given with a checkbox and kept when the plan is edited; the comparison is the bar itself; a 50/30/20 plan's buckets remember their share
question: How does a month get a plan, where does the plan-versus-actual comparison live on Plan, and how does a 50/30/20 plan still read as 50/30/20 once it is one bucket per category?
answer: A plan_month row (month unique, plan link; a ledger-pack declared format, no migration) says which plan a month is on; a month with no row is on the default. The pack moves applied_to_period onto a row on open and empties it (inert). Plan's 'Months on this plan' is 12 checkboxes (setPlanMonths; plan_month's months/back_to_default); a month keeps its plan when the plan is edited. 'Use for the month' is gone: a record line appears only when the month is on the plan and a goal/debt bucket has something to record. The comparison is always on screen: Against (default last whole month) fills each bucket and the bills piece in its top line's colour up to what it got, over = a bar at the right end, no red/green; table has Planned and Got in <month>. split_bucket.share (NEEDS/WANTS/SAVING) is set by the starter, which orders Needs, Wants, Saving, biggest first, once; sectionBuckets heads by share, no headings without shares; bucket menu has 'Counts as'. Plan says Bills.
state: live

### D-371
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: Every bank account and cash counts toward the cushion until it is unticked; with no bills the In the bank card tracks them in place, and Plan's cushion line sets the months there
question: Must a person tick each bank account and visit Plan for bills before the cushion says met or short?
answer: No. in_cushion empty counts; only a written 0 leaves an account out (amends D-360's none-ticked start; no conversion). With no bills, Overview's In the bank card lists billCandidates with CandidateCard (Track it / Change… / Not a bill), linking to Plan's Add a bill only when none is found. Plan's CushionPanel sets the months (MonthChoice) and Plan buckets (CountFromPlan) in place; Overview keeps only which accounts count. The goal's Emergency kind was already out of the form (D-363); the unused formatMonths went. Fixed expenses are 'bills' on both surfaces.
state: live

### D-372
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: A form makes what it needs in place: a select whose last option is + New…, and the category picker always offers it
question: How does a form let the person make a thing it needs (a holding, an account, a category) without sending them elsewhere first, without building a framework?
answer: One small piece, SelectOrNew (src/ui/components/SelectOrNew.tsx): a native select whose last option is + New…, opening a caller-supplied form that returns the new id; NewByName is the usual form (name + optional kinds, writes on Create through the existing create function, Enter never submits the outer form). Applied to a deposit's holding (makePlace, lifted from goalWhereRepository), a place's account when it names none (createAccount), a goal's feed category (a + New… choice in its list, createCategory kind SAVING). CategoryPicker shows + New… when nothing is typed (covers rule and bill categories) and its outside-click reads composedPath so the row works by mouse. Left alone: bucket category (PointsAt already makes), WherePicker (deferred write), debt hint (a debt is its whole form), BankSplit's Add a bill link (D-371), Goals' Make one on Plan (a plan is not picked from a list).
state: live

### D-373
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: One way to make a rule from a row: the offer, which matches by contains, files the rows already here by default, and asks for its category
question: There were three ways to make one rule from a row (By merchant's tick, the correction offer with three buttons, the detail panel's button to the editor) and two match kinds (exact vs contains). Which one offer, which one match, and what about the rows already there?
answer: Every rule made from a row is a CONTAINS rule over the normalized merchant, the pattern an editable field (learnedDraft). Exact missed every merchant whose name changes past a trailing branch number (a city after it, an order reference, a long terminal number) silently every month, and a shortened pattern matched nothing as exact; contains can over-claim, but the offer counts the rows it would file before writing. The row menu's 'Rule from <merchant>' / 'Rule from the words you highlight' and the detail panel's 'Make a rule for this merchant' open the same inline offer (offerForDraft) as a correction: a category picker, the pattern field, 'No rule' / 'Make the rule', and 'Also file the N rows already here' ticked by default when N > 0 (pastRows, the same planReapply the write runs). By merchant's tick writes the same CONTAINS rule. A Rules button sits in the Transactions and Categories headers; editing rules, the provider-category rule and By merchant's 'Write a rule for…' stay on Settings > Rules. Existing EXACT_MERCHANT rules are not converted. Supersedes the ledger's D-042 on the match kind.
state: live

### D-374
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: engine
title: Putting a pane away steps back to the list's own history entry rather than pushing a new one; Back and Forward arrows by the document's name; Open recent beside Open; the window never scrolls as a page
question: Why did the mouse's back and forward land somewhere unexpected, and what do the arrows, Open recent and the whole-window scroll do?
answer: The stray entries came from the list-and-detail pane: Escape, scrim, Close and ClosePane navigated to the list, pushing a second list entry, so Back reopened the pane. ListDetail now remembers the history idx the list was on (module-level, since the routed screen is keyed by path) and closing is navigate(listAt - here), or a replace when no list entry is behind it; details close through useClosePane (outlet context). The goal drawer's Edit and its return replace. The palette's Go to the current screen replaces. HistoryArrows (title bar) are navigate(-1)/navigate(1); Forward is counted from pushes vs pops. Open recent is a ChoiceField of the shell's recents beside Open…, absent in a browser tab. The app root is overflow-clip so nothing (the 4px view entrance, a popover) makes the page scrollable.
state: live

### D-375
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M31
scope: ledger
title: One name for one thing: reader, Where the money is, left out of totals, card payment, bill, and a bucket is for something; Wealth's first tab is Net worth and its accounts section Balances, so Settings › Accounts is the one screen called Accounts
question: Which one word does each thing get on the screens and in the plugin's text, where several were in use?
answer: Kept ← retired (text only; identifiers, tables, routes, tool and parameter names keep theirs): reader ← saved mapping / template / stored format / layout-as-reader (a file's shape is a 'kind'); Where the money is ← sits / held / 'Deposits usually go to' (place and holding stay two things); left out of totals (leave out) ← exclude / excluded / 'Exclude these from spending' / 'never counts as spending' / 'Excluded from statistics'; card payment ← settlement / card charge / card bill ('This pays a card' stays as the action); bill ← fixed expense / standing commitment / monthly obligation; bucket, and a bucket is 'for' something ← budget / points at (a category's figure is its Plan bucket; format links still 'point at'); Net worth ← Overview (Wealth's first tab); Balances ← Accounts (the section on Net worth). Two Accounts screens are named apart: Settings › Accounts makes and sets up accounts, Net worth › Balances reads what is in them.
state: live

### D-376
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A bank or cash account's own place adds up to its statement: each goal saved there is a row with its part, and its own Cash is what no goal has taken; parts beyond the statement are a failed check; nothing stored, and no total moves
question: What does a bank or cash account's own Cash show, and how does its place add up, when goal money saved there is inside the statement balance?
answer: While the account has a statement balance, its own place's figure is that balance plus any other holding there; each goal saved in its Cash is a row with its part (goalParts in savingsRepository.ts, the cushion split's parts, read by cushionSplit over that one account); the Cash row 'Cash, not for any goal' is the balance less the parts. Parts beyond the balance are a failed check (none, and by how much), never negative or clamped. Derived on read in documentMoneyMap (withStatements) and shown on Wealth's places, the Money map and the savings tool; liquidity, In the bank, Net worth, Home and the cushion still read deposits and do not move. Overview lists the account once at its place's figure; Home no longer asks about such a Cash. A holds-things account's Cash stays its latest reading (D-365). No statement balance: Cash stays the deposits.
state: live

### D-377
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: A link that stops being a card payment leaves the bank row's left-out-of-totals flag as it is; a written payslip runs the same payroll sync from a tool as from a screen
question: When a stale card-settlement link is dropped, should its exclusion be undone, given is_excluded_from_stats cannot tell a link's exclusion from a person's? And where does a payslip's post-save work (goal deposits, debt payments) run so a conversation's slip feeds them too?
answer: Dropping a stale settlement link no longer touches is_excluded_from_stats (amends D-069's undo): a hand answer is never cleared, and a row left out wrongly is visible and one click back; M36 U04 moves the settlement answer off the flag. syncPayroll (payrollSyncRepository.ts) runs syncPayrollDeposits then syncDiscoveredPayments; Paychecks save/delete, DeductionTypes link and record_paychecks all call it. Not in the after-write hook: the debt scan reads every transaction and most writes have nothing to do with payroll.
state: live

### D-378
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: engine
title: Every plugin open brings the ledger up to what this build declares, in memory, and a write saves it with its change; no repository probes for an older shape, and an older text document is refused from its header
question: Must a conversation wait for the app to open a document after a pack change, and may repositories read older pack shapes?
answer: No. bringUpToDate (data/packs/packs.ts) — installLedgerPack plus every account's own cash, where the document keeps a ledger — runs in the app's open and in the plugin's gated open for every read and write. Reads keep it in memory unsaved; writes run it under the lock before the work and save it with the change; a refusal is PACK_REFUSED. Schema migration is still refused by the plugin (D-093). Every probe for an older pack or engine shape is gone; an older text document opens as an empty document at its header's schema so the gate refuses it without rebuilding. Ledger-only after-write steps (syncGoalFeeds, ensureEveryOwnCash) run only when documentHasLedger.
state: live

### D-379
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: The ledger reads the figures its formats declare — a debt's balance, a goal's totals, a payslip's unexplained and saved, a fund's latest — and a reading's price check is an identity
question: Where the ledger's formats can declare a figure, should its code still re-add the rows in TypeScript?
answer: No. debt_payment.principal_part; debt totals principal_paid/total_paid/unconfirmed/unconfirmed_count and worked-out outstanding/interest_paid/progress; saving_goal balance/opening/growth/liquid and put_in/progress; paycheck saved_employee and unexplained (gross - deducted - net); fund_account.balance picks latestSnapshot. Read through packs/ledger/figures.ts (declaredFigures: the view's SELECT with totals read as worked-out columns, one query; latestOf for a latest). principalOf and the debtBalance sums are deleted. A payment/deposit in another currency makes a debt or goal UNCHECKED (DebtBalance union, GoalProgress.unchecked), not a smaller sum. holding_reading price is the identity value = quantity * price * 100 ± 0.1% (was one unit or 0.1%; assumes hundredths). Drafts, balanceOverTime/projectPayoff, contributed/withdrawn stay code; employer/tax totals wait for U04. Pack installs derived columns in its second pass. Ledger tools on a no-ledger document refuse in one sentence (noLedgerRefusal in the plugin's read/write path).
state: live

### D-380
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: engine
title: A filter can say is not, is one of and is empty; the ledger's declared spending is the one rule for what counts, and the person's left-out flag is only theirs
question: How does a total or rollup say 'not a transfer', 'no holding' or 'one of these kinds', and where does the ledger's rule for what counts as spent live?
answer: A filter is still one column: `is X`, `is not X` / `is not one of X, Y` (an empty cell, or empty link, passes — never unchecked), `is one of X, Y` (empty is undecided, as `is`), `is empty` / `is not empty` (any column but a list). Language 19; stored in format_aggregate.where_member as what follows `is`. transaction.spending declares the rule (direction OUTFLOW, is_excluded_from_stats false, counted_on_card not true, holding empty, account.holds_things not true, category.kind not one of TRANSFER, SAVING); statisticsRepository.spendable, monthlyTotals/summarizeTransactions' went-out and fixedExpenseRepository.actualsByCategory read it via rollupFilterSql/spendingRuleSql. Code beside it: pointedAtCondition (person-declared links, paired transfer ends) and the salary match. A settlement writes the new optional counted_on_card column (cleared with a stale link); a salary answer is read in salaryCoveredRefs; is_excluded_from_stats is only the person's. Other totals read countsCondition. The pack rewords a rollup it owns on install. paycheck declares employer_paid, tax, compensation, tax_rate.
state: live

### D-381
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: engine
title: A worked-out column reads the latest; a holding's worth is declared, and a goal's feeds are worked out on read, never stored
question: Can a derived column read a latest/earliest total, how much of a holding's worth and growth can be declared, may a derived column read a neighbour's total through its link, does a hand-typed deposit count as put in, and must feed deposits be stored?
answer: Yes: a derived column reads latest/earliest (correlated ORDER BY LIMIT 1, empty on a tie, an undated taken row, no row or an undecided filter), language 20. holding declares reading (latest holding_reading by as_of), bought (sum of -amount over transaction.holding where is_excluded_from_stats is false), deposited (typed MANUAL/FROM_PLAN/OPENING_BALANCE deposits into it) and put_in = bought + deposited; holdingWorths(db, currency) reads them. Ruling 1: worth stays the latest reading plus what moved after its day (rows, typed deposits; an account's own cash: its rows), and that part and growth = worth - put_in stay code, because a holding sold whole after its last reading would otherwise keep the reading forever. Ruling 2: no hop through a neighbour's total yet - a goal's figure depends on which feed it has and an expression cannot choose; feeds are worked out on read in TS (fedDeposits). Ruling 3: a hand-typed deposit is money put in (U01's finding was a bug); one typed after the reading is in the worth. saving_deposit stores only typed kinds; listDeposits returns typed + fedDeposits (ids fed:...); syncGoalFeeds and syncPayrollDeposits are gone (syncPayroll keeps the debts); goalFigures adds fed deposits to the declared balance/growth/liquid; bringUpToDate removes stored copies an older build left (dropStoredFeeds).
state: live

### D-382
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: The ledger declares its waiting questions as start views — transfers, card settlements and payments to confirm — and Home counts what they find; a start view's `is` takes true or false on a boolean
question: How does a ledger document answer start_here, and where do Home's waiting counts come from?
answer: src/data/packs/ledger/views.md declares start views: transfer_pair and card_settlement_link at user_decision is PENDING, debt_payment at is_confirmed is false. installLedgerPack gives a format the pack's view of a kind only when the document has none of that kind. A start view's `is` takes true/false on a boolean (an empty boolean is neither). Home's waitingItems counts them with startCount/waitingIn; pendingTransferCount and pendingSettlementCount are gone. Detected bills are not a view: DETECTED_PENDING is never stored, billCandidates works them out on read.
state: live

### D-383
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: Net worth is one figure — everything owned, each once, less what is owed — read by Overview, Home and the savings tool from the declared parts plus the statements
question: Net worth was computed four ways (Home's from deposits with no statements, Overview's bankAndWorth, the savings tool's Total with no debts, the money map's display override). Which one is it, and where does it live?
answer: One netWorth(db, asOf, currency) in netWorthRepository, arithmetic in domain netWorthOf; Overview, Home and the savings tool read it. Overview's meaning: In the bank (last statements + liquid money outside them − set aside) + held at accounts that hold things + locked holdings outside a statement + funds' declared balance − debts' declared outstanding. A debt with payments in two currencies is the gap UNCHECKED_DEBT, not summed. asOf cuts deposits only. Set aside is taken off only while some account has a statement balance. The savings tool's Total row is now Net worth with its parts. netWorthReport/netWorthAt/netWorthOver/trailingMonths/bankAndWorth/goalMoneyOutside and NetWorth.total/assets/reachable/liquid are deleted. The money map's withStatements stays display only.
state: live

### D-384
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: A bank account's own cash is in no place: a place is an account's because the account's own cash is in it, holding_place.account goes, and a required column made optional keeps its values
question: Every bank account had an automatic place plus its own Cash, and a place named its account by holding_place.account, so Wealth showed each account several times. What does an account's money belong to, without a place per account?
answer: A bank/cash account's own Cash holding (holding.account) is made with the account in no place; holding.holding_place is optional. A place is an account's because the account's own cash is in it (HoldingPlace.accountId is derived); holding_place.account is emptied and dropped by the ledger install (RETIRED_COLUMNS). A placeless cash reads as the account's own row, id account:<id>, in listHoldingPlaces/findHoldingPlace/Holding.holdingPlaceId, so today's screens group by account or place unchanged; place edits refuse it, and adding a holding there makes a real place named as the account and moves the cash in. Naming an account from a place moves its cash there (and drops an old bare place); unlinking keeps D-354. Delete/merge/made-a-card let go of the cash (gone if unused, else kept in a place). The plugin's per-write hook went; on open ensureEveryOwnCash stays, placeless. Engine: a required column made optional over rows is LOOSEN_COLUMN (copied through a nullable twin, every value kept), and the install applies a loosened column. Old automatic places stay and read as the account, untouched.
state: live

### D-385
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: Net worth is one table — one row per account or place, then the funds and the debts, adding up to netWorth; the cushion is a column of ticks and a line; an account with holdings is one name; and a bank account's own cash is made with it, never on open
question: How does Wealth show each bank account once, and what happens to an account an older build left without its own cash?
answer: #/wealth is one table (netWorthTable in ui/wealth/netWorthRows.ts): Bank accounts and cash, Accounts with holdings, Places kept by hand, Funds, Owed; its last line is netWorth().worth and a test holds the rows' sum to it. A bank row opens to its statement and check, the opening balance (Change/Set), BankSplit's bar for that one account (goal parts, then Cash, not for any goal), the lines, and Add a holding here / Merge into / Rename / Archive; places and accounts with holdings open to their holdings. Balances, BankSplit's section, Where the rest is and MoneyMap.tsx are gone; #/wealth/places redirects; the cushion is a tick column plus CushionLine. User-visible text says 'account with holdings' (HOLDINGS / holds_things). A bank or cash account's own Cash is made by createAccount (and setAccountKind from a card) only: ensureEveryOwnCash and its on-open run in bringUpToDate are gone, as are the ensures on unarchive and after a merge — no old-document support.
state: live

### D-386
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: engine
title: A pack can rebuild its own table — it vouches for a column it retired or an enum it re-listed, never a person's format — and the ledger's patches go: HOLDINGS and a bucket's FUND and ACCOUNT are real kinds, the inert plan columns and an Emergency goal's months are gone
question: The reconciler refuses to drop or re-constrain a column holding data (D-216), so the ledger carried patches (HOLDINGS stored as CASH + holds_things, FUND/ACCOUNT buckets stored as FREE, inert split_plan columns, an Emergency goal's months). How does a pack change its own table?
answer: adoptFormat/planReconcile take `vouched` (column names). For a format with an owner pack only: a vouched column the declaration dropped is dropped with its data; a vouched enum whose list changed is rebuilt as REBUILD_TABLE (new table, every row copied, renamed back, indexes and check triggers restored) provided every value the rows hold is on the new list (checked via ObservedColumn.values, refused by name otherwise). The ledger names them in REBUILT_COLUMNS (RETIRED or RELISTED) in pack.ts, replacing U08's RETIRED_COLUMNS. Retired: account.holds_things (HOLDINGS a real kind), split_bucket FIXED_EXPENSES (FUND/ACCOUNT real kinds, link required), split_plan fixed_expense_mode/fixed_in_split/applied_to_period with convertLegacyRoles/moveAppliedMonths, category.monthly_target, saving_goal emergency_months/emergency_basis with emergencyFund and the derived target (an Emergency goal is ordinary, offered on the form), fixed_expense.source DETECTED_PENDING. No conversion of old values.
state: amended

### D-387
date: 2026-10-05
milestone: M36
scope: ledger
title: Fewer places to go: one Readers list beside Read files, which reads fund reports too; Rules beside Categories; the whole cushion on Plan; Plan's header one month control; the deposit check a section of Funds; the waiting list opens the thing; Pays into makes what it needs
question: Where do the ledger's readers, Rules, the cushion's settings, the deposit check and Plan's controls live, and how does Read files take a fund report?
answer: #/read/readers (Readers.tsx: StatementReaders + DocumentReaders) is the one ledger Readers list, beside Read files; #/transactions|paychecks|wealth/readers and #/settings/mappings|formats redirect there; a declared format's readers stay on #/formats/<name>/read (engine's). Read files shows a PDF/txt as 'Payslip or fund report': A payslip -> Paychecks, 'A report of…' -> /wealth/funds/<id> with state.files, read once by ReportIntake(files). Rules: #/categories/rules (tab of Categories); #/settings/rules redirects. The cushion is set only on Plan (CushionLine via CushionPanel: months, buckets, 'It lives in' account ticks); Net worth's tick column and cushion line are removed; an unchecked cushion names each counted account without a statement with 'Leave it out'. Plan header = name, menu (open another plan, draw another beside, Bar/Ring, copy, default, rename, delete) and the month pager; 'Net pay is' behind the Net pay figure's Change (open while there is no figure). #/wealth/deposits renders Funds with the deposit-check section open. Waiting list: a fund with no balance opens that fund; a found payment's Edit opens its debt. Deduction types' Pays into is SelectOrNew: fund/goal via NewByName (fund type from the line), a debt via NewDebt with what was borrowed. PLACE_KIND_LABEL.INVESTMENT = 'Account with holdings'.
