### D-394
date: 2026-10-06
milestone: M34
scope: engine
title: A yes covers the dry run it answered and nothing after it: a batch of the same shape that follows gets its own dry run and its own yes, and fewer stops come from a bigger batch shown once
question: When a conversation writes rows in batches of the same shape, does one approved dry run cover the batches that follow?
answer: No. Every write keeps its own dry run and its own yes; both instruction blocks say so beside the dry-run rule. A person who wants fewer stops is shown one bigger batch (writes take up to 200 rows), never a commit that was not shown. The code already worked this way — every write is stateless, a dry run until commit: true on that call — so nothing changed in it. The safer default, chosen for the maintainer, who may revisit it (a plan covering a stated number of batches would need state the plugin does not keep).
