### D-395
date: 2026-10-06
milestone: M34
scope: engine
title: Many files read in one call, each onto its format, in the order their links need: the plan is the write rehearsed in a transaction that is rolled back, written whole or not at all, a line naming a parent that is not there refused by file and line; declare_format takes several formats the same way
question: How are several linked files read in one call, so a line can link to a row another file of the same call writes, with one plan before anything is written?
answer: read_onto_format takes files: [{file, format, ...mapping}]; the Read files screen puts each file onto the format whose reader fits or the one picked beside it. Both use planBatch/writeBatch (src/data/intake/batchReading.ts): files ordered so a file comes after the files whose formats it links to; the plan is each file's planReading plus recordIntake run inside rehearse() (database.ts), a transaction always rolled back, lifting a dry run's query_only for that span. Any file that may not be written (planWrites false) refuses the whole batch, named; a line that does not read (a parent not there) is refused by file and line and the rest written. declare_format takes formats: [...] judged against the document plus the set, declared in link order, all or none. Rejected: a stand-in for rows that will exist. Batch files are ReadTables with name and hash, so U3 and U7 build on it.
