title: What is wrong is said without being asked: every read accounts for each line of the file and reports what the engine can see mechanically in the formats it wrote — a link empty where most rows fill it, rows the same in every column, identities failed or unchecked; format_problems and a band on the format's page say it on demand; nothing is guessed that needs a declared rule
question: How does the engine say what is wrong without being asked, and account for every line a read takes in?
answer: lineTally (src/domain/format/audit.ts) splits a file's lines into heading, header-row lines, read, refused and empty, summing to the file; every read prints it (single file and files, dry run and commit) and the Read files screen shows it per file. auditRows/auditFormat (formatAuditRepository.ts) report: a link or links column filled on more than half the rows and empty on some (self-links skipped), rows identical in every stored column, identities failed or unchecked through the join. After a read it covers every format written, rehearsed for the dry run. On demand: the format_problems tool and the 'What looks wrong' band on #/formats/<name>; screens name failures and leave unchecked as a count. Rules nobody declared (a Done project with Not started tasks) are not guessed - an open question.
