### D-398
date: 2026-10-06
milestone: M34
scope: engine
title: Several of a list in one column — `enums`, its members rows of a side table whose CHECK names the list, written as a list, matched on one member, and split from a spreadsheet cell only by a separator the reading states
question: How does a column hold several members of a declared list (tags, allergens) without falling back to comma-separated text?
answer: A sixteenth type, `enums` (language 22, schema 59). No column in the format's table: each member is a row of fmt_<format>__<column> (row_id, member, position; PK row_id+member) whose CHECK names the list. Written as a list (one alone is a list of one), case-insensitive, stored as the list spells it; a member off the list is refused by name, a repeat refused; never required, unique or in a unit. match is membership (null = holds none); search reads the members; a text document writes a JSON list. read_onto_format splits a cell only by `separators: {key: ","}` (screen: Split by under the mapped column), kept in format_intake_column.separator; no separator = one member. A list changed over held members is refused like an enum's; empty is rebuilt. Sheet and entry view edit it as chips. isListType = links|enums, isChoiceType = enum|enums, memberColumnOf gives `member` for enums and `member_id` for links.
