### D-400
date: 2026-10-06
milestone: M34
scope: engine
title: A folder of Markdown notes is a table — a note a row (`title`, `file`, each frontmatter key, `body`), a link read from `[[name]]` or `[text](file.md)` as the title of the note it names; a link column is guessed when a header names it; and the Read screen reads a file no reader fits by the guess, shown in place
question: How does a folder of Markdown notes (a vault, a wiki, an export) read onto a format without a reader per product, and how do its links fill?
answer: src/domain/format/notes.ts turns notes into a ReadTable: a row per note, header title (frontmatter title, else opening # heading, else file stem), file, every frontmatter key in first-use order, body. YAML subset: scalars, [a, b] and - a lists, | > blocks, comments; nested maps dropped; all text. A list is joined by ';' and ReadTable.separators marks it, so a guess onto enums/links splits it. A value wholly [[name]] (|alias, #heading ignored) or [text](path.md) becomes the title of the note it names, found by stem (exact, then case-insensitive) or title across every note in the call/screen; else keeps the name; then D-261 exact unique name or the line is refused. links columns now read from files (split, each member resolved). guessReading(declaration, table, formats) guesses a link column when a header names it exactly and its target's naming column is unique (amends D-261's never-guessed); the label column also answers to name/title. read_onto_format: file may be a .md or a folder (direct .md files; others and subfolders named as not read); refused notes named by file (ReadTable.rowNames, rowLabel). Screen: .md picked, folder chosen (webkitdirectory) or dropped are grouped per folder (src/ui/formats/noteFiles.ts), links resolved across all; a file no reader fits is read by the guess shown in place (GuessLine) and kept as its reader on Write; Make a reader is gone (Change); a file whose name names a format goes onto it (formatNamedBy); link keys selectable in the grid. Hash: notesDigestText on both halves.
