question: A row had two views, each with half of it: the entry (edit, Save, no links) and the page (links in and out, read only, raw Markdown). What is the one view, and how does it write?
answer: One view at entry/:id for every way in; page/:id redirects; 'Its page', 'Edit' and the uuid in the bar are gone. entryLayout (view.ts) puts every column in one part: title (first text drawn as a line, D-296), header line (enum, enums, boolean, date, month, time, instant, single link, and any column whose entry setting says `header`), figures grid (number types, worked-out columns, totals) with verdicts under it and failed checks underlining their figures, texts, and `links` columns on the right above 'what names this row' (entryLinks: every link naming the format, a section each, one hop). A long text (a line break or >120 chars in any row on the sheet's page) defaults to markdown. A field writes when left and a pick when picked: coerceRow, then updateRow with only the changed columns; a refusal stays under the field, Esc reverts; a new entry is a draft until Add, which opens the entry. Show-as glyph on each field (today's inputs until M35 U3); Arrange keeps only order; no undo (the document has none). The page's body/line are the entry's markdown/header (views.md and memory.emd moved; the page kind is still read, drawn by nothing).
