question: How is each column type shown on the entry, how is it edited, and what becomes of M26 U6's inputs?
answer: waysFor (src/domain/format/view.ts) gives each type the approved mockup's set, the default first and the sheet's look: text Line/Markdown/Mono; integer, real, decimal Figure/Bar/Slider (both bounds); percent Figure/Bar/Ring/Slider; money Figure/Large figure; quantity As written/In one unit/Bar; date Date/Relative/Both; month Month/Relative; instant Date and time/Relative; time Clock; enum Chip/Menu/Buttons/Steps; enums Chips; boolean Tick/Yes or No/Buttons; link Name/Card; links Chips/List/Cards. Editing follows from the way (bar, ring, one unit and relative open their field when pressed; chip and Yes or No open the members; buttons, steps, tick pressed; link name opens, pencil changes). Kept in format_view_column view entry, written by setEntryInput alone; field and search are retired words read as no choice; an unoffered word draws as the default. Worked-out columns take their result type's ways (percent when every named column is a percent), never edited, and a check over percents alone prints percents. A bar is measured against the declared maximum or the page's largest; one unit is the declared unit or the one most rows use. A text defaults to Markdown on a line break, 120+ characters, or inline markdown (bold, link, heading/list/quote start) — code spans and single * or _ do not count, so a title quoting a name stays the title. A choice never reaches the sheet's cells or a board's cards.
