question: Can a conversation set how a format is shown — an entry column's Show as and place, the header line, a board's lanes, a sheet's widths — when the screens' reason for refusing was 'a conversation draws no page'?
answer: Yes. One engine tool, `arrange_views` (src/plugin/tools/views.ts), takes a list of {format, view: entry|board|sheet, column, show_as, header, order, width}, dry-runs until commit, applies whole or not at all, and writes through the screens' own functions (setEntryInput, setEntryOrder, setBoardLanes, setColumnWidth) plus the new setEntryHeader. Unknown format/column, a way the type does not offer, a lane by a non-enum, a worked-out column in the header are refused by name; a pack's format refuses entry settings, as on the screen. `formats` with a `format` prints each column's Show as, ways, place, header and width and the board's lanes. Settings stay engine view tables, never a fmt_ view format. Canvas places stay the screen's (D-291). The sheet now prints a worked-out percent figure as a percent.
