question: How does a document come to keep a pack other than the ledger — from a conversation and from the Packs screen — what does create_document default to without `packs`, what happens to formats the document already holds of a pack, and may a document with rows keep one?
answer: One write, keepPack in src/data/packs/packs.ts (planKeep is its dry run), generic over PACKS: each pack entry has `declarations` and `install`. The Packs screen (#/settings/packs) shows Keep this pack here on every pack card; keep_packs (dry-run until commit, list of pack ids) and create_document's `packs` call the same function. Omitted `packs`: the ledger on the full server, none engine-only (engineOnly reaches tools through ToolContext). A held format that is the pack's (shared columns same type/target/unit, enum values a superset) is completed with the optional columns it lacks; anything else is a clash, refused whole naming the column (src/data/packs/fit.ts). A pack already kept is a no-op that says so. A document with rows may keep a pack: keeping only adds.
