question: How does a note's body fill a links column, and what happens to a body link that names no row?
answer: notesTable adds a `body links` column (only when a note links): every [[name]], ![[note#section]] (links to the note) and [text](file.md) outside code, resolved to the linked note's title as frontmatter links are, once each, a self-link dropped; list-separated, and marked ReadTable.prose. guessReading never matches it by header words; it maps it onto the one `links` column whose target is where the links resolve (formatsNamed: rows the document holds by id or unique name, or notes another folder of the same read writes) — exactly one, else no guess. resolveReadLinks leaves a prose member that names no row out of the row and keeps it in ReadRow.unlinked; the tool report and the Read screen name each by note and the note is read. Only a required links column emptied by that refuses the line. Frontmatter links still refuse their line (D-261). Links between notes of one folder are not filled (no ids before write) and are named with that reason.
