title: A new document is called `untitled-YYYY-MM.emd`, and New asks first: the title bar has a New beside Save while a document is open, and every New (it, `Ctrl+N`, the palette, the shell's File menu) goes through `requestNew`, which holds the request in a notice — Save, then new · Discard mine, new · Stay here — when there is unsaved work
question: What is a new document called when first saved, how is New reached while a document is open, and what happens to unsaved work when it is pressed?
answer: suggestedFileName (src/data/storage/adapter.ts, the one place) returns untitled-YYYY-MM.emd; no pack word, the month kept so an overwrite is recoverable. DocumentBar shows a secondary New between Save (the one primary) and Open…. Every New — the button, Ctrl+N via the shell menu, the palette's doc:new — calls documentStore.requestNew: with nothing unsaved it runs createNew at once; with unsaved work it sets pendingNew and Notices shows 'X has unsaved changes' with Save, then new · Discard mine, new · Stay here, ranked with the document waiting to open. Opening another document clears pendingNew. Before this, createNew discarded unsaved work from every entry point (the brief assumed Ctrl+N asked; it did not). The empty window's New / New ledger still call createNew. Not changed: Open… through the picker still replaces unsaved work without asking.
