question: Where do a tour's rows live, how does the tour start without seconds of nothing, how does the frame lay out at any width, and how is every tour checked?
answer: tours.emd beside the app page: fixtures/synthetic/demo/tour.format.md and tour_step.format.md (declarations and rows) joined by make-demo-document.mjs as a text document under this build's schema and read back through the plugin; the frame reads it with the engine (rows.ts) so the title and first caption show at once; never in the played document (it would list Tour step in the visitor's rail). The first play skips the second open; reading time counts from when a caption appeared. layout.ts: app laid out at least 960 wide (+260 while the paper shows), scaled to fit, fills the height under the strip; movie below 690. Caption wraps, cell reserves the tallest tour caption. npm run check:tours = build:demo + scripts/check-tours.mjs (loopback server + offscreen Electron at 1280x800 and 375x440, ?check), fails naming the first missing anchor or highlight; ~5 s on a built demo.
