question: How does the demo frame pace a caption, how wide does it lay the app out, and what does it show on a phone?
answer: PACE.lead 400 ms after a caption the ring sets off; the caption's reading (counted from when it came up, travel included) is held before the scene's first click or keystroke, capped at PACE.read 3.5 s; a row that outlines acts first. LAYOUT_LEAST is 1120 = the expanded 200 px sidebar + the receipt's 904 px sheet + a 10 px scrollbar (960 assumed a 56 px rail and scrolled the sheet sideways). check-tours fails any row at which a box of the app scrolls sideways. Below MOVIE_BELOW 690 the app is laid out 1120x720 and the frame draws a window of it at CROP_SCALE 0.75 (cropAt), on the highlight else the ring's anchor, a sheet row by its text's extent, panning at the ring's pace, jumping under reduced motion; the paper is a corner card the window keeps clear of. The tour has five captions and ends on the answer. Amends D-414's widths and pacing.
