### D-416
date: 2026-10-07
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The tour's ring travels on the app — worked out in the app's own pixels each frame and mapped through the iframe as drawn — never by a CSS transition on its place; and a crop starts at 0.75x until the visitor picks a speed
question: Why did the tour's ring miss its target when the app was scaled or cropped, and what does a phone's crop play at?
answer: The placement math was right (0 px at rest); the ring's travel was a CSS transition on its place, restarted every frame the app moved under it (a crop's pan, the scale easing as the paper comes in), so it trailed by up to a travel and pressed 28-271 px off in the phone column. The ring now travels on the app: place.ts travelled() interpolates from where it was to its anchor in app pixels on the frame's ease (cubic-bezier 0.65,0,0.35,1) over travelAt(speed), and onViewport() maps it through the iframe as drawn each frame; .tour-ring has no transition on its place (a test holds it). Measured after: 0-1 px at every press, wide and phone. A crop (below 690) starts at MOVIE_SPEED 0.75x via startingSpeed(); a speed the visitor picked on the slider wins and is remembered; until then the default follows the frame across the crop's width.
