title: The demo is embedded by a contract of three things: `?tour=` picks the tour and `?autoplay=1` plays it, without which the frame holds the tour's first frame — the poster — under one *Watch the tour* control; the frame tells its parent, as `source: 'emerald-demo'` messages, which step is up, a take-over and a Reset, and nothing else; and `check-tours` refuses and fails any request outside the folder. Pages publishes `dist-demo/` from a public repository only, and the first deploy is the maintainer's
question: How does a page embed the demo — what it asks for in the URL, what the frame tells it, and how is 'nothing leaves the page' kept true — and how does it get deployed before the public repository exists?
answer: main.tsx: ?tour=<name> (first if absent/unknown), ?autoplay=1 (or bare, or true) plays at once; without it TourPlayer.wait() holds mode 'ready' (first caption, document open) with a 'Watch the tour' accent button over the app; Watch, a click on the app, Reset or a dot starts it. embed.ts: messageBetween posts {source:'emerald-demo', event:'step'|'took-over'|'reset', step (1-based, as the strip), of} to window.parent only, targetOrigin '*' (no-referrer means the origin is unknowable; the payload is two counts and a word); step only while watching, never in fast-forward; took-over not on a lost tour; reset on the Reset button with step 1. Nothing inbound. check-tours-window.cjs refuses and fails any request not to the served origin or data:/blob:. Proved at 127.0.0.1:4180 (demo-static) embedded by docs/mockups/m33-u4/embed.html at localhost:4182 (demo-embed) with referrerpolicy=no-referrer allow='': autoplay, messages, waiting frame, partitioned speed storage. Poster: npm run demo:poster (scripts/make-demo-poster.cjs, offscreen Electron, light, 1600x1000, control hidden) -> fixtures/synthetic/demo/poster.png. .github/workflows/demo.yml: npm ci (no Electron binary) + build:demo + Pages actions, job gated on a public repository, so the private repo never deploys; the first deploy is the maintainer's (Settings > Pages > Source: GitHub Actions in the new public repo).
