question: How does Emerald animate rows, layout, verdicts and navigation app-wide, and how is the U1 mockup switched?
answer: One module src/ui/motion/: motion.ts (switch, 180 ms / 150 ms fade / one easing --ease-out, off under reduced motion), flip.ts + Flip.tsx (FLIP measured around React's commit with getSnapshotBeforeUpdate, only pieces in view, removed pieces leave an inert ghost, >3 entering/leaving or a new sort snaps), Reveal.tsx (panel grows its room, closes by fading out; dialog fades out), useMark.ts (verdict change marked once via useChanges). Not view transitions: overlay takes clicks, every change must be wrapped where made, one snapshot per row. Keys are row name + occurrence, never id (D-247). Mockup is import.meta.env.DEV only, switched by ?motion=on or the palette; with it on no figure counts. Unapproved until the maintainer looks; U2/U3 port it.
