question: How do navigating and closing move (M39 motion 4), app-wide, without blocking input or confusing the tour runner, and what happens to the dev-only mockup switch?
answer: A route change is a 150 ms opacity-only fade (fc-view-enter itself; no rise, no crossfade — the old screen goes at once), so every box is final from the first frame. The routed view is keyed by screenOf(pathname): a ListDetail detail address keys to its list, so opening/closing the pane never remounts the screen; the pane grows its width opening and fades out of its room closing, and the detail inside is keyed by its address. Closing is src/ui/motion/closing.ts, one MutationObserver on the page: an element with fc-pop-enter or data-motion-close that React removes leaves an inert, unnamed copy that fades (positioned: fade only; in flow: its room closes, LAYOUT_MOTION). Not a close: replaced in the same commit, a Reveal's own release, anything removed inside something larger. Reveal keeps only grow. The switch, pill, palette entry and slow-down box are removed (browser devtools slow animations). Ported from U1 unapproved.
