question: How does an element that appears get its motion, and how is motion kept off a keystroke?
answer: An entrance is CSS on the element already there: what opens (dialog, popover, menu, card, panel, notice, inline form) carries fc-pop-enter, which closing.ts also fades out; what replaces another at one place (a flow's step, a view swap) carries fc-view-enter and a React key so it remounts. No JS, no wrapper component, no per-screen timing. In-place editors, single lines and pointer-following things do not move. Motion keys never change while text is typed: a sheet drawn from a draft keys columns by the draft key (RowSheet columnKeys, the NEW mark's key). check:tours types every field a key at a time and fails on layout motion (not a leave) after the first key; layoutSettled also waits for fc-pop-in. The audit list is docs/mockups/m39-u1/motion.md, F1.
