answer: Timesheet day: date, start, end (time), rate (money), paycheck (link found by date in period, D-350); hours = end - start and earned = hours * rate computed. The paycheck is only added to: a total worked (sum of earned over its days) and the claim hours_paid: gross = worked; its columns are unchanged (D-269 lets additions through). The claim must sit on the paycheck's side: a total folds rows naming a row, and a claim cannot hop to a total. A paycheck with no days fails (a sum of nothing is zero) — not fixed. Because the paycheck's sheet is 2,620 px against 920 (sideways scroll refused, M33 F1), a tour write also takes {"declare": {...}} in declare_format/extend_format's words plus sheet widths, judged by declarationRejection and declarationChangeRefusal and written by adoptFormat (src/demo/tour/declare.ts). An unchecked money claim now prints its figures in the currency of a figure it names.
