### D-431
date: 2026-10-08
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: A format's sheet is drawn in the conversation as an MCP App: `format_sheet` names one `ui://` page the server serves from memory, the page is the app's own `FormatRows` over the store's `openBytes`, the file rides in the result's `_meta`, and the frame runs sql.js's asm.js build because a frame's CSP refuses wasm
question: How does a format's sheet get drawn inside a conversation without a second data path, and does sql.js run in an MCP App's sandboxed frame?
answer: `format_sheet` (a read; its text is format_rows' word for word) carries `_meta.ui.resourceUri: ui://emerald/sheet.html`; the server serves that one resource as text/html;profile=mcp-app from a string compiled into server.mjs. The page (src/frame/main.tsx, built by `vite build --mode frame` into .frame/frame.html, script and style inline, fonts dropped) speaks the MCP Apps postMessage protocol by hand (src/frame/host.ts), takes the file's base64 bytes from the result's `_meta['emerald/sheet']`, opens them with documentStore.openBytes and renders the app's FormatRows in a MemoryRouter. The spec's default frame CSP has no 'wasm-unsafe-eval' and a page cannot declare one, so wasm is refused; the frame build aliases sql.js to its asm.js build (same package and SQLite), measured drawing docs/memory.emd's milestone sheet in ~1.7 s under the strict CSP. Bytes are carried only for a declared format, whether or not the client advertises io.modelcontextprotocol/ui. No ext-apps dependency.
state: amended

### D-432
date: 2026-10-08
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: The frame draws every view of a format at the app's own paths, read-only, with a test that fails on a control leading nowhere; `start_here` is a page; the copy goes only to a client that advertises MCP Apps
question: How does the MCP App frame draw more than the sheet without a control leading nowhere, and who is handed the document copy?
answer: src/frame/routes.tsx routes FormatRows, FormatRoadmap, FormatReady and FormatPage at App.tsx's own paths (sheet, entry, board, roadmap, ready); an undrawn path is a sentence, never a snap back; NOT_IN_FRAME names what is not drawn (only /read) and why. The ReadOnly context (src/ui/formats/readOnly.ts) locks every format page as a pack's is locked: no add, edit, remove, rule set, claim or column change; views, search, sort, opening rows, links, lanes and widths still work on the copy. src/frame/routes.test.ts fails on an App.tsx format route neither drawn nor in NOT_IN_FRAME, and renders every view of memory.emd and a synthetic ledger read-only, failing on links to undrawn paths or writing controls. start_here names the same page and opens on 'start': the roadmaps the ready rows fold under, cut to the live rows, then the ready lists (startPicture). format_sheet takes view, refused when the format lacks it. The copy rides in _meta only when the client advertises io.modelcontextprotocol/ui (ToolContext.drawsApps), amending D-431; whether a real host keeps it from the model is unmeasured. Fonts: system stack in src/frame/frame.css (CSP has no font-src). ui/notifications/tool-cancelled is said.
