### D-433
date: 2026-10-08
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: The server draws the engine's views and nothing else draws them: the frame ships inside `server.mjs`, no pack carries UI, nothing leaves the frame, and it is read-only; a model draws when a person asks to see and reads rows with `format_rows`
question: What shape does M41 leave: where the conversation views ship, who decides what they draw, what may leave the frame, can it edit, and when should a model draw rather than read?
answer: The frame page is compiled into dist-plugin/server.mjs as a string and served as its one ui:// resource; no separate download, and M42's package carries it by carrying the server. What it draws is chosen by the document's own views (sheet, board, roadmap, ready, start_here's picture), never by anything a pack wrote: no pack carries UI. No request leaves the frame: one self-contained file under the spec's default CSP (connect-src 'none'), the document a copy in the result's _meta, sent only to a client advertising io.modelcontextprotocol/ui. Read-only: M41 U3 (edits) moved to Later 2026-10-08. Both instruction blocks (the shared formats half) say: format_sheet and start_here when a person asks to SEE something; format_rows for rows a model filters, counts or reasons over (~450 chars of instructions; the 42.5k tool-list budget unchanged). Hosts, read 2026-10-08 from MCP's extension page and community client matrix: Claude web, desktop and Code tab, ChatGPT, VS Code with GitHub Copilot, Goose and others — reported, not seen here; Claude Desktop on Windows shows local servers' views as text only (anthropics/claude-ai-mcp#1069) and web chat draws only from remote connectors; every other host gets the text. Proved on a clean copy of dist-plugin/ in a scratch folder beside only the SDK, sql.js and xlsx and their dependencies: format_sheet answered, the page served with no external src/href, the stand-in drew start_here from it (frame:try --server=<path>, new). The real-host check is owed. Runs as node dist-plugin/server.mjs; one-click install and whether Node is needed belong to M42.
