answer: As `rule` rows: extend_format added `ui` to rule.scope (how a screen looks, moves and speaks; `app` stays how the renderer behaves) and style now covers how a screen is drawn. A UI rule needs every rule column — several decisions, a test in enforced_by — which a ui_rule with one decided_by would lose. 69 new rows plus Accent is for acting and Hebrew needs bidi isolation moved from app: 71 with scope ui, none newly always. Query: format_rows rule match:{scope:ui, state:live}. The values (colours, ramp, spacing, radii, shadow, durations) stay only in src/ui/theme/tokens.css and the rows name tokens, never values — the note's copies had drifted (hairline, the pre-M39 durations, an ink focus ring). docs/11 is a 61-line pointer note kept because many notes and comments link to it; a code comment citing docs/11 for a rule means the ui rows.
