question: How are multi-word filter members written, how is a batch's uniqueness judged, and how is a link name resolved when the target's name repeats across parents?
answer: `status is one of Planned, In progress` (comma-split) and `status is "In progress"` (quoted when alone; unquoted multi-word is refused saying so). A batch is judged against its own end state and update_format_rows retries index-refused edits after the others. A rebuild's taken-down-and-put-back check steps are `kept` and never printed. A target declaring `one row per <link>, <name>` resolves a name only among the rows of the parent the writing row links to (fixed or a cell); a name still held twice is refused naming the rows.
