question: How does a conversation give a document a start-here question, a ready list or a roadmap, without a pack's views.md?
answer: `arrange_views` with `view: roadmap | ready | start`, a `column` and a `setting` — the views.md word (`order`, `under`, `line`; `waits`, `ready <members> done <members>`; `is <member>`, `latest <n>`), null clears. Each is judged as roadmapOf/readyOf/startOf read it and refused by name if the view would skip it; a sole word (order, waits, ready …, latest) moves off other columns; the dry run says what start_here and the roadmap will answer. The roadmap screen's *In the order of* menu writes the same `setRoadmapOrder`; ready/start/folds have no screen yet (a screen trail in docs/parity.md). A setting is at most 32 characters (052's CHECK), refused naming the bound. Engine-only definition budget 50.5k.
