### D-471
date: 2026-10-14
milestone: M49
scope: engine
title: A date moves by whole days and weeks — `last_reviewed + 7 days` — as the whole of a computed column (a computed date, `date()` in the view) or one side of a claim, and either end of `end - start`; never by months; and a computed column sorts, and a computed date filters, on the screen and in `format_rows` alike
question: How does a computed column or a claim add days or weeks to a date, and how does a computed date sort and filter?
answer: The grammar reads `<whole number> day|days|week|weeks` straight after a number as a DAYS token (span.ts DAY_WORDS); `1.5 days` and `+ 1 month/year` are refused in words. A date column moved by DAYS (shiftedPoint) may be the whole of a computed column — DerivedType DATE, SQL `date(t.col, '+N days')`, TS dateOfOrdinal — one side of a claim against another point (equationPointProblem; pointVerdict carries `points` so sentences print dates; tolerance in days, RELATIVE refused), or either end of a span (spanPair.days). Elsewhere it is a lone point. Only dates move; times and instants are refused. DAYS alone is a figure in `day`. RowQuery.order and match may name a computed column via derivedValueSql (the view's SQL for the row); match only for a computed DATE; filterQuery always passes formats. The sheet's computed headers sort; format_rows' order takes computed names. Engine-only budget stays under 50.5k.
state: live

### D-472
date: 2026-10-14
milestone: M49
scope: engine
title: Today belongs in questions, never in claims: a filter (`due is within 14 days`, `before today`, `after today`, `today`), a sort and a computed column shown on read (`days_left = due - today`) may read the clock; an identity, a declared total, a rule set and the stored view may not, and are refused saying why
question: Where may `today` be read — which parts of a format may depend on the day they are asked on?
answer: Questions only: a filter's window (`due is within 14 days` = today through +14 both ends; `before today`, `after today`, `today`) in parseFilter, `match` on a typed or computed date (format_rows, format_sheet, the screen's address via one filterQuery) and a rollup's where; a sort; a computed column like `days_left = due - today`, worked out by the reader's own SELECT and never in the stored fmt_<name>__derived view. An identity, a declared total (or one folding a today column), a rule set's where are refused with CLOCK_REASON. The engine reads no clock: the day comes as YYYY-MM-DD from ui/today.ts or plugin/today.ts (S-064 twins); a reader told no day refuses. `today` is reserved as a column name. Engine-only budget stays under 50.5k.
state: live

