question: What makes the fixed-expense detector offer a merchant as a bill, and which date gives its day of the month?
answer: The month is the charge date's (D-006) but the day is the purchase's (ExpenseObservation.transactionDate), since a card charges every line on one day. Every candidate must keep one signal (figure within the 10% band, or day spread <= 3); a candidate seen in only two months needs the identical figure and a steady day. The demo keeps no not-bills marks.
