title: A unit's `paths` are one repository path per line beside its prose `files`, and `dispatch_plan` answers, for a list of unit refs, which can run at once, which share a path and go one after another, and which have no paths and are unknown
question: How does a manager know which ready units can run at once, when a unit's `files` is prose nothing can compare?
answer: `unit` gains `paths`, a text column of one repository path per line (a folder ends in `/`); `files` keeps the prose, and what every unit appends to (the decision log, docs/memory.emd) is left out. `dispatch_plan` (read-only) takes up to 50 unit refs, or none for every ready unit, and answers: At once (no path shared with another listed nor with a unit in progress), One after another (groups joined by a shared path, a running unit first, with a table of each pair and what it shares), Unknown (no paths, never safe), Not ready and why; then each ready unit's paths, files, blocks, the decisions it links or its brief names, and its brief. Paths are shared when equal without case or when one is a folder holding the other. Every answer says overlap is only as good as the paths written at planning. Old rows are not converted. Rejected: a `texts` engine type (an engine type with a screen editor for one column), links to a `path` format (dearer planning), a start_here section (takes no argument), the name `dispatch_units` (reads are nouns, D-096).
