answer: `rows … --once-per-session` reads session_id from the hook's stdin and keeps, in `<document>.told` beside the lock (never in the document), marks of the rows printed in full by what they say (ids renew on text writes). An unseen row prints in full, alone; when all are seen the hook says one count line once, then nothing until the rows change; no session id prints every row as before. The status line is `dist-plugin/status-line.mjs`, a separate small build pass that reads `<document>.status` (written by `server.mjs status`, stamped with size and mtime) and never opens the document; a stale cache prints anyway and is refreshed once, detached. start_here and the watch are unchanged.
