title: A hook's start_here text says first that it is text and nothing was drawn, and a request to see calls the drawing tool anyway
question: Asked to see what is ready, a session retyped the SessionStart hook's start_here text and never called a drawing tool, so D-489's first line never reached it. How does a session know the hook's text is not a drawing?
answer: The hook's start-here output opens with PRINTED_NOT_DRAWN (src/plugin/hooks/commands.ts): printed as text, nothing was drawn; asked to see, call start_here or show_format anyway, on a server the host runs itself if the session has one; never call a view drawn unless that answer says so; say so in words when nothing was. Both instruction blocks' When they ask to see paragraph says the same before 2,000 characters. Host-neutral; the Claude desktop app's case (call it on emerald-ledger, never the .mcp.json emerald) is one sentence in CLAUDE.md. D-489's evidence re-checked: the live log is %LOCALAPPDATA%/Claude/logs/claude.ai-web.log (the %APPDATA% one is a stale copy ending 2026-08-22); 1 of 30 emerald and 23 of 27 emerald-ledger drawing calls mounted a frame; it holds.
