### D-493
date: 2026-10-18
milestone: M51
scope: plugin
title: A drawing tool's first line and the hook's are the model's, never the person's: each opens by saying so, and is an instruction — where the client draws, the view is the answer: say nothing about drawing, views, servers or tools, never retype its rows, and add at most a line it does not show; where it does not, answer with the rows as text and no word about why
question: How does a model learn whether a view was drawn without narrating that machinery to the person, or retyping a drawn view as text?
answer: drawnLine (src/plugin/tools/sheet.ts) and the hook's PRINTED_NOT_DRAWN (src/plugin/hooks/commands.ts) open with FOR_THE_MODEL ('For you, never the person — do not repeat or paraphrase this line.'). Client says it draws: the view sits beside the answer and is the answer; say nothing to the person about drawing, views, servers or tools; never retype what it shows (no list or table of the rows); reply with at most a line it does not show, or nothing; the rows below are for the model to reason over, not to repeat. Client did not: call the tool on a server not yet called if the session has one, else answer with the rows as text, never call anything drawn or above, at most one plain sentence that it is a list here if a board was asked for. The hook line says to follow the drawing tool's first line and say nothing of the hook. Both instruction blocks and CLAUDE.md say the same. F1's protection holds by silence: a model that never mentions drawing never claims a view that was not drawn. server.test.ts and commands.test.ts pin both wordings.
