### D-494
date: 2026-10-18
milestone: M42
scope: plugin
title: What only Claude reads lives in `hosts/claude/` — the hooks and the status line, the skills a stranger gets, and the plugin's manifest — built beside the server as `hooks.mjs` and `status-line.mjs`; nothing in `src/` or `electron/` imports from `hosts/`, and a host reaches the server only through `src/plugin/host.ts`
question: Where does what only Claude reads live, so the MCP server every client runs carries none of it?
answer: hosts/claude/hooks/ holds what src/plugin/hooks/ held, the status line's entry and a new main.ts: `vite build --mode claude-hooks` writes dist-plugin/hooks.mjs and `--mode claude-status-line` status-line.mjs, beside server.mjs, which answers MCP and `watch` and nothing else; hooks.json names ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks.mjs. hosts/claude/skills/ holds the skills a stranger gets (declare-a-format now), each the same file as this repo's .claude/skills/ copy (skills.test.ts); this repo's own skills stay out. src/plugin/host.ts is what the server exports for a host. src/plugin/hostBoundary.test.ts: nothing in src/ or electron/ imports from hosts/; a host imports from src/ only host.ts (a test may add src/testing/) and from electron/ only bridge.ts. The frame stays in the server (MCP Apps is an open extension). A second host is hosts/<name>/. This repo's .claude/ stays the configuration for developing Emerald. Rejected: hooks as a server.mjs subcommand built from hosts/ (the server would import the host); `plugin/` as the folder name (src/plugin is the server's); moving declare-a-format out of .claude/skills/.
