question: Do the plugin's hooks and status line run the published package through npx, or a cached copy with plain node?
answer: Through npx, by the maintainer's 'use npm for it' (2026-10-18). Hooks: `npx -y --prefer-offline -p emerald-mcp@<version> emerald-hooks start-here "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"` (SessionStart, timeout 60) and `… rows "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" inbox --match state=new --once-per-session` (UserPromptSubmit). Status line (the person's setting): `npx -y --prefer-offline -p emerald-mcp@<version> emerald-status-line`. emerald.mjs and the data-folder copy are removed. Every pin equals plugin.json's version (hosts/claude/plugin.test.ts). Cost, Windows, cache warm: inbox hook ~1.95 s per prompt, start-here ~2 s and the server ~2.2–2.6 s once a session, status line ~1.7 s (over its 200 ms). Amends D-498's launcher only: marketplace, server command, single version and no .mcpb stand.
