question: How is Emerald listed in the MCP Registry, and how is a version cut now that the registry needs mcpName in the published package?
answer: server.json at the root names io.github.kfireliyahu/emerald and points at emerald-mcp on npm; npm-package.mjs stamps its name as mcpName. A version is cut in package.json, server.json and PLUGIN_VERSION (registry.test.ts) and pushed; the maintainer publishes npm; node scripts/pin-plugin.mjs moves the plugin's pins once npm has it (pins may trail, never lead). .github/workflows/registry.yml (push on server.json or plugin.json, daily, dispatch) publishes with mcp-publisher 1.8.1 and GitHub OIDC only when npm has a version the registry lacks. No tag; the desktop release does not move (page RELEASE stays 0.1.0). 0.1.1 is the first listable version.
