body: "M52 F2 is built on claude/m52-f2-quieter-writes-76670d at f1edbee (worktree F:/projects/emerald/.claude/worktrees/m52-f2-quieter-writes-76670d). No decision, no migration. It also answers inbox 036f0773 (the pack's notes describe Emerald's own repo). Land it with land_units inbox:[this id].\n\n```json\n{\"unit\": \"M52 F2\", \"files\": \"src/plugin/write.ts\\nsrc/plugin/backup.ts\\nsrc/plugin/tools/formats.test.ts\\nsrc/plugin/instructions.ts\\ndocs/plugin.md\\nhosts/claude/skills/declare-a-format/SKILL.md\\n.claude/skills/declare-a-format/SKILL.md\\nhosts/claude/skills/closing-pass/SKILL.md\\nhosts/claude/skills/review-phase/SKILL.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/decision.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/open_question.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/milestone.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/review_entry.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/unit.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/formats/inbox.format.md\\nsrc/data/packs/development/past.ts\\nsrc/data/packs/development/pack.test.ts\\ndocs/memory.emd\", \"commit\": \"f1edbee\", \"branch\": \"claude/m52-f2-quieter-writes-76670d\", \"decisions\": [], \"review_entries\": [{\"do\": \"create_document with packs [development] at a new path, then formats decision and formats open_question\", \"should\": \"Both read sensibly to someone outside Emerald: neutral examples (D-12, Q3, M2), no docs/ path, no D-/H-/M-number of this repo, and decision's law says a decision others rely on is superseded, not changed in place, while a same-day wording fix is fine\", \"breaks\": \"A document that already keeps the pack (another project's document) gets the new format notes from keep_packs but keeps the old column notes: keep_packs never brings a column's note\"}], \"report\": \"M52 F2 built at f1edbee. (a) The backup notice prints on a document's first write in a server's run and is silent after (write.ts, a set of resolved paths); the copy is still taken every time; named copies and keep_copy still print; a refused write now names the folder of earlier copies. Test: three writes, one notice, three copies. (b) Hand edits to a text .emd are checked on the next call: a bad date, enum member, unknown column, missing required value, repeated name or dangling link refuses the whole document (UNREADABLE) with the line and reason, until fixed; nothing is dropped. So the instructions (shared Formats section), docs/plugin.md and the skills declare-a-format, closing-pass and review-phase say: edit the text while ideas move, then one format_problems call checks it. (c) Both instruction blocks now say to collect rows and write them in one call. (d) The six declarations of the development pack are rewritten in general terms, column specs unchanged; decision's law corrected. pack.test.ts has a new test failing on this repo's paths or numbers; past.ts has the new fingerprints; docs/memory.emd follows the pack (pack.test says so), so its declaration prose was replaced in the text, frontmatter kept. No decision: no row stated the old law. Not done: hosts/claude/plugin.test.ts wants a new plugin version (skills changed), left for the 0.2.0 cut; ask-cold could not run (claude CLI not logged in). Found: keep_packs brings a format's notes but never a column's note, so documents already keeping the pack keep the old column prose.\"}\n```"
