body: "M53 U6 is built on worktree-agent-a55f1f9ab4b315ff9 at 5d39450; land it with D-516.\n\n```json\n{\"unit\":\"M53 U6\",\"files\":\"src/ui/charts/chart.ts, src/ui/charts/Chart.tsx, src/ui/charts/chart.test.ts, src/ui/charts/categoryPalette.ts, src/ui/formats/rollupChart.ts, src/ui/formats/rollupChart.test.ts, src/ui/formats/RollupView.tsx, src/ui/theme/tokens.css, docs/09-decision-log.md\",\"commit\":\"5d39450\",\"branch\":\"worktree-agent-a55f1f9ab4b315ff9\",\"decisions\":[{\"ref\":\"D-516\",\"title\":\"One general chart draws plain series as bars or a line, only what its axis can hold, read by a screen reader as a table; a rollup's chart is bars by month, one series per linked row, the eight largest drawn and the rest said, never summed\",\"question\":\"How does Emerald draw a chart that is not the ledger's, and what does a rollup's chart show?\",\"answer\":\"src/ui/charts/Chart.tsx takes plain series (chart.ts): labels, points that are Money, a plain figure, a word (unchecked) or nothing, and an axis {currency} or {unit}. Money becomes a number only in drawnValue; money in another currency or a plain figure on a money axis is not drawn. One series is ink, several take the category palette by key; the SVG is aria-hidden and an sr-only table reads every point. rollupChart.ts turns a rollup into bars by month (a line on a toggle), every month first to last, one series per linked row plus none, the axis the most common currency, at most 8 series; rows with no month, other currencies and series past the eighth are said under the chart, never folded into an other. Nothing in src/ui/charts/ imports the ledger (chart.test.ts).\"}],\"review_entries\":[],\"report\":\"M53 U6 built at 5d39450 on worktree-agent-a55f1f9ab4b315ff9. One general chart, src/ui/charts/Chart.tsx over plain data in chart.ts: labels, series of Money / plain figures / a said word / nothing, an axis in a currency or a unit; bars or a line, hand-rolled SVG in the theme tokens, light and dark, the picture aria-hidden and an sr-only table reading every point. RollupView draws its rollup above the table with a Bars/Line toggle, one series per linked row (rollupChart.ts); what the chart cannot hold is said under it. The frame draws it through FormatRows' View menu, unchanged (no new FrameView, so show_format cannot open on a rollup yet). categoryPalette.ts now declares the Category shape it reads instead of importing the ledger's type, so chart.test.ts checks the whole folder imports no ledger. tokens.css gains .fc-grow (bars grow once) and the chart's hover classes. Ledger charts not moved. Verified in the worktree's dev server on a synthetic expense/project document (bars 19 rects, line 4 paths, light and dark) and in the frame stand-in (try-frame) with the same counts. docs:check fails on this branch only for D-516's missing row, which this landing writes. check:tours skipped: no tour passes a rollup view.\"}\n```"
