### M29
title: formats are easier to make
goal: From a new-user run, 2026-10-03: a newcomer could not make a format do what was wanted — two views for create and edit, columns stuck in place, no percent, and no way to record hours and add them up. M29 makes one editor, lets columns move, adds percent and time of day, and lets dates and times be subtracted into durations inside an identity.
state: closed
position: 290

### M30
title: An account that holds things
goal: Money that leaves the bank for another account the person owns (a broker, a savings account, a deposit) is followed there: the two ends of a transfer are one pair, a row can turn cash into a holding, a goal is fed by its holding's rows, a dated reading says what a holding is worth, and what sits in the bank is split between the cushion and the goals saved there. Abstract on purpose: nothing in it is about securities (2026-10-04: based on it, but abstract). Answered 2026-10-04: a place LINKS to an account (not merged); NO app reader for broker PDFs (already tried before D-308: too expensive, not good enough) — a conversation reads them and writes rows; interest, bonuses and fee rebates on such an account are growth of its cash, not income, and its leftover cash belongs to no goal unless chosen; a goal's progress is what it is worth now (latest reading), with what went in beside it; the cushion is measured against the bank accounts the person picks, and the bank's balance can be split across the cushion and other goals saved in the bank. Evidence: real broker exports in the real-documents folder/investments (one-page PDFs: a holdings snapshot with cost basis and cash line, and a movements list with cash and quantity balance after each row; per security, buys sum exactly to the printed cost basis and quantity).
state: closed
position: 300

### M31
title: Fewer steps
goal: Every everyday task takes the fewest steps the app can manage: what it can infer it does, what a task needs it can make in place, every question waits in one list, and one thing has one name. Measured as click paths before and after (the driver's mapping, 2026-10-05: a goal for bank money 7 steps, first run ~14, monthly saving 5-7).
state: closed
position: 310

### M32
title: A pack anyone can make and share
goal: A person turns formats they made into a pack, hands it to someone as one file, and the other person adds it to their document and gets its formats, links, identities, views and readers with no code and no screen of its own. Done when the development pack round-trips through a file into a fresh document unchanged, and one pack that is not ours, made from a real use case, does the same. The line held throughout: a shared pack is data only; a screen it needs is a view kind the engine draws, never UI the pack carries; a reader it carries holds positions and labels, never a figure. Planned 2026-10-05 in a product session: the tool is the product and packs are how anyone finds it.
state: planned
position: 348

### M33
title: A showcase you can try
goal: A public page a stranger opens from a post and plays with, and a frame the maintainer's own site embeds: the real app on a synthetic document, walked by a drawn pointer through a workflow like a video, which the visitor stops with a toggle or a click and then drives (D-413). Four tours over one document, each a script of rows: a custom format declared, refused and linked; the ledger reading a statement, reconciling, categorising, a goal; the development pack's board with a claim and a refused state; a timesheet declared on top of the ledger and summed against the paycheck. The AI half stays a recording and the page ends with an email, 'what would you use it for?' and a count. Nothing recorded and nothing copied: the tours run the app's own components on the real engine, the document is built at build time by the engine's own tools, and one deployed build serves both sites through an iframe with parameters. Done when the custom tour is on a static host embedded in the maintainer's site, the page carries all four, and the maintainer has written the kill criterion before posting it. Planned 2026-10-05 as islands; re-planned 2026-10-07 as tours and ordered before M32. Closed on 2026-10-18 with the tours built: the deploy (M33 U4) and the kill criterion (M33 U9) are publishing rather than the tour, and moved to M42 with their refs unchanged.
state: closed
position: 344

### M34
title: What the Notion trial found
goal: A stranger's model, handed any export, reads it in with the engine's own readers instead of typing rows through the chat, and the document says what is wrong in it without being asked - so 'won't let you be wrong quietly' runs on its own, for the person and for the model. From the Notion trial, 2026-10-05: 19 tables and 902 rows came across and every count matched, but nothing was checked; the session cost ~4.8M tokens, ~40% of it hand-typed rows, because read_onto_format read as finance-only; a hand-typed degree average of 85 against data giving 84.52, stale statuses and empty links surfaced only when asked; and the model dropped rows and assumed a time zone without saying so. Done when the Obsidian trial and a Notion rerun (T1) import with no rows typed through the chat and the document reports the source's problems unprompted.
