### Stable ids
question: Should a row's id be made once, at creation, and written into the text document — a short random id that never changes — instead of derived from the row's content (D-247) and left out of the text (D-245)? A derived id changes on every edit: on 2026-09-23 an update was refused because the ids from the call before it were already stale. A written id stays valid across edits, survives a merge (two branches cannot collide on a random short id), and answers 'M22 U6 #1'. Cost: a text row carries one more line, and D-245 and D-247 are revisited.
