breaks: No column for it; the identity document extended its own copy with answer and blocks
state: accepted

### Arrange a dashboard: make one block wider or taller than the others
unit: M53 U7
should: A block is resized by dragging its edge, in width and height
breaks: Maintainer, 2026-10-22, reviewing the dashboard: 'id like the blocks to be resizeable.' Blocks have fixed widths (a total one column, others two) and height by content. Fix: M53 F4.
state: fault

### At `#/formats`, go to New format → By hand. Call it `Ingredient`, then add a real column with a unit and a minimum, an enum with two members, and a money column. Change a type after filling its fields. Save, then Edit, take a column out, and read the plan. Then use From a declaration: paste the ingredient fixture and press Open it in the editor. Try Copy the declaration. (M20 T1 has since turned this form into a four-step walk; judge it there.)
unit: M19 U2a
should: Fields follow the type: bounds only on integer and real, members only on enum, no unit on money. A retype clears what the new type cannot hold. A new format does not open red — the count says 3 things to fix and Save is disabled, but no field is accused until it has been typed in. Each problem sits beside its column. Removing a money column shows two steps (`price_minor`, `price_currency`). The import lands as 31 filled fields with the name locked. Copy puts on the clipboard the same markdown that Show prints.
breaks: A refusal drawn on the wrong column: `price_minor` has to find its way back to the money column `price`, and no test covers that lookup. Second: the draft is lost if you navigate away mid-edit. That is deliberate, and it may be wrong.
not_tried: A refusal on screen; the clipboard inside the shell; and a format you actually want, declared from scratch in the form with nobody helping.
state: open

### At the 0.2.0 release cut: bring the testing rule into the plugin's generic skill copies, `hosts/claude/skills/closing-pass/SKILL.md` and `hosts/claude/skills/run-milestone/SKILL.md`, from M51 F6's own edits (`git show ee9d513 -- hosts/claude/skills`, reachable from main through merge f19f264), in the same commit that sets the plugin manifest's version for 0.2.0.
unit: M51 F6
