### Build the recipe case at `#/formats` in this order: `ingredient` (name, kcal), `recipe` (name, servings min 1, printed_per_serving), then `recipe_line` with links to recipe and ingredient, `amount_g` in g, and nothing has to add up. Then edit `recipe`: add the sum `total_kcal` over recipe_line.recipe, working out `amount_g / 100 * ingredient.kcal` in kcal; and use Write one out for `total_kcal / servings = printed_per_serving` at ± 2%. Add rows from a conversation and read the recipe back. Try deleting `ingredient`.
unit: M19 U4b
should: Points at appears for a link column and lists the other formats and this one. Whose link lists only the columns pointing back at recipe. The plan says "fmt_recipe already matches. Saving changes the wording and nothing else." format_rows prints `total_kcal: 1805.8 kcal — the sum over 2 rows of recipe_line.` above `per_serving: proved`. Deleting ingredient is refused, naming recipe_line.
breaks: Judge first: the ordering does not close, so a conversation can never set up the recipe case end to end. Three ways out: leave it; let declare_format add an aggregate; or let it take several formats at once. It is your decision; M20 U5's drag answered it from the screen side. Then: a fold refusing in whole is correct and may be unpleasant on a half-typed vault — would you rather have "1,405 kcal over 3 of 4 lines"? And one hop means recipe → line → ingredient → supplier is unreachable. A sum of no rows is 0, so a new recipe fails per_serving loudly.
not_tried: A real vault and any scale: a fold is one query per row per aggregate, and scale.test.ts covers no declared table. Also untried: what a model does when it needs two linked formats and gets one call.
state: open

