### Declare `ingredient` with name and `density` (real, g per ml — Per appears only on integer and real), `recipe` with name and `printed_g` (real, g), and `recipe_line` with the two links and `amount` of type quantity (the Unit box disappears). Then edit recipe: sum over recipe_line.recipe of `amount in g via ingredient.density` in g, and the identity `total_g = printed_g` ± 1. Add rows with the plugin, since a quantity needs two keys (`amount: 200`, `amount_unit: ml`).
unit: M19 U4c
