breaks: The editor had no way to enter a quantity row (M20 U1 has since added a row form — check it takes the two boxes). `per` is free text, so `g` per `mL` is accepted at declaration and only fails when an identity bridges through it. The call most worth overturning: a `via` that could never fire is refused as dead weight, even `weight_g in kg via density`, where it may just be someone drafting. And a quantity takes no bound, so "never negative" is not sayable.
