breaks: The seeded table is 28 guesses. Are the conventions right for your kitchen (tbsp 15 ml, cup 240 ml, tsp 5)? Is COUNT with only `each` an obstruction? Is `in` the word, and does binding tighter than `*` match what you'd write? The asymmetry worth disagreeing with: conversion happens only where `in` is written, so `pack + serving` adds 1.5 to 250 and says nothing. That is the price of Atwater being correct. Is the density-is-a-column boundary the one you meant? Every later format is written against it.
not_tried: A real note of yours: whether any vault identity wants a conversion, and which units the notes really use. Also untried: a .format.md written against a corrected 20 ml tablespoon carried into another document — nothing warns.
