breaks: The switch is per machine, not per document (localStorage), so it is the same answer for every .emd you open and it does not travel to another machine. That is probably right — a rail is not a fact about a file — but it is the call most worth disagreeing with, and it is cheap to move. And turning the pack on inside a fresh document drops you straight into the eight-step wizard, sidebar and all gone, because an untouched document is one the ledger has never onboarded: correct by the flow's own rule, and it feels like a trapdoor.
not_tried: The shell. Everything was driven in the browser. `electron/menu.ts` is File/Edit/View and names no ledger screen, so nothing is expected — but the menu, the recents list and a .emd opened by double-click have not been seen with the pack staged.
