### Link
flag: two_words_one_thing
issue: One relation, five phrasings: link (the column type), 'Points at' (the column form), 'Links here' (the far entry), 'has many…' (the drag on Connections) and 'point it at' (the tour); the screen that makes them is Connections.
rename_to: Link (the column form says 'Links to'; the far entry keeps 'Links here'; the tour says link)
means: A column holding the id of a row of another format — the first type whose meaning is outside its row. It may point at its own format. The REFERENCES clause is documentation; the refusal that holds is at the moment a row is written. A `links` column holds several, in order.
rejected: Points at (the column form, until D-451); point it at (the tour's caption, until D-451)
named_by: D-451
scope: engine
shown_in: screen
