### M22 U2
milestone: M22
scope: engine
title: the migration, and only the list-shaped notes
landed: 2026-09-23
state: built
brief: Moved the list-shaped back-catalogue into the document, with `scope` (engine, or ledger for the pack's) on every decision and unit row: M19 entire (decisions, units, review entries), every engine decision D-001..D-208, and the ledger's M5-M7 and M13-M17 — 208 decisions in all. Each answer is a judgement, enough to act on without the argument; an overturned entry is amended or superseded, and `supersedes` holds one link, so a second amender is named in the older row's answer. STOPPED SHORT ON PURPOSE (author, 2026-09-23): the ledger's M1-M4 decisions (D-001..D-059 in docs/packs/ledger/decisions.md), the roadmap's pre-M19 unit lines and review.md's pre-M19 entries stay in docs/archive/ and the ledger notes — the pack is parked and moving them was several sessions for records nobody asks. A miss there means grep. If one ever matters, move that one row then. The prose notes never moved.

### M22 U3
milestone: M22
scope: engine
title: the gap list, written down as it is found
landed: 2026-09-23
state: built
brief: The gaps the dogfood exposed are rows now, 'M22 U3 #1' to '#8', not prose. Two are answered: proofs are idle for lists (D-242) and a link printed as a uuid (D-241). Six are open: a supersedes chain needs more than one hop, search is substring and not ranked, one file on one machine versus a two-branch merge nobody has tried, a write that names a link's target by name, a column that can say unique (two rows really did share a ref), and the two windows in documentStore.save(). Each is a question, never a licence to change a rule. From here on a gap is a row when it is found, so this unit does not need to reopen.

