### M22 U5
milestone: M22
scope: engine
title: the easy path is the typed one
landed: 2026-09-23
decision: D-246
state: built
brief: The document is additive work today — markdown AND a row — and markdown is the path of least resistance, so the rule to write both lasted four hours and its own author broke it four times. HALF OF THIS IS RETIRED BY D-246: with the document itself readable there is no second file to drift, so the render step and the staleness check both go. What survives is only what is needed while 09-decision-log.md is still the home of M0-M19, which is until U2 lands. Cheap and now: docs:check fails when a `## D-xxx` heading exists with no row (about twenty lines, runs at the commit seam where it would have caught all four); the closing-pass skill writes the row, since it is already invoked at the moment a decision is recorded; CLAUDE.md carries the four formats' columns so a write needs no round trip first; and the tools stay loaded rather than deferred, which U0's ~4,970 tokens is what made affordable. But affordance beats enforcement and that is U4 and U6: a document with no second copy has nowhere to type one.

