brief: The idea: each column type has one or more inputs, chosen per format; adding an entry is one seamless page running through them in column order; a long-text column renders as markdown, so a mostly-text format reads like an .md note. The view lives beside the format, not in its declaration (presentation is not the domain layer). The page's shape is the format: no free blocks — that is the line from a general workspace. Design the view so M27's views (roadmap, board) are the same kind of thing. The table stays; this is the readable door, for people who will not read a table. Decided 2026-10-01: the sheet stays the default view; every row gets a button that opens the entry view for that row. BUILT (D-294): RowEditor became EntryView at #/formats/:name/entry/:id (and entry/new), still inside FormatRows; inputs per column in format_view_column (migration 052, one table for every view kind) and views.md; our own markdown subset; pack entries read-only.
