scope: engine
title: the roadmap tracks a session live
landed: 2026-10-01
decision: D-304
state: built
brief: The idea: with memory.emd open on the roadmap (U4), a unit is seen to move to in_progress and then built as a session works. Unit-level only; step-level progress was rejected (D-298). (1) unit.state gains in_progress, plus claimed_by (text) and started (date). (2) A conditional write: an update may say what it expects ('set state to in_progress only if it is still planned') and is refused otherwise. This answers 'Conditional write' and is how two agents claim without both getting it. (3) /run-milestone and the closing pass mark a unit in_progress when it is handed out and built when it lands. (4) The app picks up a write from outside without a prompt when it holds no unsaved change: find what useDiskWatch does today first. The view is read-only while it tracks, so the second writer of 'M22 U3 #8' is not opened by this unit; say so in the decision, do not close that question. Where it breaks: a text document's ids change on every edit (D-247), so the session must address the unit by ref, not by an id from an earlier call; a session that dies leaves a unit in_progress forever, so show started.
files: src/plugin/tools/formats.ts (where, expect), src/plugin/write.ts (holdingLock), src/plugin/tools/claim.test.ts, src/state/documentStore.ts (followDisk), src/data/storage/externalChange.ts, src/ui/useDiskWatch.ts, src/data/packs/development/formats/unit.format.md, src/data/packs/development/views.md, .claude/skills/run-milestone/SKILL.md, .claude/skills/closing-pass/SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/plugin.md
