### M27 U8
milestone: M27
scope: engine
title: the views get a design: a timeline roadmap, motion that explains, one theme
landed: 2026-10-01
decision: D-306
state: built
brief: Fault on M27 U4 (2026-10-01): the UI is too simple. THE SPEC IS THE APPROVED MOCKUP: docs/mockups/m27-u8/ (roadmap.dc.html, board.dc.html, page.dc.html; approved 2026-10-01, chosen over a design tool on token cost and because motion is judged live; live copy https://claude.ai/artifact/SomQxRNuTNVuE3VpTef7Sb). Read the three files' <style> and markup; the data in their scripts is a snapshot, the app reads the document. What it settles: (1) the roadmap is a timeline: a dot per row on one vertical line, closed filled ink, open ringed accent with a halo, planned hollow; the line solid to the open row and dashed after; a segment bar per row (one segment per folded row, coloured by state) and its counts; rows fold with a grid-rows transition, the open and planned ones start unfolded. (2) Motion that explains a change only: a moved board card slides in from the side it came from; a unit the disk watch sees change pulses its dot once and its row flashes accent-soft; nothing animates on first paint; prefers-reduced-motion turns all of it off. (3) One theme: square cards (radius-card 0, as M26 U1), uppercase label chips, the board's lanes on surface with an empty lane showing a dashed 'Nothing <state>', and the page as body left and links one hop each way in a right column with 'Nothing' where there is nothing. Approved with the mockup and to be written as U8's decision: accent marks in_progress and the open milestone (live work is where you act), an amendment to D-125's 'accent never reports'. Write what is new into docs/11-ui-design-language.md. Where it breaks: 30 milestones must still scan; dark mode; Hebrew titles keep Bidi; a live update animates the row that changed and nothing else.
