### M28 F11
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: two exports of one bank are one account, a known layout is recognised, an overlap is caught
landed: 2026-10-03
decision: D-337
state: built
brief: 2026-10-03, reading statements on Home (Read files, D-313/U5): a second spreadsheet export with the same layout was not detected as the same structure; two exports of one bank with an overlapping month were not caught; and Wealth counted the one bank as two. Either the input was wrong or the detection was. Investigate before fixing: (1) why a second export with the same layout was not matched to the reader the first one taught (header fingerprint too strict? a title row, a date in the header, a sheet name?); (2) whether two files of one bank and account with an overlapping month dedupe the overlap (natural keys, D-098 idempotent imports) and, if the rows were written twice, why; (3) why the same bank became two accounts/institutions on Wealth Overview (the new_account path in import_statement or the screen's create-account step of D-313 making a fresh institution each time instead of matching an existing account by number/bank). The real exports are in the real-documents folder: read them (copies in the scratchpad), never write to a real .emd, never copy them into the repo; reproduce with synthetic fixtures for the tests. If it was an input mistake, the screen must have made it easy to make: say what it was and make the right choice the obvious one (e.g. offer the existing account first). Fix each cause; a file whose rows are already in the document says so on the read screen rather than quietly writing or skipping. Record a decision.
