### M28 F29
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: Groups and top-level categories are one tree, and a bucket points at any category
landed: 2026-10-04
decision: D-348
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-04, after F25 (D-342): 'yes, let a bucket point at a group. but im not sure both group and top level category is needed- don't they shadow the same thing?' then, offered merge vs keep both: 'merge them, now'. Today there are three levels (category_group → top-level category → subcategory) and group and top-level category both mean 'a heading that collects what is under it'. Merge: a group becomes a top-level category that holds others (the seeded Living, Transport, Lifestyle… become seeded top-level categories with the starter categories under them), so the tree is up to three deep (decide and log the depth limit; three is enough). A Plan bucket points at ANY category and counts everything filed under it and its descendants (check what a bucket on a parent counts today and make it so). Plan's headings (F25) become the top level of the tree. F25/F28's group machinery folds into 'move a category under another': the group select, New group…, group rename, and the `group`/`groups` arguments of create_category/edit_categories become parent/reparent (keep parity, D-227/D-234); category_group retires (the pack's RETIRED_FORMATS path, M28 U1). Keep the existing rules: a parent and its children share a kind (same tab); system categories stay system; F18's delete/move targets (D-340) and merge follow the new depth; the category picker, ParentPicker search, Categories list/panel, By merchant and Transactions handle three levels; Hebrew names stay Bidi-isolated. NO conversion machinery for old documents (author: 'ill make a full new workflow of my ledger after m30'), but an older document must still open without error. Log a decision superseding D-342's group parts. The author tests this, then closes M28.
