### M28 F7
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: the plan's dividers snap, and a change flows only to the right
landed: 2026-10-03
decision: D-321
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-03, trying U7/U7b (D-319, D-320): (1) 'the sliders don't snap to 50 shekels or percentage, i think percentage should only be int when slided unless explicitly written with a dot.' Dragging (bar or ring, pointer or arrow keys) snaps a fixed-amount bucket to ₪50 steps and a percent bucket to whole percents; a value typed into the bucket's field keeps whatever precision was typed (e.g. 12.5%). U7b already saw '₪5,500.50' while dragging a percent bucket. (2) 'when sliding a bucket or changing its split it changes all other buckets. i think it should be left to right, if i change left only right onward changes.' A change to bucket k — by dragging its divider or by typing its amount/percent — never moves buckets to its left; the difference is taken from (or given to) the buckets to its right, the next one first, then onward if it hits zero, and a 'what's left' bucket absorbs as it does. Find why every bucket moves today (percent buckets re-deriving from a changed base, the remainder, or the trade code) and fix the cause. This refines U7's choice 2A (neighbours trade): the neighbour on the right absorbs first. Bar and ring share the code; both must behave the same. Tests for the snap and the left-to-right rule, including a percent bucket followed by an amount bucket and a remainder at the end.
