### M28 U4
milestone: M28
scope: ledger
title: the frame and Paychecks get the new design, mockup first
landed: 2026-10-02
decision: D-312
state: built
brief: Closing M27, 2026-10-01: follow the new design and layout and improve the UI in general, perhaps with an HTML preview as just done. Aimed at D-306's look (square cards, uppercase chips, lanes on surface, accent on live work, motion only for a change). Decided 2026-10-02: go SCREEN BY SCREEN. This unit is the frame every screen shares (navigation, the new button style, the progress indicator) applied to ONE screen, Paychecks; each later screen is its own unit, named when it is reached. MOCKUP FIRST, the way M27 U8 was done: HTML mockup(s) in docs/mockups/m28-u4/, published as an artifact so they can be judged live, then STOP for approval. Nothing of the design is built before approval; the approved mockup is then the spec. Judging U3: the reading screen looks great; the navigation as a whole did not work, with the question why add paycheck/read payslips is at the top, and the buttons seemed no longer to fit the new design and to need better, modern ones; where it went should not be a separate tab of the paychecks, which should page by month or through clickable graph points; deduction types + readers is nice. So: navigation as a whole, actions placed where they belong rather than at the top, a new button style, Paychecks loses the where-it-went tab for month paging and clickable graph points. Asked for 2026-10-02: a trademark progress indicator for every loading or in-progress state, special to Emerald, perhaps the emerald icon assembling/disassembling — drawn from src/ui/emerald.svg's facets, in code (SVG + CSS, respecting reduced motion), one component used for every loading/in-progress state, and shown while payslips are read; it belongs in the mockup, live. Small and separate from the mockup, do it first and commit it on its own: once paychecks are added from read, redirect to the paychecks screen where all the paychecks are (after Write on #/paychecks/read). Carried from D-306: the live/done/dropped word list in src/ui/formats/tone.ts is not declared, and light mode was never checked visually. DONE so far: redirect 741f2a1; mockup 7d8e016, docs/mockups/m28-u4/paychecks.html, https://claude.ai/artifact/3eCeFsysUmqofbDF6qS3Uy. The mockup was APPROVED 2026-10-02: navigation A (tree sidebar, the open section's pages under it); buttons B (split tile, icon in a darker leading tile); month paging keeps all three (arrows + arrow keys, clickable graph points, clickable table rows); the indicator keeps cycling during a batch rather than tracking slips read. Build exactly that into src/ (the frame app-wide, the indicator as the one loading component, Paychecks), drop the unchosen options; amend docs/11-ui-design-language.md (the indicator breaks 'no loading state longer than one cycle'; the split-tile button goes beyond the two weights) with a decision.
