brief: Asked for 2026-10-03: after Wealth, revamp the ledger onboarding. A new user was run through the app the same day. RESHAPED 2026-10-03, before the mockup: instead of onboarding, 'guide me through the app', with an onboarding dialog explaining where to put what, navigating inside the ledger, and the same structure later for the general engine (unrelated) — less heavy, less disconnected, lighter as a feature. So: no separate onboarding flow. A 'Guide me' that walks the real screens: a small dialog anchored to the place it is explaining (where to drop statements and payslips, By merchant, Plan, Wealth's opening balance and cushion), moving through the ledger's actual routes, skippable and resumable, offered on a new document and reachable any time later. It should lead into what M28 built: batch reading (D-310, D-313), By merchant (D-315), Plan (D-319), opening balance and cushion (D-324, D-325, D-328). Build the guide so it is not ledger-specific: a pack declares its steps, so the engine (formats, linking) can get its own guide later with the same structure (that is a later unit, not this one). DONE so far: vs plan fix 83d2f4c (D-329); mockup 4679ade, docs/mockups/m28-u9/guide.html, https://claude.ai/artifact/MHoRFUbfDRcjJCkYsLRJ2y — it is the spec; build by porting its own source. Six steps (read files, By merchant, fixed expenses, the split, opening balance, cushion) as a pack-declared list with route, anchor, words, done-test. APPROVED 2026-10-03 with every recommendation: (a) B — the onboarding flow goes, its checklist becomes the guide's done-tests and its Home line is where the guide resumes; (b) A — a step only points and ticks itself when the document shows it done, no new write; (c) B — picks up where it stopped, from Home's line and Help › Guide me; (d) B — done steps ticked and passed over, still reachable. ALL suggestions: S1 a done step names what it found ('Read 3 statements and 2 payslips'); S2 the pack declares its steps as a list (route, place, words, done-test) so the engine's guide reuses the reader; S3 ← → move between steps, Esc puts the guide away; S4 each screen names its places (data-guide) and a test fails if a step names a place no screen has; S5 on an empty document a step that needs a statement says 'later' and waits; S6 no dark overlay, the screen stays usable underneath; S7 a guide_status tool replaces onboarding_status and advance_onboarding (parity in step, D-227/D-234). Build exactly that; record a decision.
