### M29 F7
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: A total can add up a worked-out column, and a sum of money keeps its currency
landed: 2026-10-04
decision: D-349
state: built
brief: 2026-10-04, working out how to check a paycheck's gross against the days worked (days with hours = end - start and earned = hours * rate, worked out): what if the day's earnings is derived automatically? (1) An aggregate (a total on the target, D-224) may fold a worked-out column (D-334): today aggregateRejection resolves names from stored columns only (src/domain/format/declaration.ts ~1363, via resolveName ~1169) and refuses with 'work_day has no such column' though earned is on the sheet; a rollup already folds derived columns (declaration.ts ~1514), so make the two agree. It folds each row's figure AS SHOWN (rounded per row, D-333), so the total equals the sum of what the rows display. (2) A sum of money keeps its currency: evaluateAggregate folds bare minor units (src/domain/format/aggregate.ts ~334-369) and inputsWithAggregates sets none (src/data/repositories/formatJoinRepository.ts ~518-521), so USD and ILS rows add up silently and a USD sum can prove against an ILS figure (a D-138 hole); mixed currencies make it unchecked naming a row, and the identity refuses a currency mismatch as it does for two columns (identity.ts ~935-941). (3) The total shows on each target row as a read-only figure (asked for: visible), like paycheck's deducted. Synthetic tests: a work_day with derived earned, a paycheck total of it, gross = total proved and failed; mixed currencies unchecked.
