### M29 U3b
milestone: M29
scope: engine
title: a column can be derived from other columns, and SQL can read it
landed: 2026-10-03
decision: D-334
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-03: 'what if we add columns automatically derived from other columns rather than asserted, additionally? like excel has its sum and formulas.' and 'why isnt it an sql column querable? can we make it so?' then 'whatever u think is best, not overkill and doesn't hurt existing engine structure.' Driver's shape, agreed: a derived column is an identity's expression (D-222 grammar, D-224's one hop and aggregate, D-223's units) used to PRODUCE a value instead of checking a typed one — same parser, no new language. It lives in a per-format SQL VIEW (e.g. fmt_<name>_v: the stored columns plus every derived one), compiled by the engine from its own parsed AST, never from the declaration's text — so nothing a person or model wrote reaches db.run (amend D-222's 'no identity becomes SQL' to say exactly this). Why a view and not generated columns: a view covers same-row arithmetic, a linked row's column, an aggregate over linking rows and unit conversion (a join to the units table) with one mechanism, is computed on read so it cannot go stale, stores nothing twice (D-087), and anything that opens the .emd (sqlite3 included) sees the derived columns. Rules: a derived cell is never editable; an empty input gives an empty cell naming the input, never 0 (NULL propagates; x/0 is NULL = unchecked); an aggregate is NULL in whole if any covered row cannot answer (CASE WHEN COUNT(*)=COUNT(x)); money stays integer minor units with an explicit rounding rule; the result type (money, quantity with its dimension, number) is inferred and checked at declare time, two currencies refused or unchecked; derived on derived is allowed, a cycle is refused at declare; still no functions or conditionals. Identities stay exactly as they are, evaluated in TypeScript; a test proves the SQL compile and the TS evaluator agree on the shared grammar over a table of cases (moving identity verdicts into the view is NOT this unit). Screens: a derived column shows read-only with its expression on hover; the format editor (U1) declares one. Tools in step (D-227/D-234): declare/extend take a derived column, format_rows returns it. Record a decision. Before U4, so U4's durations are a derived column.
files: src/domain/format/derived.ts (new), declaration.ts (language 16, derived, nameRejection), identity.ts (toWhole exported), artefact.ts (derived table), draft.ts (DerivedDraft, renames follow); src/data/db/migrations/055_derived.sql, database.ts (drop views before migrating); src/data/repositories/formatRepository.ts (format_derived, dropDerivedViews/buildDerivedViews), formatDerivedRepository.ts (new, derivedOf), formatJoinRepository.ts (exact carried), storage/encoding.ts; src/plugin/tools/formats.ts (derived on declare/extend/formats/format_rows); src/ui/formats/DerivedQuestions.tsx (new), ShapePanel.tsx, ColumnQuestions.tsx (worked out tile), shape.ts, RowSheet.tsx, NewFormat.tsx, screens/FormatRows.tsx; tests formatDerivedRepository.test.ts (agreement), draft.test.ts, formats.test.ts, parity.test.ts, server.test.ts
