### M30 U5
milestone: M30
scope: ledger
title: A dated reading of what a holding is worth
landed: 2026-10-04
decision: D-358
state: built
brief: Decided 2026-10-04: a goal's progress is what it is worth now (the latest reading), with what went in shown beside it — a goal can go down, and that is true. Interest, bonuses and fee rebates on such an account are growth of its cash, not income; its leftover cash belongs to no goal unless chosen. Add a holding reading (holding, date, quantity, value as printed, cost basis as printed, the statement it came from), modelled on fund readings (fund_balance_snapshot, fundRepository) and recorded through a tool; growth = reading − what went in, derived and keyed by the reading, never a fetched price (D-308). quantity × price is a check only (the broker prints price in agorot). Re-recording the same date changes nothing. The cash line is checked against the account's running balance. Goal views show worth now and put in.
