### M32 U1
milestone: M32
scope: engine
title: A pack is a file
state: planned
brief: Product session, 2026-10-05: the development pack is already pure data (five .format.md files and views.md, no seeds, no code, no screen), so a pack a person makes should have its shape, not the ledger's. Define one file, <name>.pack.md: a text document (D-246) with a header - pack (name), title, summary (one sentence), version, needs (other packs, by name; may be empty) - followed by format and views parts, and no rows except, optionally, rows marked as examples. Read and write it in src/domain/format/ (pure, imports nothing - the boundary test holds). A pack from a file is data only: anything that is not a header, a declaration, a views line or an example row is refused by name, and a declaration that names an owner (D-269 - written only through a pack's code) is refused, because a file can bring no code to honour it. That is a decision; write it. Done-test: the development pack's five formats and views.md written as one .pack.md and read back give declarations and view settings identical to what src/data/packs/development/ holds; a pack file with an owner, or with an unknown part, is refused with a sentence naming the line.
files: src/domain/format/document.ts, src/domain/format/pack.ts (new), src/domain/format/pack.test.ts (new), docs/engine.md

### M32 U2
