### M32 U3
milestone: M32
scope: engine
title: Add a pack to a document
state: planned
brief: Open a .pack.md and add it: the reconciler adopts its formats (adoptFormat) behind the usual plan - what tables appear, which of the document's own names clash and are renamed (D-268's rule), which needs are missing (refused here; U5 offers them) - and restores its views (restoreViewSettings). The document records the pack it now keeps - its header, as a part of the text form and a table in the SQLite form (schema change, migration, docs/04-data-model.md). That is a decision against D-115's 'nothing is stored to say a pack is shown': argue it is document content the person put there, not app state, and write it either way. A new engine write is a failing test until both halves exist (D-234): add_pack (dry-run until commit: true) beside the screen. Done-test: adding the development pack's file to a fresh document yields the same formats and views as docs/memory.emd, adding it twice changes nothing, and a clash is renamed and named in the plan.
