### M32 U9
milestone: M32
scope: engine
title: A pack carries its readers
state: planned
brief: Author, 2026-10-05: readers go inside packs. A reader is a saved mapping of one file layout onto one format (src/domain/format/reader.ts, M26 U5): the header in the file's order, its signature, the header row, and which column is which key - positions and labels, never a figure. So a pack can carry, beside a format, the readers that read a known export onto it (a bank's .csv, an app's export), and a person who adds the pack reads that file in one step: fitReader finds it by signature, as if they had made it themselves. Save as pack (U2) offers the readers each chosen format has, by their names; Add a pack (U3) adds them as readers of the formats it adopts, behind the same plan, and a reader whose format was renamed for a clash follows it. The privacy line is D-211's third point - designing is public-safe, filling is private: a reader in a pack holds header cells and bindings and nothing read from a row, and a fixed value that names a row of the person's own (a link fixed to their account) is dropped and said so. Tabular readers only: the ledger's label-value templates (payslips, fund reports, document_template) ship in its bundle already and stay out of scope. Done-test: a pack saved from a document that has read a .csv carries that reader and not one value from the file's rows; added to a fresh document, the same .csv reads onto the format with no mapping step; a reader whose format is missing from the pack is refused by name.
files: src/domain/format/reader.ts, src/domain/format/pack.ts, src/data/repositories/formatIntakeRepository.ts, docs/mapping-templates.md
blocks: ["M32 U2","M32 U3"]

### M33 F1
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The receipt tour, from a look at U3
landed: 2026-10-07
decision: D-415
state: built
brief: 2026-10-07, watching U3 (ce32ea4, 5382be4) on docs/mockups/m33-u2/host.html with the browser pane visible: (1) THE EDIT/ADD COLUMN OVERLAPS, not well, even at the minimum size; it looks clunky. In the driver's look at an 800-wide pane, the 'Say what adds up' bar sits over the sheet's top-right corner and the row-icon and '+' columns crowd the last column. Find every overlap in the frame at the host page's sizes and fix it where it lives: in the app if the app overlaps at that width on its own, in the frame's scaling if the frame causes it. (2) THE DELAY IS STILL THERE: the stillness before the first motion, and the caption holds before each scene moves. Measure it with the pane visible (it is now; motion can be seen). The ring should start moving within about a second of a caption appearing, travelling while the caption is read; the reading-time hold applies, capped, before the first click or keystroke, not before any motion. (3) REMOVE STEP 6 ('Your turn. Describe something you keep, and type in what it says.'): it has no point. The tour ends on the answer, 'They don't: the card was charged 12.00 more than the receipt says.', held, then loops; Try it stays in the strip. (4) ON A PHONE IT IS TOO TINY: the whole app scaled to 375 is unreadable. Decided: it has to be cut-off screenshots. Do it as a CROP of the live app rather than stored images: at phone width the app still lays out at desktop width, and the frame shows a zoomed window around where the action is (the highlight's box, else the ring's anchor), readable at 375, panning smoothly between steps and static under reduced motion. Stored screenshots only if a live crop cannot be made legible, and then say why. The strip stays readable above it. Done-test: no overlap at any host-page size; first motion within ~1 s of each caption; five captions; at 375 the tour is readable as a moving crop; check:tours passes at both sizes.
