### M33 F5
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The development tour, redone as a conversation with a model beside the sheet
landed: 2026-10-07
decision: D-427
state: built
brief: 2026-10-07, on U6 (9de9696): TOO COMPLICATED; a visitor is distracted easily and there is too much text to read. Perhaps this pack has no question but an answer: the tour is a conversation with a model shown on the side, a mock, the way the custom tour shows its synthetic receipt beside the sheet. The story: the person asks for a feature; the model answers that it contradicts a decision the project already took (the decision row is shown); they reach a conclusion; the model writes it down: a decision row, a milestone and its units, which appear in the sheet or on the board as the chat says so. Few, short captions; the chat carries the story and is short too. Honesty as with the receipt: the app has no chat on its own screens, so the chat is the tour's own panel and must not pretend to be the app; the rows land through the real engine (as the MCP server's write would), never painted into the page. Keep U6's synthetic project (the shared shopping list) and the taken_by rename. STOP: the storyboard (the chat's lines and the captions, in a few lines each) for approval before it is ported; the U6 tour stays until then. Done-test: the storyboard is approved; the ported tour runs to its last caption under check:tours at both sizes; at 375 the crop follows the rows as they appear; no screen the visitor reads has more than one caption and one chat line new at a time. The storyboard was APPROVED 2026-10-07 (bb3ebbe, docs/mockups/m33-u6/tour-development-chat.md) with the driver's picks: (1) undo against D-4; (2) the title 'Ask for a feature. The project answers first.' (a statement, since this pack has an answer, not a question); (3) the panel header as written, and no result line under a writing line; (4) no refusal beat; (5) the ending on the roadmap with M4 and its units. The `write` step action through DemoHandle.record (the same stageRows/insertRows the tool uses) is accepted. Port it; it replaces U6's tour.
