brief: 2026-10-07, on F5 (bb5e4d9, D-427): (1) each chat message is highlighted when it is sent: the tour's outline (the same highlight that draws itself around a box) goes around the newest chat line as it arrives, desktop and the 375 card alike, static under reduced motion. (2) A BUG: the highlight box stays for a moment when the tour goes from step 3 to step 4; the outline must leave when its step ends (or move straight to the next box), never linger over a box that is no longer the point. Find the cause (likely the closing fade's inert copy of the outline from M39 U3/F1, or the outline waiting on settle before it clears) and fix it where it lives; check:tours should catch an outline that outlives its step if that is cheap. (3) RETIRE THE SHOPPING-LIST PROJECT: a specific fake project confuses a visitor. The project in the tour is generic: plain names that read as any software project (no product, no app idea to understand first), so the visitor follows decisions, milestones and units, not a made-up product. Keep the approved shape: a feature asked for, the model shows it goes against a decision already taken, they settle on what the decision allows, the model writes a decision, a milestone and its units; reword the feature and the decision generically (the session drafts it; the maintainer judges it after, so record the new lines in tour-development-chat.md, marked as changed from the approved ones). Also, as found on F5: at 1280x800 the last unit line (M4 U2) is cut about 15 px at the end; fix it if small. Done-test: every new chat line is outlined as it arrives; no outline outlives its step (3 to 4 included); no shopping-list words remain in the tour, its rows or the project fixture; check:tours passes at both sizes.
