### M33 F7
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: A claim over a sum of no rows, and rows named by id
landed: 2026-10-13
decision: D-465
state: built
brief: Found by U7 (765c21e, D-429), 2026-10-07, for the maintainer to decide before it is built: (1) a claim whose total folds no linked rows FAILS, because a sum of nothing is zero: in a real ledger every paycheck month before the timesheet started would read failed for hours_paid (gross = worked). Should a total over zero linked rows leave its claim unchecked (nothing to prove) rather than failed, or is zero the truth? This touches D-224's sum rule ('a sum that skipped a row is a smaller number and not a truer one'); a decision row records the answer. (2) A format with no text column (the timesheet day) shows row ids in another format's 'Links here' column; name such rows by something a person reads (e.g. the date, or the first column) instead of an id. Also: U7 left unused data-tour anchors in ColumnQuestions, DerivedQuestions, ConnectionPanel and Connections (a permission check refused reverting them); remove them if nothing uses them. And from U7's look: the ledger's Paychecks screen in the timesheet tour shows a red '800.00 stops here' because the demo has no split plan; give the demo document what it needs so scene 1 shows nothing red that is not the story.
