### M33 U2
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The frame and the custom tour, as a mockup and a storyboard
landed: 2026-10-07
decision: D-413
state: built
brief: STOP first: a mockup to be approved, ported in U3. Two things on paper. (1) The frame's chrome: a drawn pointer that is a ring and not an arrow, one caption line, a dotted progress line with a dot per step the visitor can jump to, the toggle between watching and trying, and Reset; the app's design language (docs/11-ui-design-language.md), accent on what you can act on; below a width the frame scales down and plays as a movie with take-over off. (2) The storyboard of the custom-format tour, the one the maintainer's site embeds: each step's anchor, action and caption, in the maintainer's words. The story it tells: a kind of thing the ledger does not have is declared by hand (a product the person tries, with a price and a rating), a row is added, text typed into the money column is refused, the row is linked to the transaction that paid for it, and the entry page shows both ends; then the caption says try it. Captions say what is happening, never what the engine is. Done-test: the mockup and the storyboard are in the repo and approved; nothing is ported. 2026-10-07, on the first mockup (bc37f31): it drew the app instead of running it, so it did not look like the real UI. Redo it on the real app: the frame's chrome around the real demo build (U1's dist-demo), the ring driving the real screens through the storyboard. Going back to Watch after Try it reopens the document's bytes and fast-forwards to the step it had reached; what the visitor changed is thrown away. The custom tour stays first (the ledger tour is U5). P1-P12 and the captions are judged on the redo. 2026-10-07, on the redo (a36eb13): the tour had no point a visitor could name, and its pacing was uneven. THE STORY IS REPLACED (the tried-product story above is withdrawn): a grocery receipt. A receipt format is declared (shop, date, printed total, and its lines); the lines are entered with a synthetic grocery receipt PNG shown beside the sheet, typed in by the ring as a person would (the app does not read a photo on its own screens and the tour must not pretend it does); a first identity proves the lines add up to the printed total; the receipt is linked to the card charge on the demo statement that paid it; a second identity fails because the card was charged 12.00 more than the receipt says; then the visitor's turn. The caption at the failure says only what was found (charged 12.00 more than the receipt says), never 'overcharged'. The goal a visitor leaves with: describe something you keep, and it becomes a table that won't let you be wrong quietly, even when the mistake is somebody else's. The ring is the accent, not ink (P1 reversed: white/ink was almost invisible). Pacing: every caption is held for a reading time set by its length before its actions start, and the actions run at one steady tempo (ring travel and typing speed constant); never paced by how many steps sit under a caption. Also fix, as found on the redo: the transaction page's six empty ledger link groups each saying 'Nothing' (show only what the tour needs, or hide empty groups if that is right for the app too), the refusal line showing tool wording on screen (price_currency, a format_rows hint, JSON), and the movie's last caption saying 'Press Try it' where a movie has no Try it. The synthetic receipt and its charge are added to the demo document's committed sources. 2026-10-07, on the third pass (14115ab): NO LEDGER in this tour and FEWER STEPS. The tour opens its own document, which holds no ledger pack: one declared card_charge format (date, merchant, amount stored positive) with a few synthetic rows including the Corner Market charge; U1's ledger document stays for U5, so the frame picks a document per tour. The receipt's LINES ARE DROPPED, and with them the receipt_line format, the Connections join and the first identity. The story, about six captions and under a minute: card charges already in the document; a receipt is declared (shop, date, total, paid_with -> card_charge) with one identity, total = paid_with.amount; the receipt is typed from the PNG (three cells); it is pointed at the Corner Market charge; the identity fails, 'The card was charged 12.00 more than the receipt says'; your turn. No minus caption. The ring is still too fast, and on every click it jitters a little toward the top-left and back: find the cause (the ring follows the clicked element every frame while it changes size or moves, the press animation, or the half-width offset) and fix it so the ring sits still through a click. The driver left uncommitted edits as a starting point: travel 900 ms, key 90 ms, beat 500 ms, and place() holding position when the anchor measures 0x0 or is disconnected. 2026-10-07, same pass, four frame asks: (1) a speed slider in the strip scaling the whole pace (about 0.5x-2x, default 1x; remembered only as a guarded per-viewer convenience); (2) a highlight: an accent outline that draws itself around the box the eye should be on, like a line travelling around it, then held, following the box as the ring does (e.g. the Corner Market charge's row at the start); a step property separate from where the ring points, static under reduced motion, used where the story needs the eye; (3) the strip moves to the TOP of the frame (P3 reversed); (4) each tour has a larger title and a one-line description under it, tour data, drafted for the maintainer to reword.
