### M33 U3
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The runner and the custom tour, as approved
landed: 2026-10-07
decision: D-414
state: built
brief: The runner (src/demo/tour/), as approved in U2. A tour is rows of a declared tour_step format in the demo document (tour, position, anchor, action: click, type, press, wait or say, value, caption), written by make-demo-document.mjs from a committed .format.md and rows under fixtures/synthetic/demo/, so the runner is generic and a pack can one day carry its own tour (M32). The runner moves the ring to a data-tour anchor, dispatches the real event, waits for the next anchor to exist and never for a fixed delay, updates the caption and the dots, and loops by reopening the document's bytes. A visitor's click or the toggle stops it and lifts the overlay that swallowed input; Reset replays; a dot jumps by resetting and fast-forwarding without animation; prefers-reduced-motion drops the travel and keeps the steps. Anchors are data-tour attributes on the app's elements, added only where the custom tour needs them. scripts/check-tours.mjs replays every tour at fast-forward in a real browser and fails on the first step whose anchor is missing; the Electron binary already in devDependencies is preferred over a new dependency, and the session says what the check costs. Done-test: the custom tour runs to its last caption under the check and in the browser pane; a click mid-tour stops it and the visitor can type into the sheet; Reset replays from the first step; the mockup's text matches the frame's. 2026-10-07: Watch after Try it never plays on over the visitor's changes; it reopens the bytes and fast-forwards to the step it had reached. U2's redo runs on the real app, so whatever of the runner it already built is U3's starting point, not throwaway. 2026-10-07 (from U2's fourth pass): each tour opens its own document (the custom tour's holds no ledger pack); a tour carries a title and a one-line description; a step carries a highlight anchor (the box outlined) beside the ring's anchor; the check also fails on a missing highlight anchor. 2026-10-07, U2 approved (ac8c8eb) with three first tasks: (1) THE WHY. A viewer followed what happened but never why; the tour opens with the question the person has and the red verdict answers it. Title: 'Did the card charge what the receipt says?' Description: 'You kept the receipt from the grocery store. The card statement came in. Do they agree?' First caption carries the motive (e.g. 'The card statement came in. One of these is the grocery store.'); the failure caption answers it ('They don't: the card was charged 12.00 more than the receipt says.'); the steps between read as moves toward the answer. (2) The first step feels like five seconds of nothing: find what holds it (load, reopen, the first caption's reading time at the slower 1x, a wait for an anchor) and make the tour start moving promptly. (3) It may not scale well across screens: measure the frame on the host page (docs/mockups/m33-u2/host.html) at a ladder of widths (about 1440, 1280, 1040, 900, 768, 720, 600, 375) and heights, and fix what breaks (caption and title wrapping, the strip's controls, the ring and outline in a scaled app, the movie threshold); report the narrowest width it still lays out at, which U4 hands to the maintainer's site.
