### M33 U4
milestone: M42
scope: engine
title: Deployed and embeddable: Pages, the frame's contract, and the handoff to an embedding site
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-495
state: built
brief: A GitHub Pages workflow that builds dist-demo/ on push and serves it under the repository's path (relative paths already; Pages sets no X-Frame-Options and no frame-ancestors). The frame's contract: ?tour=<name> picks the tour and autoplay=1 starts it; the frame posts {source: 'emerald-demo', event: 'step' | 'took-over' | 'reset', step, of} to its parent and nothing else; it works with referrerpolicy=no-referrer and an empty allow list; below a width it renders at desktop width scaled to fit and take-over is off; nothing leaves the page. Everything here is proved locally before any account exists: dist-demo/ on one origin and a test page on another (127.0.0.1 and localhost are different sites, so storage partitioning is exercised), the maintainer sees and tries it in the browser pane. Only the deploy itself waits: Pages on the free plan serves public repositories only, so the first deploy is under the new public repository and is the maintainer's act (STOP). The handoff an embedding site asked for: the demo URL, a 1600x1000 PNG of the tour's first frame in the light scheme as the poster, and the narrowest width the frame still lays out at, written into this row; the embedding waits for both and blocks nothing here. Done-test: the custom tour autoplays inside an iframe on a page of another origin locally; the workflow publishes the folder when the maintainer runs it; the poster PNG and the width are in this row. HANDOFF TO THE EMBEDDING SITE (2026-10-07, D-418). Demo URL: https://<owner>.github.io/<repository>/ until the maintainer deploys; embed <URL>?tour=custom&autoplay=1 in an iframe with referrerpolicy=no-referrer and allow="", 16:10. Poster: fixtures/synthetic/demo/poster.png in this repo, 1600x1000, light, the custom tour at the end of its first scene, the Corner Market row outlined (D-419; remake with npm run build:demo && npm run demo:poster); it goes into the embedding site's images. Width: the frame lays out from 375 px wide and needs at least 440 px of height, so the site can show its 'Open the live demo' control down to 375 (it hides it under 832 today); from 690 px up a visitor can take the app over (Try it), below 690 it is a moving crop that is watched only. Messages the site may listen for: README.md, 'The demo, and embedding it'. Left for the done-test: the first deploy (the maintainer's). HISTORY-REWRITE GATE (an inbox row triaged in M44 U5, 2026-10-08; D-430): every commit so far is authored and committed under an old private address, which must never be public, and Pages serves public repositories only (D-418). Before the first deploy, in order, every step the maintainer's act: every Emerald session stopped at a commit seam; one git filter-repo with a mailmap on a fresh clone, so every author and committer reads Kfir Raphael Eliyahu <me@kfireliyahu.com>; pushed to a fresh, empty github.com/kfireliyahu/emerald-emd, not a transfer; the pre-rewrite clone deleted or moved offline; only then this unit's deploy. A session drafts the commands on the maintainer's go and runs none of them.
files: The deploy: the showcase is live at https://getemerald.dev from GitHub Pages on the public repository kfireliyahu/emerald-emd (source: GitHub Actions; the Demo workflow, .github/workflows/demo.yml, run 39129125774 succeeded), deployed from the first public commit 35309f4. HTTPS enforced; DNS at Cloudflare; the domain verified on the account. The build (D-418, 2026-10-07): .github/workflows/demo.yml, src/demo/tour/ (main.tsx, player.ts, Frame.tsx, frame.css, embed.ts + embed.test.ts), scripts/check-tours-window.cjs + check-tours.mjs, scripts/make-demo-poster.cjs, fixtures/synthetic/demo/poster.png, docs/mockups/m33-u4/embed.html, .claude/launch.json, README.md (the embed contract)
