### M33 U5
milestone: M33
scope: engine
title: The ledger tour
landed: 2026-10-07
decision: D-413
state: built
brief: The tour a stranger who keeps money would follow: Home on a lived-in document; Read a statement, where in demo mode the picker is a list of bundled synthetic files, the only demo-only control in the app; the preview reconciling against the printed total; the uncategorised merchants filed with a rule; a goal made in place (M31). Captions in the maintainer's words, a storyboard approved before it is ported. The statement, the paycheck, the goal and the debt it needs are in the document from U1. Done-test: the tour runs to its last caption under the check; the bundled-file picker exists only in the demo entry and the app's own build is unchanged. 2026-10-07, on the draft (7deb0f6, storyboard docs/mockups/m33-u5/tour-ledger.md): MAKE THE STATEMENT ENGLISH: the bundled statements and every shop name the tour shows are English (synthetic, no real shop; the new shop that gets filed is an English-named studio), so a visitor who reads no Hebrew can follow it; captions' figures follow the new statement. The rest of the draft stood without objection: the question 'Where did this month's money go?' with its line, the five captions, the goal beat dropped, the picker's wording. Finishing U5: port the English statement, re-run check:tours, and close the unit as built; the bills-detector fault it found is M37 F2, and the demo's not-bills marks stay until that lands.
