### M34 U1
milestone: M34
scope: engine
title: The plugin says what it does
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-394
state: built
brief: Strangers reach Emerald through a model, so the tool texts are the onboarding, and the Notion trial (2026-10-05) found them misleading in six places. (1) documentInfo.ts:121 says the plugin 'opens the document read-only' while the same plugin writes. (2) The declare-a-format skill is named at instructions.ts:57, formats.ts:263 and :583, but it lives only in this repo's .claude/ and no stranger has it: describe the conversation inline or ship it with the plugin. (3) vocabulary.ts:83 says of links 'Only an aggregate reads through it', which read as 'cannot be written': say it is written as a list of names. (4) formats.ts:2613 pushed the model to answer nothing_must_hold 19 times without thinking: per D-242 a list-shaped format answers 'nothing adds up' and still gets every refusal, and the question about identities is asked only where figures relate. (5) enum: say what a value may hold (spaces, emoji, case). (6) Routing: the full plugin's instructions and start_here are ledger-first, so non-finance work had nowhere to begin: say where it starts (formats, then read_onto_format), and lead read_onto_format's description with 'any .csv or .xlsx, not only statements'. Decision owed on the dry run for bulk writes: whether one approved plan covers the batches of the same shape that follow (D-099 says a dry run alone is not always enough of a gate). Done-test: the catalog tests assert the new texts, and none of the six phrasings remains.
