brief: The trial's largest cost was rows typed through the chat. read_onto_format reads one file onto one format; give it, and the screen's Read a document, a list of files, each onto its format, read in the order the links need, so a line can link to a row read earlier in the same call. One plan for the whole lot before anything is written, the refusals counted and named per file and line. Declaring several formats in one call, with links between them resolved in order, is included if declare_format cannot already do it. Parity (D-227, D-234): the tool and the screen both. Readers are generic by kind of file, never by product (author, 2026-10-05): .csv, .xlsx and, from U7, .md - no reader names Notion, Obsidian or any other product. Done-test: a synthetic folder of three linked CSVs (fixtures/synthetic) reads in one call with every link filled; a line naming a parent that is not there is refused and named; nothing is written before the plan is accepted.
