### M35 U1
milestone: M35
scope: engine
title: Suggestions and a mockup for the entry page
landed: 2026-10-06
state: built
brief: "STOP for approval, the way M28 and M30 F3 did it. Read the entry page as it is (src/ui/formats/EntryView.tsx, D-294) against what the Notion trial put in a document: long Markdown bodies (notes, page bodies - EntryView already parses Markdown, so check where raw text still shows), thought records with many figures, tasks with links in and out (the trial asked whether backlinks show; check). Write a short list of suggestions, each with what it changes and why, then a mockup in docs/mockups/m35/ carrying two or three directions where the choice is real: field order and grouping, the body as the page rather than a field, what links here, where verdicts sit, editing in place against a form. The design language and the frame are the new screens' (docs/11-ui-design-language.md, D-312). The brief's first line: the entry page needs an improvement or a rework. Record the choices in M35 U2's brief.\n\n2026-10-06: there is both a view when an entry is clicked and its page; there should be only one entry view, editable by the user, the new UI adapted to it, with more options per column type to view; parts of the current page view are liked, but it should combine the other view into one. So: ONE entry view, replacing both what opens when an entry is clicked (the row editor/panel on the format's sheet or board) and the entry page; it is the page view as the base, keeping what works there, with the other view's editing folded in - editable in place, not a separate form. Find every place an entry opens today and name which disappears. And per column type, more ways to show a value (e.g. a number as figure/bar/progress, a date as date/relative, an enum as chip/select, text as line/long body, a link as name/card) - the mockup proposes the set per type and where the choice is made. Directions differ on the real choices, not on whether there is one view."
