### M35 U2
milestone: M35
scope: engine
title: The entry page as approved
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-401
state: built
brief: "Port the approved mockup: its source, its text diffed against the page (no screenshots, model-split memory). Split into more units after U1 if the approved direction is larger than one. Parity unchanged: the entry page's writes are the sheet's and the tools'. Done-test: the page's text matches the mockup's for a note, a row with an identity and a row with links in and out; the parity test and the entry page's tests pass.\n\n2026-10-06, the picks on docs/mockups/m35/entry.html: (1) direction A - the page with a links column (title and header line, figures as a grid with verdicts under them, long texts, links in and out in a right column; opens in place of the list). (2) A field writes when you leave it - no draft and no Save; a new entry is still a draft until Add. (3) Show as is chosen per field (the glyph on hover), not in Arrange. (4) No - a Show as choice does not reach the sheet's cells or the board's cards. (5) moot (B not chosen). Also from U1's findings: one view at entry/:id for every way in; page/:id redirects there; EntryView's 'Its page' and PageView's 'Edit' go; backlinks, figures, verdicts and worked-out columns show on the one view; long text defaults to markdown rather than a one-line field; the development pack's views.md 'page' body/line settings fold into the entry's setting (pack.test.ts flags it). It is to be made efficiently: if this is more than one session's work, split it (e.g. U2 the one view in direction A with save-on-leave, U3 Show as per type) by writing the new planned unit rows first, then build only the first."
