### M35 U3
milestone: M35
scope: engine
title: Show as, per column type
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-402
state: built
brief: Split from M35 U2 (as asked: U2 the one view in direction A with save-on-leave, U3 Show as per type). U2 leaves the one entry view at entry/:id drawing each value one way, with today's inputs (inputsFor) picked from a glyph beside the field's name on hover; Arrange keeps only the order. This unit gives each column type the set of ways the approved mockup proposes (docs/mockups/m35/entry.html, the 'Show as, per column type' table and WAYS in its script), the first being the default and what the sheet's cell already shows: text - Line, Markdown, Mono; integer/real/decimal - Figure, Bar (against the largest), Slider (only when both bounds are declared); percent - Figure, Bar, Ring, Slider (bounded); money - Figure, Large figure; quantity - As written, In one unit (converted), Bar; date - Date, Relative, Both; month - Month, Relative; instant - Date and time, Relative; time - Clock only; enum - Chip, Menu, Buttons, Steps (the members as a path); enums - Chips; boolean - Tick, Yes or No, Buttons; link - Name, Card (its state and line); links - Chips, List, Cards. Worked-out columns take their result type's ways, never editable. Editing follows from the way (a figure, bar or ring opens a field when pressed; a slider drags; a chip or menu opens the menu; buttons and steps are pressed; a link's name opens its row and a small pencil changes which row). Show as replaces the input: Line, Markdown, Slider, Menu, Buttons and Chips keep their words; Field becomes Figure, Search becomes Name; Date and Month are their types' defaults; a stored word no longer offered draws as the default. Kept per format in format_view_column, view entry, as the input is now. The picks: chosen per field (the glyph on hover, a popover headed 'Show <column> as' with 'For every <one>, in this view. Kept beside the declaration.' at its foot), not in Arrange; a Show as choice does NOT reach the sheet's cells or the board's cards. Done-test: view.test.ts covers the set per type and the fallback of an unoffered word; the entry view draws each way for a synthetic format of every type, its text diffed against the mockup's catalog; parity unchanged (setEntryInput is still the write). M35 U4 (a conversation arranges a view) builds on this.
