### M35 U4
milestone: M35
scope: engine
title: A conversation arranges a view
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-403
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-06: 'can a conversation edit a page view? pick how it looks like? if not - is it possible? should be a unit then.' Today it cannot, on purpose: parity.test.ts refuses setEntryInput/setEntryOrder (D-294) and setBoardLanes (D-301) as 'a conversation draws no page'. That reason is wrong now - the person the conversation works for is on the other side, looking at the page ('show the steps as markdown and kcal as a bar'), and a pack made in a conversation (M32) needs its views set the same way. Reverse it with a decision superseding those two gaps: one tool that takes a list of view settings (format, view - entry, board, sheet widths if cheap - column, setting: input, order, Show as from M35's Show-as unit, board lanes), dry-run until commit like every write, and `formats` (or the format's own answer) reports the current arrangement so a model can read before it changes. The settings stay engine view settings, not a declared format: 'a view format' holding them as fmt_ rows was considered and is overkill, and it would break the rule that no built-in table carries the fmt_ prefix. Build after Show as lands, so the tool covers it from the start. Done-test: the parity entries for those writes name the tool instead of a gap; a tool call sets a column's input, order and Show as and the entry view draws it; an unknown column or a Show as the type does not have is refused, naming it.
