brief: Author, 2026-10-05: plan the payslip linking tool. Today only the Deduction types screen (#/paychecks/deductions) sets what a deduction type counts as and pays into - updateDeductionType in the repository; the plugin's funds/paychecks tools only READ the link (the fund deposit check finds payslip lines through deduction_type.linked_holding since M36 U12, D-389), and update_format_rows refuses the ledger's own formats. M36 U12's subagent had to set the link the way the screen does to test a real fund report against real payslips. Against D-227 (anything a screen can do, a conversation can do). Add one tool that takes a LIST of deduction types (by name or id) and sets, per type, what the screen sets: what it pays into (a fund holding, a goal or a payroll loan / debt - whatever 'Pays into' offers since U10/U11, D-387/D-388) and its 'Counts as' answer (out of net, saving - the flags U11 turned into one 'Counts as' column, keeping its 'set by hand' marker). Dry run by default, commit:true writes, whole batch or nothing, refusing a target of the wrong kind by name. Reuse the repository function the screen calls, so src/parity.test.ts derives both halves and its gap entry (if any) goes; regenerate docs/parity.md. Say in the funds tool text and docs/plugin.md that this is how a fund finds its payslip lines. Synthetic tests only; drive the built plugin on a synthetic .emd.
