### M36 U13
milestone: M36
scope: engine
title: Nothing personal in the repository or its history
landed: 2026-10-05
decision: D-390
state: built
brief: 2026-10-05: clean up any reference that could be personal and unfitting for open-source development; the repo is private with no other clones, so it should be easy. Found while driving M36: the U08 mockup carried a figure, account names and card last-4s from a real document (fixed in place by the driver), and names like Everyday Bank have sat in src/ and docs/ since M30 F2. Scope: the working tree AND git history. Look for: real figures and balances, real banks/cards/brokers/fund houses/employers and their last-4s or account numbers, names of real .emd files and paths under the real-documents folder, people's names, Hebrew text lifted from real payslips or statements, anything in fixtures, tests, docs (decision log, archive, packs/ledger notes), mockups, memory.emd rows and commit messages. Replace each with synthetic stand-ins that keep the test meaning (a generic 'Everyday Bank', round figures). Keep a denylist of the real terms OUTSIDE the repo (gitignored, or under the user's home) and add a check (docs:check or a test that reads it when present) so a real name cannot come back quietly. Then the history: list what the rewrite would remove (git filter-repo with a replace-text file built from the denylist), and STOP for the maintainer's yes before rewriting and force-pushing origin main - it is irreversible and outward-facing. No real document enters the repo at any point; the denylist itself never is committed.
