### M37 F2
milestone: M37
scope: ledger
title: The bills detector calls every shop on two statements a monthly bill
landed: 2026-10-14
decision: D-474
state: built
brief: Found 2026-10-07 by M33 U5's session (commit 7deb0f6), building the demo's lived-in ledger document; author asked it into M37 the same day. After a second card statement is read, the fixed-expense (monthly bills) detector offered all 35 shops as monthly bills: it reads each line's single charge date, so a shop that appears once on each of two consecutive statements looks monthly. The demo hides it by marking the shops as not bills in demo.emd; the real ledger still has it. Find where candidates are scored (fixed_expense_candidates, src/domain/ ledger fixed-expense detection) and require real evidence of a recurring bill (e.g. at least three months, a stable amount band, a stable day of month, or whatever the detector's own design note says it needs), with a failing test first built from two synthetic statements where ordinary shops repeat once each. Done-test: two statements with repeating ordinary shops offer no bills; a genuine monthly charge (same amount, same day) across enough months is still offered; the demo document no longer needs the not-bills marks (remove them from make-demo-document.mjs's sources if so).
