brief: Author, 2026-10-14: 'advanced filtering like choosing multiple values under the same thing.' M44 U7's FilterBand holds a column to ONE value: RowQuery.match is a Map<string, StoredValue> (src/data/repositories/formatRowRepository.ts), so state=planned OR in_progress cannot be asked. Make a held column take a set: RowQuery.match's value becomes a list (one value stays the common case), compiled to SQL IN through the one filterQuery/matchCells reading (M44 U6) — no second filter and no client-side re-filtering. Add the two words D-380 already gave a declared filter, so the screen and a declaration say the same things: is not (one of) and is empty. In FilterBand the value step becomes ticks (pick several, the band shows 'state: planned, in progress'), with is / is not and an 'empty' choice; the address carries them (repeat the key, or a comma list — the repo's existing query convention), so reload, back and a bookmark keep it. Parity (D-227): format_rows and format_sheet take a list in match (match:{state:[planned, in_progress]}) and the not/empty forms in the same shape, documented in the tool descriptions; src/parity.test.ts. A list column (enums, M34 U5) holding any of the ticked members matches. Done-test: #/formats/unit?state=planned,in_progress shows exactly format_rows unit match:{state:[planned,in_progress]}, in every view kind; is not and is empty agree the same way; suite, typecheck, build, check:tours, docs:check; verified in the browser.
