### M37 U4
milestone: M37
scope: app
title: A table column's header lists every value it holds, with counts, and filters by them
landed: 2026-10-15
decision: D-477
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-14: 'in table view user should be able to see all unique values under each column and filter by it too.' On the format screen's table (sheet), each column header opens a menu of the values that column holds — each with how many rows hold it, the empty ones counted as '(empty)' — with a search inside the menu and a tick per value; ticking writes U3's multi-value filter into the address, so the header menu and the FilterBand are two doors to one filter and always agree (the band shows what the header ticked, and the reverse). Counts are counted in SQL (GROUP BY over the filtered query the other columns already hold, so a menu shows what is left to narrow), never by listing every row in TypeScript — valueChoices' listRows(limit 5000) in FilterBand.tsx is the thing to replace, and it serves both. An enum lists its members in declared order, zero-count ones dimmed; a link its rows by name; money and quantity columns offer a range (from/to) instead of values; a column of passages (VALUE_LONGEST) offers search only. Sorting by the column sits in the same menu. Hebrew values through Bidi. Conversation half (D-227): a format_rows ask for a column's values with counts (e.g. `values: <column>`, or what format_rollup already answers — check before adding a tool). Done-test: on a synthetic format of 500 rows, a header menu's counts equal format_rows' counts for each value, ticking two narrows exactly as U3's filter does, other held filters narrow the counts; suite, typecheck, build, docs:check; verified in the browser without screenshots.
