### M37 U6
milestone: M37
scope: engine
title: A cell can point at a file on this computer, and opening it opens the file
landed: 2026-10-15
decision: D-479
state: built
brief: 2026-10-14: link files on the computer from a field, for easier access. A new column type, `file` (a path on this machine, not its contents — the document never copies the file in). STOP first with a short write-up for the maintainer's picks, then build: (1) stored relative to the .emd's folder when the file is under it (so a folder that moves keeps its links), absolute otherwise — recommended; (2) filled by picking (the shell's file dialog through bridge.ts), by dropping a file on the cell, or by typing/pasting a path; (3) in the desktop shell a cell shows the file's name and opens it with the system's default app, with 'show in folder' beside it (electron shell.openPath / showItemInFolder, behind bridge.ts — src/ imports nothing else from electron/); in the web build the path is shown and copied, since a page cannot open a local file; (4) a file that is no longer there says so, and is never an error that stops a save. Whether text columns should also turn a path they hold into a link is the second pick (recommend no: one name per thing, the make-it-in-place rule). Also asked by a second project's planner session (2026-10-14): a note app's own address (a custom scheme such as `notes://open?vault=...&file=...`) as well as a path, handed to the system to open in that app — a local app's scheme is not a request, but an http(s) address is, so the column refuses http, https and every scheme that reaches the network (an allowlist of local schemes, not a denylist), or 'no network' stops being true (D-124, D-308). Offline stays: opening a local file is not a request, but check electron/network.test.ts still holds and that no file:// load reaches the page. Privacy: paths name a person's own files — a test fixture uses synthetic paths only (src/privacy.test.ts, D-390). Engine: the type in src/domain/format/ (declaration, ddl as TEXT with a CHECK it is non-empty), the .format.md syntax, a migration if format_column needs it (docs/04-data-model.md), and the conversation half: declare_format / extend_format take it, record_format_rows takes a path, format_rows shows it. Done-test: a format with a file column, a row pointing at a synthetic file beside the .emd, opens it in the shell (verify-in-shell) and survives the folder being moved; a missing file says missing; an https address is refused with the reason; suite, typecheck, build, build:electron, docs:check.
