### M38 U1
milestone: M38
scope: engine
title: The Markdown reader's small faults
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-404
state: built
brief: From the M34 T1 review entries (2026-10-06), bundled because each is small: (1) hidden files - names starting with '.' (the '._' copies a disk leaves) and files with no extension - are skipped and listed as not read, never rows; (2) the title comes from frontmatter's title or the file name, and the body is kept whole - the first # heading is not cut from it (two notes headed 'For 1 serving' clashed); (3) a guessed key can be mapped to nothing (null is refused today, so a model sent a 40-key mapping to drop one); (4) inline #tags in the body can fill an enums column, by the mapping; (5) the spreadsheet reader keeps emoji (it drops them silently); (6) fixed currency for a file applies only to rows with an amount; (7) a quantity in a unit the document does not know is refused naming the ones it does - the trial says 'ug' was accepted, verify first; (8) a dry run shows long text cut short (one 16 KB note was echoed in full). Generic by kind of file, never by product. Done-test: a synthetic folder with a ._ file, a note headed differently from its title, an inline tag and a long note reads with each fixed; the spreadsheet fixture keeps an emoji.
