### M38 U3
milestone: M38
scope: engine
title: Reading the same source again
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-408
state: built
brief: "Both trial verdicts: an import is a one-time copy that drifts from its source within a week. Let a second read of the same files update the rows the first read wrote, by a key - a note's file path, a spreadsheet's declared key column or the row's name where unique - adding what is new and naming (never silently deleting) rows whose source line is gone, with the dry run showing changed / added / gone per file. Decision owed: what the key is per kind of file and where a row remembers its source, and what 'gone' does (named in the report, removed only on request). Parity: the tool and the Read files screen. Done-test: a synthetic folder read twice with one note edited, one added and one removed changes exactly one row, adds one and names one, and writes nothing else.\n\nFound in M38 U1 (2026-10-06), fix first: read_onto_format with commit:true fails on a document stored as text (memory.emd included) - the text form does not keep the record of what was read in. That record is where a row remembers its source, so the text form must carry it before this unit can work; done-test adds a text-stored document read twice."
