title: Creating a document without the ledger, with a pack
landed: 2026-10-06
decision: D-405
state: built
brief: "Author, 2026-10-06: \"There is no option to leave the ledger off and no tool to enable a pack, so every document the MCP creates is a ledger document, and I declared my own formats because the development pack's were not reachable. That is a gap in the Emerald MCP: create_document should take something like ledger: false and packs: [\"development\"], or a separate tool should enable a pack on an existing document.\" Read how a document comes to hold a pack today (D-214, D-282: the ledger is declared formats, identities, links and pack code) and what the app's own new-document and pack screens offer, then give the conversation the same: create_document takes which packs to start with (the ledger no longer implied), and a tool enables a pack on an existing document, dry-run until commit. Both servers (engine-only and full) where each applies. Parity (D-227/D-234): name the screen and the tool for each write, or a gap entry with its reason. Decision owed: the default when packs is omitted (keep the ledger for the full plugin, or nothing) and whether enabling a pack on a document with rows is allowed. Done-test: a plugin test creates a document with packs:[\"development\"] and no ledger, and `formats` lists the development pack's formats and no ledger table; enabling the development pack on an existing empty document does the same; enabling twice is a no-op that says so.\n\nAuthor, 2026-10-06: \"i tried with the ui on a new document to select the dev pack and there is no button for it - why?\" Because M27 U7 left it unbuilt on purpose: src/ui/screens/Packs.tsx says adding the development pack \"is a declaration copy, and its tool half is not\", so under D-234 neither half was built and only the ledger has a button (Keep a ledger here). This unit builds both halves together: a Keep this pack here button on each pack card in #/packs (the development pack's beside the ledger's), and the tool. Generic over PACKS, not a development-only branch: a pack entry in src/data/packs/packs.ts says how it is installed, as the ledger's installLedgerPack does. A document that declares some of a pack's formats: say what installing does to the ones it already holds (complete them if they match, refuse naming the clash if not). Done-test adds: in the browser, a new document's Packs screen shows the button on the development pack, pressing it makes the rail show Roadmap/Boards/Ready."
