decision: D-421
state: built
brief: STOP first: a mockup to be approved, ported in U2 and U3. On the real app, not drawn (M33 U2's first mockup drew the app and was rejected for it): the motions prototyped on the real screens, e.g. behind a dev-only switch or on a mockup page that mounts them, so they are judged on the familiar UI. The four: (1) a row added or removed grows or shrinks into place and the rows below slide; (2) a layout that reshapes (a panel or drawer opening, a column added, a sheet widening) moves its existing pieces to their new places (FLIP, or same-document view transitions where Electron's Chromium has them); (3) a claim whose verdict changes (proved/unchecked to failed especially) is marked once, briefly, never looping; (4) navigating between routes and closing a window or panel: a short crossfade at most, about 150 ms. Durations short (about 150-200 ms), one easing, nothing that counts a figure up or otherwise animates a number (a figure is a fact, D-125's spirit), everything static under prefers-reduced-motion. Measure that a large sheet (hundreds of rows) stays smooth. Done-test: the mockup is in the repo and runnable, it is approved, nothing is ported.
files: src/ui/motion/ (new: motion.ts, flip.ts, flip.test.ts, Flip.tsx, Reveal.tsx, useMark.ts, MotionSwitch.tsx), src/ui/formats/RowSheet.tsx, src/ui/formats/EntryView.tsx, src/ui/screens/FormatRows.tsx, src/App.tsx, src/ui/CommandPalette.tsx, src/ui/commands.ts, src/ui/useAnimatedNumber.ts, src/ui/theme/tokens.css, docs/mockups/m39-u1/motion.md (new), docs/11-ui-design-language.md (pointer only), docs/03-module-and-package-structure.md, docs/09-decision-log.md
