### M41 F2
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: The frame gets its document in every host that draws it, and the model gets a short answer
landed: 2026-10-08
decision: D-446
state: built
brief: 2026-10-08, in VS Code's Copilot Chat (agent mode, auto-routed to another model) after restarting VS Code on the 4e8861f build: 'Use format_sheet to show the milestone format of docs/memory.emd with view roadmap' drew a frame that said 'No document came with this answer, so there is nothing to draw', while an earlier VS Code session on the same machine (after M44 U4) drew the frame whole. Cause to confirm: since M41 U2 (D-432) the document copy rides in the result only when the client advertises io.modelcontextprotocol/ui (src/plugin/server.ts drawsMcpApps), and frame_copy is listed only to such clients; this VS Code chat evidently did not advertise it in the form the check expects (or at all), so the frame drew and had nothing. A gate that fails silently is the wrong design. FIX: (1) log, to stderr (which VS Code shows under Output > MCP: emerald), the client's name, version and the ui extension entry on initialize, so what a host advertises can be seen; (2) make the frame get its document wherever it is drawn, without the copy reaching a model: the expected shape is that the tool result carries no copy at all, and the frame, once drawn, fetches it through the app-only frame_copy (_meta.ui.visibility ['app']) through the host's tools/call; decide whether frame_copy is listed to every client (a host that ignores visibility would then show a model a tool it could call to pull a large base64 blob into its own context: guard it, e.g. it refuses without the frame's token or stamp that only a drawn page has, or answers a model with a refusal), or kept advertising-gated with a fallback, and say why; measure the copy never appears in what Claude Code or the CLI shows the model. (3) THE TEXT ANSWER: format_sheet's and start_here's text sent with a drawn view was format_rows' full answer (14.9 KB for memory.emd's 27 milestones, which Copilot could not read at once and saved to a file) and cut at 25 rows while the frame drew 27. Make it a compact summary of every row the view shows (the row's name and its state or the view's grouping column, no long text, no 25-row cut; a line saying the full rows are one format_rows call away), aiming at 1-2 KB for that case; a client that draws nothing gets the same compact text plus that pointer. (4) If the frame still has no document after its fetch, it says why in a line a person reads (e.g. the host refused the call), not only 'nothing to draw'. Verify on the stand-in in both an advertising and a non-advertising host (teach scripts/try-frame.mjs a flag that omits the ui extension from its initialize), and leave the maintainer one instruction for VS Code. Done-test: in a host that does not advertise the extension, the frame draws the roadmap; the model's text for memory.emd's milestone roadmap is under ~2 KB and names all 27; frame_copy cannot be used by a model to pull the copy; the server logs what each client advertised.
