### M41 F3
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: The frame finds its document without the result's _meta
landed: 2026-10-08
decision: D-447
state: built
brief: 2026-10-08, VS Code Copilot Chat (agent mode, auto-routed model), after reloading the window on 796f016 (M41 F2, D-446): the frame drew and said 'The host handed this view the answer without its _meta, so it does not know which document to draw.' So VS Code passes the tool result to the view WITHOUT its _meta, where F2 put the path and the ticket. The model's text was right (all 27 milestones, ~1 KB). Make the frame independent of the result's _meta: (1) take what to draw (path, format, view) from the tool INPUT the host hands the view (ui/notifications/tool-input), which VS Code passes; fall back to the result's _meta or structuredContent when a host passes those; (2) move the proof that the caller is the drawn frame out of the result and into something a model never sees: the expected shape is a per-server-start key the server writes into the ui:// page it serves (resources/read, which hosts do not put in a model's context), with which the frame signs its frame_copy request for the path from the input (an HMAC over the path, or the key itself if that is enough; say which and why); frame_copy without a valid proof keeps refusing a model with the pointer to format_rows; (3) if a host caches the page across a server restart the key is stale: the frame says so in a line a person reads and asks to be shown again, and say whether hosts cache it; (4) keep the frame's step-by-step failure lines (they found this). Also measure and say what VS Code passes to a view (tool-input yes or no, result content, structuredContent, _meta), using the stand-in's message log to model it: teach scripts/try-frame.mjs a flag that strips the result's _meta before handing it to the frame (as VS Code does) and verify the roadmap draws with it. Done-test: on the stand-in with the result's _meta stripped and the ui extension not advertised, memory.emd's milestone roadmap draws; a model calling frame_copy (no proof) is refused; the built server is current for the maintainer to try in VS Code.
