### M41 F5
milestone: M41
scope: engine
title: In VS Code the frame paints the chat panel's colour, since a transparent frame shows the window's
state: dropped
brief: DROPPED, 2026-10-08, before any code was written: Emerald stays general. The frame follows the MCP Apps style variables and a transparent page (D-445, D-448) in every host and carries no host-specific code (the same spirit as 'generic readers only'). In VS Code's Copilot Chat the frame shows slightly darker than the chat because VS Code hands --color-background-primary = var(--vscode-editor-background) (#121314 in the dark theme in use) and floats the view over the workbench, so a transparent page reveals the window's #121314, while the chat pane paints --vscode-sideBar-background #191a1b (measured in Webview Developer Tools: chat pane rgb(25,26,27); inside the frame nothing large paints). That is VS Code's to fix; the maintainer files an issue with VS Code. The considered workaround (paint --vscode-sideBar-background when --vscode-* variables are present) was rejected as the first host-specific code.
