report: Agenda done: readAgendaDone took any member called done, date or line as a stray keyword, so no spelling naming the member done was a setting. Now only the first word is the keyword and commas read as spaces: `done done`, `done done dropped`, `done dropped, done` and `done done, dropped` all mark the members, and arrange_views stores `done done dropped`. `done DONE, DROPPED` is refused as "`state` has no DONE, DROPPED; its members are open, in_progress, done, dropped." The view words say "an agenda" / "an entry". Entry order: did NOT reproduce. Synthetic formats (title declared tenth, sent first; SQLite and text storage; one commit with show_as, board lanes, agenda date, order and header; then extend_format adding two links, a link and a constraint) keep the order exactly, with new columns appended and the declaration only growing at the end. setEntryOrder, the text views part and extend_format's adopt path all keep places by column name. views.test.ts pins both cases. A review entry asks the maintainer for the exact calls. Full suite: 4776 pass; privacy.test.ts and hostBoundary.test.ts timed out under full-suite load and pass alone.

### M42 F12
milestone: M52
scope: app
title: Deleting an entry from a filtered table returns to the table as it was filtered
landed: 2026-10-20
state: built
brief: Maintainer, 2026-10-20: in the app, open a format's table, filter it, open an entry, delete it. The app goes back to the table, but the filter is gone and every row shows. Expected: back on the same table, with the same filter (and search, sort, scroll if the table keeps them), minus the deleted row. Find where the entry page's delete navigates (the formats UI under src/ui/formats/) and whether the table's filter lives in the route, the store or component state. The fix is likely to send the person back to where they came from (history back, or the table's own URL with its query) rather than to the bare table route. Check that leaving an entry without deleting already keeps the filter. If it doesn't, the same fix covers both. Add a test in the repo's style, plus a browser check: filter, open, delete, still filtered. App-only; reaches people with the next release.
files: src/ui/screens/FormatRows.tsx (the missing-row redirect and back), src/ui/nav.ts (tablePath), src/ui/nav.test.ts
taken_by: claude-code unruffled-kare-752ad2
started: 2026-10-20
branch: claude/unruffled-kare-752ad2
commit: 8880d64
report: Cause: React Router 7.18's HashRouter moves the location inside startTransition, while the document store's delete renders urgently. That first render is still on the deleted entry's address, finds no row, and the MISSING branch's <Navigate> went to formatPath(name), so the filter was dropped. Fix: the missing-row redirect and the back button both go to tablePath(name, address), which keeps the filter and search the entry was opened with (a stale bookmark keeps its filter too). Leaving without deleting already kept the filter. Browser check on a copy of memory.emd, held in memory only: open_question filtered to state=open with search 'the' (22 of 51), open an entry, delete it, and you're back on the same address at 21 of 50 with both chips. Scroll is kept. Not fixed: sort. It is FormatRows' component state, and the screen remounts between the table and an entry route, so a plain Back loses it too, as does the entry pager's order. That's a separate gap, proposed as a follow-up. Typecheck is clean, all 4777 tests pass, docs:check shows 0 errors.

