### M42 F14
milestone: M52
scope: app
title: A format's table keeps its sort when an entry is opened, and the entry's pager walks the rows in that sort
landed: 2026-10-20
state: built
brief: A format's table loses its sort after the person opens an entry, even with a plain Back, and the entry page's pager ignores the table's sort. M42 F12 (8880d64) made filter and search survive by keeping them in the address and routing Back, delete and a missing row through tablePath(name, address) in src/ui/nav.ts, used by src/ui/screens/FormatRows.tsx. The sort is kept only in the screen's own state, so it resets when the screen remounts between the table and an entry route. Keep the sort where filter and search already live, so tablePath carries it: Back, delete and a missing row then keep it, and so do a reload and a bookmark. Make the entry pager step through rows in the table's sort, as the person sees them. Tests in the repo's style (nav.test.ts, addressFilter.test.ts, entryList.test.ts); a browser check on an in-memory copy, never saving: sort, open, Back still sorted, the pager follows the sort.
