report: The sort now rides in the address beside filter and search: ?order:<column>=descending|ascending (the colon keeps it from colliding with a column, as columns: does). useAddressFilter reads it and gives setOrder, which replaces the history entry the way typing a search does, and every other change keeps it, so clearing a filter keeps the sort. FormatRows uses it in place of its own state, so tablePath carries it: Back, delete, a missing row, a reload and a bookmark all keep it. The entry list, which is what the pager walks, reads the same order. sortOf falls back to the default order when the address names a column the format doesn't have, stored or computed. The entry list's search and the 'opened from outside the search' redirect keep the order too. Saving a changed shape still drops the sort, as before. Browser check on an in-memory copy of memory.emd, never saved: open_question sorted by question, descending, writes ?order:question=descending. Opening the first row shows 1 of 51, Next shows 2 of 51 on the table's second row, the list beside it is in the same order, and '<- Open question' comes back on the same address with question shown sorted down. A stale ?order:gone falls back to ref ascending. Typecheck, all 4783 tests and docs:check (0 errors) pass. check:tours could not run, because the worktree has no node_modules of its own (fontsource package.json ENOENT), so it was not run. Briefed as M42 F13, but that ref was already the Node-range unit in the main document, so it landed as F14.

