decision: D-513
state: built
brief: On 2026-10-20 a model at the maintainer's work, asked to use Emerald for a development team's planning, refused until argued out of it, then corrected two more objections by reading the pack. Each objection was answerable from the server's text: git and an issue tracker already cover planning (plans drift in PLAN.md files and notes nobody owns); the pack means ~20 per-repo docs (one document holds milestones that cross repos); a .emd is binary and can't be committed (store_document_as text diffs in git); a gitignored file is in no worktree or cloud session (a committed text file is in every checkout, readable without Emerald); two documents can't talk (inboxes, and an elsewhere column showing the other row's state live, e.g. `unit S1 U5 · built`, not enforced); claims only see their own copy (a worktree session proposes its landing to the main document's inbox at an absolute path and the driver lands it; one document outside every repo is one copy, writes under a lock). instructions.ts says it right after the 2,000-char head in both modes, every claim checked against the code; ask-cold.mjs asks 'should my team's development planning live in Emerald?', run before and after; server.test.ts fails on wording that brings the refusal back. Ships in emerald-mcp 0.1.6.
