brief: Maintainer, 2026-10-19: a model at work, given emerald, told them 'Emerald is built for money first. Its tools describe everything outside finances as an add-on' and argued against moving their Obsidian notes, saying Obsidian needs the files. Our text caused it: `formats` says 'besides its finances'; the full server opens on the ledger as 'a complete personal-finance application that a new document keeps unless told otherwise'; 'Not everything here is money', 'they know nothing about money' and start_here's 'where work that is not money begins' are all defensive; the Markdown-folder reader (M34 U7) is mentioned only past the 2,000 characters a host may keep. Fix: (1) both instruction blocks open on what Emerald is for any kind of thing, what it reads (csv, xlsx, json, a folder of Markdown notes read in place, files unchanged), and packs as optional, ledger one of them; (2) every engine tool description says what it does without measuring against finance; (3) create_document keeps no pack unless `packs` names one, in both modes; (4) a sweep for other wrong or stale claims in the model-facing text (an audit agent's findings), each fixed; (5) a test that the money-first phrases are gone in both modes and the head names the notes folder. Done-test: server tests and typecheck green; docs:check green.
