paths: scripts/ask-cold.mjs, docs/plugin.md, docs/conventions.md, .claude/skills/closing-pass/SKILL.md
report: "Built scripts/ask-cold.mjs: each question a fresh `claude -p` in an empty temp folder, --strict-mcp-config naming only dist-plugin/server.mjs (engine-only and full), --setting-sources project, --tools \"\" (no built-ins), allowed mcp__emerald; stream-json parsed for the servers, the tools offered, the tools called and the answer; a run that sees another MCP server or a built-in tool, or begins without the server, fails. Trap found: the desktop app sets MCP_CONNECTION_NONBLOCKING=true, and -p then begins before the server connects - 3-4 of 10 runs answered 'which Emerald?'. The script drops CLAUDE*/MCP_* vars and sets it false; 10/10 connected after. Run on 2026-10-19 against 0.1.5's build, $0.74, Opus 4.8 default.\n\nWhat a cold model says now: no money-first framing in either mode. Both modes lead with asking for rows instead of re-reading forty files, typed fields that filter exactly, links followed, the same rows every session, and a Markdown folder read in place; packs named as optional; start_here (create_document for a new file) as the first call; 'no numbers' answered 'yes - numbers are one feature, not the point'. Still off: (1) engine-only 'best at' lists personal finance as one of three headline uses, ends offering 'a project or your finances', and its summary says 'prove the numbers add up' - checks creep back into the one-line summary. (2) The Obsidian answers, both modes, say keep daily notes and MEETINGS in Obsidian as prose, and engine-only ends 'if you mostly read and link notes, Emerald buys you little' - neither names the model-side gain (every session asks instead of re-grepping the vault), the decisive argument in D-507. (3) Full mode's CSV run called frame_copy, a frame's tool, as if it were the model's. Mechanical flags are noisy on correct answers (numbers-as-reason fires on 'a list needs no numbers'); judgment needed, as designed. Answers: side-session notes folder, ask-cold-2026-10-19.md."

