brief: The repository's package.json is the app's and is private; the MCP server needs a package of its own: a manifest generated or kept for dist-plugin/ (name, version, bin so `npx <name>` starts it, files, licence AGPL-3.0-only per D-430, repository pointing at the public repo, engines), carrying the wasm it needs, with no dependency it does not use at runtime. Decide and say: one package with both servers (full and engine-only, chosen by a flag) or two. STOP for the maintainer: publishing itself is the maintainer's act on the project's npm account; the session prepares `npm pack` output and a dry run, and the maintainer runs `npm publish --access public`. Waits on the public repository (M33 U4's deploy), since AGPL source should be public before the package is. Done-test: `npm pack` produces a package that, installed in an empty folder, starts the server with npx and answers start_here on a synthetic document; the maintainer has published it. || 2026-10-16 (D-481): the npm name is decided, `emerald-mcp`; the README's install line already says `claude mcp add emerald -- npx emerald-mcp`. The repository stays `emerald-emd`. || Maintainer, 2026-10-18: npm goes first, and the Claude plugin (M42 U4) runs everything from this package, never a committed build or a release asset. So the package also serves the plugin: (1) its MCP server entry will be `npx -y emerald-mcp@<version> --engine-only`, pinned; (2) the hooks the plugin ships (hosts/claude/hooks/hooks.json today calls `node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks.mjs start-here "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"` and `... hooks.mjs rows "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" inbox --match state=new --once-per-session`) and the status line (status-line.mjs, from the claude-status-line build mode) must be reachable from the package too: a bin each, or one bin with subcommands, so a plugin's hooks.json can call them through npx; mind that the inbox hook runs on every prompt, so say what an npx call costs there once cached; (3) engines: Node 24 is what CI uses. Say the choice in docs/plugin.md; hooks.json itself changes in M42 U4, not here. A bundled-for-the-plugin attempt (scripts/build-claude-plugin.mjs, and why sql.js needed its browser build when everything was bundled) is on the local branch m42-u4-wip for reference; it is not to be merged.
