commit: 1ef4e5f
paths: "electron/\nPRIVACY.md\nREADME.md\nsrc/demo/page/copy/en.ts"
report: "M42 U8 built on main in 1ef4e5f; D-502 amends D-124 (and D-452's one-address rule: Download is a second fixed address).\n\nWhat it is: one setting, off by default, in About (Updates section: the rule in one paragraph, a checkbox 'Check at start and once a day', a Check now button). Help > Check for Updates Now on all platforms, plus a palette row (menu parity). The answer is always the notice region's lowest row: 'Emerald 0.2.0 is out. You have 0.1.2.' [Download] [Later]; 'You have the latest — Emerald 0.1.2.' [Dismiss]; 'Could not check for updates. <reason>' [Dismiss]; 'Checking for a newer version of Emerald…'. No dialog; focus is not taken (checked). Download opens <repo>/releases/latest in the browser and hides the notice; nothing is downloaded on either platform. Windows and macOS share one code path until U9.\n\nNetwork: the check runs in an in-memory session 'emerald-updates' that the page never runs in; isAllowedUpdateRequest allows exactly the releases/latest URL and only while a check is in flight (narrower than the brief's 'while the setting is on'). The page's isAllowedRequest is untouched and refuses the address.\n\nVerified in the shell (verify-in-shell, CDP + Chromium --log-net-log): (1) fresh profile, setting off: About shows the section unchecked; the palette has 'Check for updates now'; the net log holds no HTTP request at all. (2) EMERALD_UPDATE_ANSWER stub (unpackaged only) v0.2.0: Check now from the palette shows the notice with Download/Later, no dialog, focus untouched; Later hides it; turning the setting on checks at once and writes settings.json. (3) real GitHub, setting on: start check silent (v0.1.0 < 0.1.2), Check now says 'You have the latest — Emerald 0.1.2.'; the net log shows only api.github.com/repos/kfireliyahu/emerald-emd/releases/latest, headers user-agent Emerald/0.1.2 and accept-language en (pinned after the first run showed en-US); the page's own fetch to the same URL is refused.\n\nTests: updates.test.ts (15: versions, setting file, ten days off asks nothing, daily schedule, Later, silent failure, check-now with setting off, single flight), network.test.ts (gate closed/open, every other host refused, page predicate refuses it, openExternal list now includes RELEASES_PAGE), menu.test.ts, menuParity.test.ts. Full suite 4740 green; typecheck clean.\n\nNot done / follow-ups: (a) every run, setting on or off, Chromium resolves 'wpad' on the local network because Windows' proxy auto-detect is on — a local DNS lookup, no HTTP, predating this unit; suppressing it (e.g. --no-proxy-server) would break the check behind a proxy, so left for a decision. (b) The macOS path was exercised only as code (same path as Windows); no Mac run. (c) U9 must change the About wording on Windows and widen isAllowedUpdateRequest to the download hosts named in D-502. (d) The native macOS About panel's credits do not mention updates; the page's About does."

