milestone: M42
scope: engine
title: On Windows, an update downloads quietly and installs when you press Install and restart, if updates are on
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-503
state: built
brief: Maintainer, 2026-10-18: with M42 U8's setting on, Windows downloads updates by itself and installs one only when the person presses Install and restart; macOS stays a notice until the installers are signed (Electron's updater needs a signed app on macOS). (1) electron-updater (electron-builder's own) for the NSIS target: electron-builder.yml gets a GitHub publish entry so it writes latest.yml (version, file, sha512) and the blockmap beside the installer; .github/workflows/release.yml uploads both to the release with the installers and adds them to SHA256SUMS and the attestations (the build still runs with --publish never; the release job uploads). (2) The app, with the setting on: checks through M42 U8's check (one check, not two), downloads the newer installer in the background, verifies it against latest.yml's sha512 (the updater does; say what it does without a code signature: verifyUpdateCodeSignature cannot verify an unsigned publisher, so the checksum from the maintainer's own release is the guarantee, and the GitHub account is the real guard), and installs only when the person presses Install and restart in M42 U8's quiet notice (autoInstallOnAppQuit off; quitAndInstall on the press), the installer per-user and silent, the app reopening on the document that was open. Downloads only from the hosts M42 U8's network exception allows, never with the setting off. A document is never touched by an update; say so in the notice's help text if there is one. (3) Users on 0.1.x without the updater download once by hand; the README says from which version updates are automatic. Done-test: tests for the updater's wiring with a stubbed feed (newer, same, older, bad checksum refused); the release workflow's rehearsal (workflow_dispatch) shows latest.yml and the blockmap among the artifacts; then the maintainer's act (STOP): tag a release with the updater, install it, turn updates on, tag the next one, and the first shows the notice, and Install and restart updates it. A review_entry holds those steps. || Maintainer, 2026-10-18: never intrusive, even when on — like the Claude desktop app: no modal, no dialog that steals focus, nothing installed unasked. A newer version shows as a quiet notice inside the window (a small banner or a button in the title bar or rail, the session’s call in the app’s design language) that stays until dismissed or acted on; on Windows, once downloaded, it reads <version> is ready with Install and restart and Later; on macOS, <version> is out with Download. Later hides it until the next start or the next day’s check. Check for updates now answers in the same notice, not a dialog. || Maintainer, 2026-10-18: getemerald.dev must always point at the newest installers. Today M42 F2 links v0.1.0 files by name (RELEASE in src/demo/page/page.ts) because the names carry the version. Make the installer names version-free in electron-builder.yml (artifactName, e.g. Emerald-Setup.exe, Emerald-arm64.dmg, Emerald-x64.dmg; latest.yml names whatever the file is, so the updater does not care), have the page link https://github.com/kfireliyahu/emerald-emd/releases/latest/download/<name>, drop RELEASE, and change the rail.test.ts guard to match the new names; SHA256SUMS and the attestations follow the names. Users who already downloaded keep their file; the README and the release notes change with it.
