### M43 U11
milestone: M43
scope: engine
title: A model finds the frame: format_sheet becomes show_format, and the line that says when to show sits where every host keeps it
landed: 2026-10-17
decision: D-482
state: built
brief: "Why: 2026-10-09 a Claude Code session in the desktop Code tab, asked to \"show me the roadmap\", gave a hand-written list and had to be asked \"why not the frame?\". Two causes, both measured that day. (1) The host cuts a server's instructions: the engine-only block is 9,376 chars, the Code tab kept the first 2,038 and then \"… [truncated]\", and \"Show when they ask to see\" starts at char 4,324, so it never reaches the model. (2) Claude Code defers MCP tools: until a session runs a tool search it sees only the tool's name, not its description, and \"format_sheet\" says nothing about showing (also \"Sheet\" is the word D-451 retired on screen for \"Table\", and a roadmap or board is not a sheet).\n\nDo: (a) Rename the tool format_sheet → show_format everywhere: the definition, catalog, server, the frame's host.ts/main.tsx (it matches the tool name on tool-input/result), try-frame.mjs, tests, docs/plugin.md and every doc that names it, and the term rows whose code_word says format_sheet (Table, Frame). No alias: nothing public has called it yet (D-092: names are an API from the first stranger's conversation, which has not happened). The view input takes `table` for the table view, the term D-451 chose; if arrange_views takes `view: sheet` too, give it the same word in this unit; storage is unchanged. The name was picked 2026-10-09. (b) Reorder BOTH instruction blocks (engine-only and full) so that, within the first 2,000 chars, a model learns what Emerald is and the show line: when a person asks to see something (the roadmap, the board, what is ready, a format's rows) call show_format or start_here, which draw it in the conversation; format_rows is for rows the model will reason over. Cut or move down what can wait (the disambiguation paragraph can be one line). (c) A test pins it: both blocks name show_format and start_here as the way to show within the first 2,000 chars, with a comment that cites the measured 2,038-char cut. (d) Write the decision row and log entry (the rename, and that the instructions' head is a budget). Not this unit: whether start_here should be renamed (it reads fine); frame_copy (not for a model). After it lands, the session's own memory note show-with-the-frame names the new tool.\n\nVerify: npm run build:plugin, then re-run the probe (spawn dist-plugin/server.mjs --engine-only, initialize, indexOf the show line < 2,000 in instructions); npm run frame:try still draws; the suite and docs:check pass. Whether a fresh Code-tab session draws the roadmap unprompted from \"show me the roadmap\" is a try only the maintainer can do after restarting the emerald server: the one line to ask for."
