brief: Gather the vocabulary, change nothing yet. Every name a stranger meets on a screen or through a tool: the rail and its groups, page titles and headings, buttons and menu items, empty states, verdict words (proved, failed, unchecked), the band names (Computed, Claims, D-417), view kind names, the tours' titles and captions, the MCP tool names and the words of their descriptions and the server's instructions, and the file-facing words (document, format, pack, entry, row, link). One row per term: the term as shown, where it appears (route or file, how many places), what it means in a line, and the decision that named it if there is one (search decision rows; do not read the log end to end). Flag the likely problems: two words for one thing, one word for two things (e.g. claim vs taken), internal words that leak onto a screen (identity, fmt_, D-numbers), and words a newcomer cannot read. If M40 U3's `term` format exists by then, the terms are its rows; otherwise a declared format of the same shape in docs/memory.emd, so the maintainer can review and mark them in the app (a `rename_to` and a `keep` per row), not in a long markdown file. STOP: the list is the maintainer's to mark. Done-test: the terms are rows the maintainer can open in Emerald, grouped by where they appear, with the flagged ones marked; nothing in the app has changed yet. From M40 U3 (c443089, D-436), 2026-10-08: the `term` format exists (140 rows; columns term, means, not, rejected, code_word, printed_as, named_by, scope, state); add `rename_to` (text) and `keep` (boolean) with extend_format, no row touched. U3 renamed two TERM ROWS where one word did two jobs, WITHOUT changing the app: the statement column 'Balance' is now 'Running balance' and the debts figure 'Monthly obligation' is now 'Monthly debt obligation', so the rows and the screens disagree on those two until the maintainer rules (U3 of this milestone applies). Also D-348 and D-369 still say 'budget', which D-375 rejected for 'bucket'; check whether any screen still says budget.
