### M44 U2
milestone: M44
scope: engine
title: The server pushes a change to whoever subscribed
landed: 2026-10-08
decision: D-440
state: built
brief: 2026-10-08: live updates are a listener, not a poll, and a general MCP capability rather than a frame trick (moved here from M41 U2 when hand-offs and listeners became a milestone of their own). The server declares resources.subscribe; a document is a resource addressed by its path; on resources/subscribe the server watches the document's DIRECTORY (a save is a rename, so a per-file watch goes deaf on the first save, D-127) and sends notifications/resources/updated for that document's URI to every subscriber when it changes, debounced, and stops watching on the last resources/unsubscribe or when the client goes. Any MCP client that supports subscriptions gets it, which also lets a session learn that another writer touched the document (the concurrent-writers case). Keep the watching code where M44 U3 (one format, and the watch command) and M44 U4 (the drawn view) reuse it. Measure and say whether Claude Code subscribes to resources or ignores them. A decision row records that the server now holds state for as long as it runs (who is subscribed to which document), which amends 'every tool opens one file, does one job and closes it, and nothing is remembered between calls': tools stay stateless; only subscriptions are held, and they hold nothing of the document. Done-test: a client subscribed over stdio receives resources/updated within a second of another process saving the document, a rename-save included, and nothing after unsubscribing; the server's tests cover subscribe, the rename-save and unsubscribe; docs/plugin.md says how to subscribe.
files: src/plugin/watch.ts (new: watchDocument, the shared directory watch U3/U4 reuse), src/plugin/subscriptions.ts (new: resources/subscribe and unsubscribe, file:// URI), src/plugin/subscriptions.test.ts (new: in-memory and stdio under vite-node), src/plugin/server.ts (resources.subscribe, addSubscriptions), docs/plugin.md, docs/09-decision-log.md
taken_by: run-milestone driver
started: 2026-10-08

### M44 U3
milestone: M44
scope: engine
title: Told when the inbox gets something: a subscription to one format, and a watch that wakes a session
landed: 2026-10-08
decision: D-441
state: built
brief: 2026-10-08: the subscriptions M41 U2 adds (a document as a resource, resources/updated pushed on change) should serve agents and the inbox too, not only the drawn view. Two gaps U2 leaves: (1) it is document-wide, so 'memory.emd changed' fires on every write, a driver's own included; (2) a model in a Claude session does not wait on MCP notifications, so nothing wakes it. Build both. (1) A subscription to one format of a document (a resource per format, e.g. the document's URI plus the format's name; the session names it with the one-name rule): the server compares that format's rows before and after a change and notifies only when they differ, so a subscriber to the inbox hears a new inbox row and nothing else. (2) A small command, `emerald watch <document> [--format <name>] [--match key=value]`, shipped with the server, that subscribes and prints one line per change (what changed, in a line a model reads: e.g. 'inbox: 1 new row from D:/projects/other/other.emd: <subject>'), so a session runs it under its Monitor tool and is woken on each line; no polling, and it exits cleanly when the document goes away. The engine's rules hold: the watch reads, never writes, and makes no network request. Say in docs/plugin.md how a session watches its inbox, and add one line to the inbox format's notes. Done-test: with a session in this project running `emerald watch docs/memory.emd --format inbox --match state=new` under Monitor, a second project's session (or a script standing in for it) writes an inbox row and the session is woken with the row's subject within a few seconds; a write to any other format wakes nothing; the server's tests cover the per-format comparison.
