### M44 U6
milestone: M44
scope: plugin
title: The frame draws only the rows asked for: format_sheet takes match and search
landed: 2026-10-09
state: built
brief: 2026-10-09: asked to show the finding rows with action:maintainer, the driver answered with a markdown table, because format_sheet cannot filter; it would have drawn all 75 finding rows. The rule is that 'show me' is answered with the frame. Give format_sheet the same `match` and `search` that format_rows takes (same semantics, same code path, no second filter implementation) and pass them to the frame, so the drawn view and its text answer show exactly the rows asked for; the view says it is filtered and by what. It works on every view kind (table, board, roadmap, ready), and the in-place update (M44 U4) keeps the filter when the file changes. The tool count does not change. Done-test: format_sheet finding match:{action:maintainer, state:open} draws only those rows in a host that draws MCP Apps, and its text answer names only them; the tool-surface tests and docs/plugin.md are updated; the full suite, typecheck, build:plugin and docs:check pass.
