### M45 F3
milestone: M45
scope: engine
title: Safety copies clean up after themselves: a gone document's folder goes after 30 days, the uninstaller takes the folder, and About shows it
landed: 2026-10-09
decision: D-457
state: built
brief: Author, 2026-10-09: asked whether safety copies pile up on people's computers; ruled '30 days is fine'. Today (D-455, M45 U4/F2) each document's folder under backupsRoot() keeps its last five copies, but nothing removes a folder: a renamed, moved or deleted document leaves its folder and five copies forever, and the uninstaller leaves %LOCALAPPDATA%\Emerald. Fix, as one decision row amending D-455: (1) Each per-document folder records its document's absolute path in a small file inside it, written when the folder is made (and written on the next copy into a folder that has none, which covers the folders already there). (2) Whenever a copy is taken (plugin and shell, one shared function in electron/bridge.ts beside claimRollingCopy), sweep the sibling folders: remove one whose recorded document no longer exists at that path AND whose newest copy is more than 30 days old. Never remove a folder with no recorded path unless its newest copy is over 30 days old and nothing exists at the path its name suggests; never touch anything outside backupsRoot(); never follow a symlink out of it; a sweep that fails is ignored with nothing lost (it is housekeeping, and it must never fail the write it rides on). The 30 days is one named constant. (3) The Windows uninstaller removes %LOCALAPPDATA%\Emerald\Backups (electron-builder's NSIS include, customUnInstall); macOS has no uninstaller, so say so in the decision. (4) Help > About shows the backups folder's path and total size with 'Open folder' (through the bridge; shell only, the static site shows nothing). keep_copy's named copies beside the document are out of scope (already capped). Tests run with EMERALD_BACKUPS_DIR at a temp dir and a fake clock: a gone document's folder at 29 days stays, at 31 goes; a live document's folder is never swept; a folder with an unreadable record is left alone. Done-test: those tests; the shell's About shows the folder and size (verify-in-shell); typecheck, the full suite, build, build:plugin, build:electron and docs:check pass; dist:win builds and its uninstaller script contains the removal (inspect the generated NSIS, do not run an install).
files: electron/bridge.ts (sweepBackupFolders, recordBackupFolder, measureBackupsFolder, ORPHANED_COPIES_DAYS, AboutFacts/EmeraldApp/APP_CHANNELS), src/plugin/backup.ts, src/plugin/write.ts, electron/documents.ts (restoreEarlierCopy sweeps, measureEarlierCopies), electron/main.ts, electron/preload.ts, electron/menu.ts, electron/about.ts, build/installer.nsh, src/ui/About.tsx, src/ui/useShellCommands.ts, src/ui/commands.ts, src/App.tsx, src/data/storage/desktop.ts, docs/plugin.md, tests: src/plugin/backup.test.ts, electron/bridge.test.ts, electron/documents.test.ts, electron/installer.test.ts
