brief: Evidence: one session in a second project (2026-10-11) made 13 empty inbox polls and 14 Monitor calls at 360K context each, about 10M tokens for nothing, and still missed the row twice. The watch command (M44 U3) existed and was never running: on 2026-10-08 nine servers were up and none was a watcher. An inbox row of 2026-10-09 ('Three inbox conventions') says a watcher must start as part of session start or the inbox reaches only sessions that have not begun. Build: a Claude Code hook set the plugin ships and this repo can use today from .claude/settings.json: SessionStart runs start_here on the document the project names (a `document` field in .claude/emerald.json, or the one .emd in the folder when there is exactly one) and prints it; UserPromptSubmit prints inbox rows in state new, when there are any, and nothing otherwise. Both go through new server subcommands beside `watch` (`server.mjs start-here <doc>`, `server.mjs rows <doc> inbox --match state=new`), so a hook costs a process, not an MCP round trip and not a turn. The plugin folder M42 U4 plans carries the same hooks. Done-test: a fresh session in a second project opens with its document's start_here in context and no poll; a row written there from another project's session appears at the next prompt; this repo's docs:check keeps the hook lines in settings.json. The convention row in this document's inbox (state new, from a second project) is applied by this unit.
