### M47 U2
milestone: M47
scope: engine
title: start_here says what a row looks like: the first call carries the columns
landed: 2026-10-13
decision: D-460
state: built
brief: Evidence: in every session on notes.emd, planner.emd and site.emd the first call was not enough. start_here answered what is open, and the session then called formats once per format it was about to write, 48 times over the week, up to 8 in one session and 5 in a row, 3 to 6 KB each, before it could record a unit. The columns belong to the document, so nothing else can know them. 2026-10-13: the count is not the point, some call is always made, and the solution lives in the document rather than in a file beside it. Build: start_here appends, after its views, the compact declaration of every format the document holds, in the shape CLAUDE.md's hand-written table uses: the format's name, its columns with their types, required ones in bold, enum members, what a link points at, computed columns marked, and the one line that writes dry-run until commit. About a KB for six formats; formats stays for the full declaration with its prose, notes and units. The section is generated from the declarations, so it is the document's and never stale, and a document that declares nothing but a pack prints the pack's. Done-test: a fresh session on planner.emd records a unit after start_here alone, checked in its transcript; this repo's CLAUDE.md table can go, since the document answers it (docs:check stops expecting it). Rejected: a generated CLAUDE.md section per document (a file beside the document, rejected), and columns in the tool descriptions (they belong to the build, not the document).
