### M47 U4
milestone: M47
scope: engine
title: A link to a row in another document
landed: 2026-10-13
decision: D-461
state: built
brief: Evidence: every cross-document reference in the three documents is prose ('planner.emd D-27', 'notes.emd D-23', 'Emerald D-418'); an inbox row's `from` is a path string and `became_unit` cannot point outside its file; on 2026-10-13 site.emd's hand-off had to say 'M1 U10 can be marked built' because the convention let no session mark another document's row, and notes.emd's M1 U10 sat in_progress a day. Build: a link column may name another document: the value is the document's path plus the row's ref (by the column the row is called by, never an id: a text document renews ids, and the open question 'Stable ids' stays open). The engine resolves it when the other file is readable and shows it unresolved, not failed, when it is not; the sheet draws it as a link that opens the other document; format_rows prints the linked row's name and state beside it, and start_here lists inbox rows with what the row they are about holds now. The development pack's inbox gains `about`, such a link, so a hand-off names the row it concerns. Needs a decision when built: D-241 says a text document writes a link as the name of the row it points at; across documents it is path plus ref. Done-test: planner.emd's inbox row about the privacy policy links site.emd S1 U5, and start_here on planner.emd shows S1 U5 built; a link to a document that is not there reads unresolved and the batch is not refused.
