### M48 U1
milestone: M48
scope: engine
title: Four engine faults: multi-word members in a filter, a batch judged by where it ends, an enum change's two messages, a link found within its fixed parent
landed: 2026-10-14
decision: D-467
state: built
brief: From a second project's planner session (its feedback items 1-4), 2026-10-14; each with a failing test first. (1) parseFilter's FILTER_PATTERN (src/domain/format/aggregate.ts:319) takes \S+ per member, so `status is one of Planned, In progress` is refused as 'not a filter' though `In progress` is a legal enum member; the session renamed its members to one word to get past it. Accept members with spaces — split `one of` on commas, and accept a quoted member ("In progress") for a lone `is` — and when a filter is still refused, say what part could not be read. Same spelling in every place the one parser serves (an artefact's over, a rollup, a rule set, a tool's where). (2) A one-row-per ... when ... constraint is judged against the rows before the batch, so moving `Current` from one semester to another in one update_format_rows call is refused and needed two. Judge uniqueness against the batch's end state (apply in one transaction and let SQLite's partial unique index decide at the end, or order the batch's writes so clears land before sets) — the whole batch still applies or none of it does. (3) extend_format change on an enum said 'No longer held to: grade is required when status is Graded', and re-adding that constraint then failed 'declared twice': one message is false. Find which (the constraint kept and the diff misreporting it, or dropped and a stale row left behind) and make the diff and the store agree. (4) Filling a link from a note's body links (unit.concepts → concept) required concept.name unique across the document, though the read had `fixed: {course: ...}` and concept declares one row per course, name. Resolve a name within the fixed parent when a uniqueness constraint makes it unique there (M38 U5's name-plus-one-column, applied from the fixed value), and refuse only when it is still ambiguous, naming the rows. Done-test: each of the four has a test that failed on main; suite, typecheck, build:plugin, docs:check.
