### M49 U1
milestone: M49
scope: engine
title: Date arithmetic: a date plus days or weeks, and the days between two dates
landed: 2026-10-14
decision: D-471
state: built
brief: M49's safe half, with no clock in it. A worked-out column or an identity can add a whole number of days or weeks to a date (`last_reviewed + 7 days`, `start + 2 weeks`, `due - 3 days`) and give the days between two dates (today `end - start` is the only date arithmetic, per a second project's planner session). Months are left out unless the decision argues them in: a month is not a fixed number of days, and the ledger's months (core/time.ts, D-023 calendar parts) are a separate thing. Compiled to SQLite date() so a filter and a sort see the same value as the screen; a date column empty makes the result empty and unchecked (D-138), never zero. The expression language's one spelling, in declare_format, extend_format, the .format.md syntax and the screen's column editor alike. Write the decision. Done-test: a synthetic format with last_reviewed and next_review = last_reviewed + 7 days shows, sorts and filters by the computed date; an identity using it is proved; suite, typecheck, build, build:plugin, docs:check.
