### M49 U2
milestone: M49
scope: engine
title: Today in questions, never in claims: due within, overdue, days left
landed: 2026-10-14
decision: D-472
state: built
brief: M49's line, to be written as a decision first: today belongs in questions, never in claims. A filter (`due is within 14 days`, `due is before today`, `due is after today`), a view's sort and a column shown on a screen or in format_rows (`days_left = due - today`) may read the clock; an identity, a claim, an aggregate a claim reads and a stored worked-out column may not, and declaring one that does is refused with that reason — a proof that held yesterday must not fail tomorrow with nothing changed. One clock for both halves: the app and the plugin each keep a today() (S-064, a deliberate twin), and this reads the same local date through whichever runtime asks; a test can pin it. The filter words join D-380's in parseFilter (M48 U1 makes multi-word members work first), so the filter band (M37 U3), a rollup's where and format_rows' match all say them. Done-test: a synthetic assignments format answers 'due within 14 days' identically on #/formats/<name>, in format_rows and in format_sheet, with the clock pinned in tests; declaring an identity that names today is refused with the reason; suite, typecheck, build, build:plugin, docs:check.
