commit: 0e9da04
report: Built `npx emerald-mcp init [path/to/document.emd]`, a subcommand of the server's bin (src/plugin/init.ts, wired in main.ts; no new bin, no package.json change). Run in a repository it (1) takes the named document, else .claude/emerald.json's, else the one .emd in the folder, else docs/memory.emd; creates it with the development pack as text inside the repo (committed, diffs) or SQLite bytes outside; an existing one is only read; writes .claude/emerald.json so hooks find it. (2) Appends/replaces one CLAUDE.md section between <!-- emerald-init: ... --> and <!-- /emerald-init -->: the start_here questions from the document's own views (new startTableOf, shared with the pack's startHereTable) and compactDeclarations' column lines; keeps the file's line endings, refuses an unclosed section. (3) Only where no emerald@ plugin is enabled (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.claude settings, or the repo's), merges the plugin's two hook commands pinned to PLUGIN_VERSION into .claude/settings.json; re-pins its own, leaves a foreign start-here hook and says so. (4) Prints what it wrote and start_here. Every file is compared before writing, so a second run is byte-identical. createDocumentFile takes an encoding. check-package.mjs step 4: npx -p <tarball> emerald-mcp init in an empty folder, runs the SessionStart hook it wrote (local hooks.mjs) and checks start_here, then a second run changes nothing — green on Node 24. init.test.ts: 8 tests incl. a declared column showing after extend_format. Full suite green (4877), typecheck, docs:check green after landing. docs/plugin.md: new 'A repository set up by one command' section, plus headings breaking the 243-line stretch after 916 and the 180-line one after 219. D-523. Not touched: hosts/claude, versions, pins. Note: the published 0.1.6 has no init (it starts the server); docs say from 0.2.0.

