### M51 F4
milestone: M51
scope: engine
title: A stalled unit can be taken over and shows itself; a landing names its commit and carries the child's report
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-501
state: built
brief: Found driving M42 on 2026-10-18 (the maintainer asked for all of these fixed). (1) TAKE OVER: a session interrupted mid-unit left M42 U4 in_progress with uncommitted work in the tree, nothing flagged it, and claim_units could not take it over, so the driver hand-edited taken_by. Give claim_units a take-over mode that names whose claim it replaces (refused unless the unit is in_progress and the named taker matches), keeps the previous taker on the row (in taken_by's history or a column of its own, the session's call), and resets started. And make a stalled claim visible: start_here (the development pack's views, src/data/packs/development/views.md) lists units in_progress for more than a day with no commit under a 'Stalled' heading. (2) COMMIT: M42 U2 and U4 landed with an empty commit column, because a landing in the same commit as the work cannot name itself; land_units refuses a landing with no `commit` unless told explicitly that the work is in the same commit (say the flag's name in the decision), and the closing pass's order (work commit, then land with that hash, then the landing commit) is M51 F5's. (3) REPORT: the host cuts a child session's note to the driver at 400 characters, so the driver pages the child's transcript to read its report. land_units takes a `report` (the child's closing report, plain text, bounded), stored on the unit row as a new `report` column of the development pack's unit format, so a driver reads it with one format_rows call; extend this repository's docs/memory.emd with it the way packs are kept again (M51 U9). (4) EDIT SHAPE: the driver took three tries at update_format_rows' shape (rows/match/set before edits/where/values); start_here's closing column list ends with one line showing a write's shape, e.g. `edits:[{where:{ref:…}, values:{…}}]`, generated, not hand-written. Tool descriptions read by a stranger stay free of D-/M-numbers (M42 U1). Done-test: tests for take-over (refused when the taker does not match, accepted when it does, previous taker kept), the Stalled list, the commit refusal, the report round trip; start_here's footer shows the edit line; parity (src/parity.test.ts) holds; build:plugin, the suite and docs:check are green. These tools ship in emerald-mcp, so the next npm version (0.1.2) carries them; publishing it is the maintainer's.
