### M51 F5
milestone: M51
scope: engine
title: The driver and the closing pass keep to one order, never commit over a child, and the timing test stops failing under load
landed: 2026-10-18
state: built
brief: Found driving M42 on 2026-10-18, the practice half of M51 F4. (1) ORDER: the closing-pass skill says, always, commit the work first, then land_units with that commit's hash (and the report F4 added), then commit the landing; M42 F2 did this by instinct (9d81f89 then e644ae6), M42 U2 and U4 did not and left the commit column empty. (2) TWO WRITERS: the run-milestone skill says that while a child session works in the same checkout, the driver writes no rows in docs/memory.emd and commits nothing there; a change the driver needs goes into the child's prompt for its landing, or waits until the child has landed (on 2026-10-18 the driver committed docs/memory.emd while a child had uncommitted work in the same folder, safe only because the child had not written its rows yet). Also: read a child's report from the unit's `report` column (F4) instead of paging the transcript; take over a stalled unit with claim_units' take-over mode (F4) after checking git status. (3) THE TIMING TEST: hosts/claude/hooks/commands.test.ts's 'prints the count in under 200 ms' failed under full-suite load in two separate sessions on 2026-10-18 and passed alone; make it hold under load without losing what it guards (the status line stays fast), e.g. the median of several runs, or run it outside the parallel pool; say which. (4) DEV DEPENDENCIES, added 2026-10-18 when the maintainer turned Dependabot alerts on: 10 open alerts, all development-scope in package-lock.json, none shipped (npm audit --omit=dev is 0): vite (high: server.fs.deny bypass on Windows alternate paths, fixed 6.4.3; two medium, fixed 6.4.2/6.4.3), vitest (critical: Vitest UI server file read/execute, fixed 3.2.6; medium mocker path traversal, fixed only in 4.1.11), tinypool (two critical prototype-pollution-to-RCE, fixed 2.1.1/2.1.2), esbuild (medium dev-server requests, fixed 0.25.0), sprintf-js (medium, no fix). Bump vite and vitest to their fixed versions within their current majors (and tinypool/esbuild with them, by override if needed); say whether vitest 4 for the mocker fix is a unit of its own; record each remaining alert's reason (dev-only, no fix) on this row and dismiss it in Dependabot only if the maintainer says so. Done-test: both skills say it; the test passes in three full-suite runs in a row; the Dependabot alerts left are listed here with their reasons; typecheck, build, build:plugin, build:demo and docs:check are green.
