report: "Built at 6420daf; docs:check green (0 errors); typecheck, build, build:plugin, build:demo green; full suite 4720/4720 three runs in a row.\n\n(1) ORDER. closing-pass step 2a now says the three steps, always: commit the work (own files only), land_units with commit: that hash and the report, commit the landing (docs/memory.emd alone), push. same_commit: true is named as the tool's option and this repository's no. Step 5 and the 'commit memory.emd' line follow the same order.\n\n(2) ONE WRITER. run-milestone: while a child works in this checkout the driver writes no memory.emd row and commits nothing there; a change goes into the child's prompt or waits for its landing; a commit that cannot wait touches only files outside the child's paths, never memory.emd, and the prompt says so. Step 3 reads the child's report from the unit's report column (format_rows ... columns:[ref, state, commit, report]); a stalled unit (start_here's Stalled) is taken over with claim_units take_over, after git status / git log, with any uncommitted files handed to the next child as a stopped session's, never discarded. The child prompt carries the closing order and 'your full report goes in the report column'.\n\n(3) TIMING TEST. Chose neither median nor a separate pool: the gate is now the status line's own process CPU time (process.cpuUsage at exit, preloaded with --import data: so the line's code is untouched), pair by pair against a bare Node run in the same moment; a pair passes under 200 ms CPU or within 150 ms of its bare Node, best of up to ten; wall time keeps a 1 s ceiling for a line that waits rather than works. Why: the first full run this session, still on the old test, failed exactly as reported (best 209 ms wall vs Node alone 57) — wall time under load measures the other workers. Measured under load: line 140-218 ms CPU, bare 15-93 (Windows ticks of ~15.6 ms); importing dist-plugin/server.mjs costs ~200 ms CPU on its own, so a line that loaded it would sit near 350 and fail.\n\n(4) DEV DEPENDENCIES. vite ^5.4 -> ^6.4.4 (esbuild 0.21 -> 0.25.12), vitest ^2.0.5 -> ^3.2.7, overrides tinypool ^2.1.2 (vitest 3 asks ^1.1.1; resolved 2.2.0, suite green). 'Within their current majors' was read as the majors the fixes are in: vite 5 and vitest 2 have no fixed release. npm audit: 14 -> 10 moderate, 0 high, 0 critical. Fixed: vite high + two medium, vitest critical (UI server), tinypool both critical, esbuild medium. LEFT, none dismissed: (a) @vitest/mocker medium path traversal (GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9): dev-only, fixed only in vitest 4.1.11; vitest 4 is a unit of its own (a major: pool and config changes across a 4,720-test suite) and worth one, small. (b) sprintf-js medium DoS (GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c), via electron-builder -> app-builder-lib -> @electron/get -> global-agent -> roarr: dev-only (the installer build), no fixed release; audit's only 'fix' is electron-builder 26.5.0, an older line. The other moderate counts are that chain's links. Dismissing either in Dependabot is the maintainer's call.\n\nNot verified: Dependabot's own list after the push (it re-scans package-lock.json on GitHub)."

### M51 F6
milestone: M52
scope: engine
title: Tests stop costing more than the work: measured, run on every push, and sessions run only what their change touches
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-515
state: built
brief: Maintainer, 2026-10-18: units took 13 to 40 minutes, and the tests took longer than the work. Cause: no CI runs the tests (.github/workflows has only demo.yml, registry.yml and release.yml), so every session runs all ~4,770 tests in 338 files itself, and briefs asked for repeat runs (M42 F3 ran the full suite five times). (1) MEASURE first: one full run with per-file durations (Vitest 4's reporter); write the slowest twenty files, the fixed startup cost and the total on this row's report. Five test files start real processes (hosts/claude/hooks/commands.test.ts, src/plugin/formatWatch.test.ts, registry.test.ts, subscriptions.test.ts, src/privacy.test.ts). (2) A TEST WORKFLOW: .github/workflows/test.yml runs typecheck and the full suite on every push to main (ubuntu-latest, Node 24, npm ci with the vendored SheetJS); demo.yml's deploy runs only after it passes (workflow_run, or one workflow with needs), so a red push never reaches getemerald.dev. The privacy test skips without ~/.emerald/denylist.txt by design; say what CI does about it. (3) THE SESSION RULE: docs/conventions.md, this repo's closing-pass and run-milestone skills, and the generic copies in hosts/claude/skills (M42 U7) say: while building and before the commit, run the tests related to the change (`npx vitest related <changed files> --run`) and typecheck; the full suite locally only when the change is broad (the engine core in src/domain/, a dependency, the test setup); CI runs the rest, and a red CI run is the next session's first task. Briefs stop asking for repeat full runs. (4) IF A FEW FILES DOMINATE: move them to a separate Vitest project or `npm run test:slow` that CI always runs and sessions rarely do. Done-test: a push shows test.yml green and the deploy following it; a deliberately failing test on a throwaway branch shows red and no deploy (then the branch is deleted); the measured before and after of a typical unit's local testing time are on this row's report; docs:check is green.
