report: "M51 F6 built at 0f5508f on worktree-agent-a382626d80a322b2d (three commits: ee9d513 work, 7cb6a89 Linux fixes, 0f5508f log). D-515.\n\nMEASURED (2026-10-22, maintainer's machine, 8 cores, Windows, Vitest 4.1.12, one full run): 340 files, 4,786 tests, 115 s (transform 22 s, import 113 s, tests 594 s summed over workers; 587 s of summed file time). Fixed startup of a one-file run: ~2.3 s wall (Vitest's own 0.3 s). Typecheck: 24 s. Slowest twenty files (s): plugin/tools/formats 28.2, tools/landing 25.6, tools/categorize 20.7, data/packs/ledger/pack 19.0, plugin/formatWatch 16.3, hosts/claude/hooks/commands 14.1, tools/ingest 14.1, plugin/server 13.3, tools/taxonomy 11.9, data/storage/encoding 11.4, data/scale 11.0, plugin/subscriptions 10.9, tools/searchDocument 10.2, tools/funds 10.1, tools/setup 9.2, tools/goalDeposits 9.1, tools/claim 9.0, tools/plan 8.5, tools/rules 8.4, tools/goalRhythm 8.3 = 338 s, 57% of the summed time; src/plugin/ is 333 s of 587. No few files dominate (top five = 19%, the slowest is 28 s of a 115 s wall), so no slow project / test:slow: it would hide the plugin's tests from the sessions that change the plugin, and related already runs a slow file only when touched.\n\nBEFORE / AFTER, a typical unit's local testing: before, the suite plus typecheck, ~140 s a run (140-165 s under the load of parallel worktrees), and several runs a unit (M42 F3: five). After, related + privacy + typecheck: a plugin change (M42 F16's files) related = 9 files, 22 s; a UI change (M42 F14's) 27 files, 26 s; plus typecheck 24 s and privacy ~5 s = ~50-55 s, once. A src/domain/format/ change (M42 F11's view.ts) is broad: related reaches 178 files, ~117 s, as the rule says.\n\nCI: .github/workflows/test.yml, on push to main and workflow_dispatch: npm ci (vendored SheetJS, no Electron binary), typecheck, npx vitest run; demo build needs test, deploy needs demo and runs only on main. demo.yml removed (one workflow so the chain is seen in one run and could be tried on a branch). Done-test on a throwaway branch (a temporary trigger line, deleted with the branch): run 39736428289 green (tests 5m36s, of which the suite 5m; demo build 2m26s; deploy skipped off main); run 39737370962 with a deliberately failing test: red, demo build and deploy skipped. Remote branch deleted. The first two runs were red for real, Linux-only: electron/windowsUpdater.test.ts asked for latest-linux.yml (now runs as Windows), and src/testing/setup.ts made the backups folder up front, which a fully skipped file (privacy, without its denylist) never removed (now tempPathSync, made by the first copy).\n\nPRIVACY in CI: runs when the repo has an EMERALD_DENYLIST secret (written to RUNNER_TEMP), skips otherwise; failures name file and denylist line, never a term. No secret is set: adding one is the maintainer's choice. Sessions now run src/privacy.test.ts before every commit, since related never reaches it.\n\nSESSION RULE: docs/conventions.md (testing bullet; Before you start item 2, a red CI run first), .claude/skills/closing-pass (step 3), .claude/skills/run-milestone (prompt; the driver reads gh run list after each unit, red is a stop), and the generic copies in hosts/claude/skills. A test that reads a changed file (a skill, a script, views.md) is named by path. The plugin is 0.1.6+1 (pin-plugin --plugin), because its skills changed.\n\nFOR THE DRIVER after merge+push: test.yml green on main and Demo build + Demo deploy following it; docs:check is green once this lands D-515's row (in the worktree its only error is that missing row). If M53 U2/U6 also cut the plugin, plugin.json/claude-plugin-release.json conflict: rerun node scripts/pin-plugin.mjs --plugin after merging."

### M51 U1
milestone: M51
scope: plugin
title: Every worktree finds the one canonical document
landed: 2026-10-17
decision: D-483
state: built
brief: `.claude/emerald.json` names the document relative to the checkout (`docs/memory.emd`), and the hooks (start_here at SessionStart, the inbox at UserPromptSubmit) resolve it the same way, so a session in a git worktree reads its branch's copy: rows recorded but not committed in the main checkout are invisible to it, and anything it writes lands in a copy that must later be merged as text. Resolve the configured document through `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` (the main working tree's root, i.e. the common dir's parent for a non-bare repo) so every worktree session reads and writes the main checkout's file; outside git, or in the main checkout, nothing changes. The lock (D-304) already makes concurrent writers safe, so nothing new is needed there. Add the guard half: a worktree branch never commits its own copy of the document (extend scripts/guard-memory-emd.mjs or a pre-commit check), since that copy is now never the one written. Say in the hook's output which file it read when it is not the checkout's own, so a session is never confused about it. Done-test: from a temporary worktree, the start_here hook prints rows recorded uncommitted in the main checkout; a record_format_rows from the worktree lands in the main checkout's file; the main checkout behaves as today; commands.test.ts covers both, with a real `git worktree add` in a temp dir (never junction node_modules into it).
