### M51 U2
milestone: M51
scope: development
title: A claim records the branch, a landing records the commit
landed: 2026-10-17
decision: D-484
state: built
brief: `taken_by` is free text (`agent 2...`), so the memory cannot answer which session has a unit, on which branch, and whether it landed. Add `branch` (text) and `commit` (text) to the development pack's `unit` format. `claim_units` takes an optional `branch` per claim (and `taken_by` carries whatever the host calls its session, e.g. a session id; the pack never depends on one host's session API, branch and commit are plain git); `land_units` takes the `commit` and refuses a landing on a unit claimed on another branch unless told. The roadmap and board views show branch beside taken_by, so `format_rows unit match:{state:in_progress}` is a live list of who is where. docs/memory.emd gains the columns through keep_packs (D-405). Done-test: a claim with a branch and a landing with a commit round-trip; a landing on the wrong branch is refused in the dry run; pack.test.ts's start_here table and column lines regenerate; the full suite is green.
