milestone: M51
scope: development
title: The files a unit touches are paths, and ready units come with which of them overlap
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-486
state: built
brief: A manager checked by eye that four of five units touched one file; `files` is free markdown, so nothing can compute it. Make the paths a unit touches machine-readable (a list column of paths beside or replacing `files`, keeping prose for notes like 'docs/mapping-templates.md if the reading changes'), and give dispatch one shaped answer: for a list of ready unit refs, each unit's brief with its linked decisions and blocks, plus which pairs share a path and so cannot run at once. A shaped tool or a start_here section, whichever fits the tool-surface rule (shaped, takes a list); not a general query. Overlap is only as good as the paths written at planning, and the answer says so. Converting existing rows is not this unit's (sole user, so old rows stay as they are): new and planned rows only. Done-test: five units, four sharing one path, come back as one runnable alone and four in sequence; a unit with no paths is reported as unknown, never as safe.
