### M51 U8
milestone: M51
scope: development
title: A session ends with the host's next-step box when it has one: Start the next unit is a button
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-490
state: built
brief: "D-258 says a closing message ends with what's next. The Claude desktop app now draws that itself: a next-step box at the end of a turn, with a recap, one question and buttons whose click sends a message. Teach closing-pass and run-milestone (this repo's, now) to end with it when the host offers one: the recap is what landed and what is not verified; the primary button is 'Start <next ready unit>' and sends the unit's ref with the instruction to claim it; a decision that is the maintainer's is the question. Where the host has no such box the closing message stays prose as today, so the skills say 'if the host offers a next-step box', never assume it. The generic copies M42 U7 ships inherit it. Done-test: a closing pass in the desktop app ends with the box whose first button names the next ready unit from start_here; in a host without it the message is unchanged.\n\n2026-10-18: fold in run-milestone driving units as the host's sessions instead of background Agent subagents, when the host offers them (the desktop app's start_session: a row the maintainer can open, watch, stop and talk to; a note back when it ends a turn). The driver M51 ran on 2026-10-18 still used Agent because step 2 of the skill says so, and nobody had revisited it since D-287. What M51 built is the groundwork: U1 (every worktree finds the canonical document), U3 (a child in its own worktree proposes its landing as an inbox row, the driver lands it with land_units inbox), U4 (which ready units overlap on paths). So: sequential units can share this checkout (use_worktree false, as today); units U4 reports as not overlapping may run in parallel, each in its own worktree, landing through U3's inbox rows. Mind the worktree cost on Windows: each needs its own npm install, and node_modules must never be junctioned into a worktree (git worktree remove deletes through it). A session's note to the driver is only its first 400 characters, so the driver keeps checking the commit, docs:check and the rows rather than trusting the note. Where the host has no sessions, the skill keeps the Agent tool as today. Write the reasoning as a decision row superseding the relevant part of D-287."
