### M51 U9
milestone: M51
scope: engine
title: Keeping a pack again brings its updated format notes and view settings, so nobody edits a document by hand
landed: 2026-10-18
decision: D-491
state: built
brief: Found twice on 2026-10-17: M51 U2 and M51 U3 changed the development pack's `unit` and `inbox` formats, and `keep_packs` on docs/memory.emd added the new columns and new views (D-405, D-443 for renames) but left the format's notes (the prose declaration) and a view's settings (e.g. the board's `taken_by: card`) as they were, so each session edited docs/memory.emd by hand to make pack.test.ts's drift checks pass. Make keeping a pack that a document already keeps bring the pack's current notes and view settings too, through the same dry run as today, which names each note and setting it would change. A setting the person changed in their own document (arrange_views on a pack format) needs a rule, said in the decision row: either the person's choice wins and the dry run says it was kept, or the pack's wins only when the document still holds the pack's previous value. Pick the one that never silently overwrites a person's choice. Both halves (D-227): the tool and the app's packs screen show the same plan. Done-test: a pack whose format notes and one view setting changed, kept again on a document holding the old pack, updates both and nothing else; a setting the person changed is not overwritten silently; running keep_packs on docs/memory.emd after this unit leaves pack.test.ts green with no hand edit; the full suite is green.
