### M53 F1
milestone: M53
scope: app
title: A list ticks only where someone said what done is, and the tick says what it sets
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-524
state: built
brief: Found in the 0.2.0 review (2026-10-22). On memory.emd's finding list, in the narrow list beside an entry, the maintainer ticked two rows by accident and their KIND changed from dead to bad. D-519's default guesses done = the first enum's last member, else the first boolean. So nearly every format's list carries ticks, and nothing on screen says what a tick writes. Maintainer: 'its just not clear what am i ticking and why does everything have a tick? who defines that?' Ruled: a tick only where someone said what done is, labelled with what it sets; no guessing. Write a decision row that amends D-519. (1) No default at all: a list shows ticks only when its view names the done column and member(s). That comes from the person, set in place from the list (a small control in the list's header, e.g. 'Tick to mark… <column> <member>', and 'No ticks'), from a conversation (arrange_views view:list, which already sets done), or from a pack's views.md. Without it the list is plain lines with no tick column, in the List tab and in the narrow list beside an entry alike. Drop the guess from view.ts and its tests. (2) The tick says what it sets: the header names it ('Ticking marks state done'), and each circle's hover and accessible name says it ('Mark done' / 'Undo: back to open'). (3) Undo: a tick shows a short undo in place, restoring the member it held, beyond the in-session untick. (4) The development pack's views.md declares done for its own formats: unit built, milestone closed, finding done, open_question answered, review_entry accepted, inbox applied. decision, rule and term get none. The ledger pack declares NONE (maintainer, 2026-10-22). Parity is unchanged: arrange_views already sets and clears done; show_format and formats' **List:** line show no tick and no done where none is set. Anything not decided here (beyond wording and the undo's timing) is the maintainer's: stop and ask (rule: Maintainer's decisions before briefs). Tests: a format with enums but no done set draws no ticks; finding's list ticks state to done; undo restores; the header names what is set. Done-test: on memory.emd, findings tick state (never kind), decisions show no ticks, and a person sets done on a task format from the list's header in place.
files: "src/domain/format/view.ts (listOf: no done default, tickWords)\nsrc/ui/formats/ListView.tsx (header tick control, labelled circles, Undo in place)\nsrc/ui/formats/Dashboard.tsx (tick labels only)\nsrc/data/packs/development/views.md, past.ts (done for unit, milestone, open_question, review_entry, inbox)\nsrc/data/repositories/formatViewRepository.ts (comment)\nsrc/ui/formats/listView.test.ts, src/parity.test.ts\ndocs/09-decision-log.md (D-524), docs/plugin.md\ndocs/memory.emd (list done set for unit, milestone, inbox, open_question, review_entry, finding)"
