state: built
brief: Found in the 0.2.0 review (2026-10-22). Maintainer: 'are saved views only created through format screen and then go into dashboard? a user cant create directly from dashboard?' Today Add a block (src/ui/formats/Dashboard.tsx, AddMenu) offers only saved views and rollups that already exist, plus Headline total, which is made in place. Its note reads 'A view is saved from its own tab with Save this view; a rollup is declared with the format.' That breaks the make-it-in-place rule. Ruled: New view and New chart made in place from Add a block, saved and placed in one step. Maintainer's answers, 2026-10-22: no mockup, build directly; New view makes list, table or board only. (1) New view: a small builder inside the Add a block panel. It takes the format (on the document's dashboard), the kind (list, table or board), the filter, order and columns, with the same pieces the format tab uses (ColumnFilter, ColumnMenu, ColumnsChoice; reuse, do not fork), and a name. Saving writes the saved view (format_saved_view, D-520) and the dashboard block together. The view is then in the rail like any other. (2) New chart: count or sum (which number or money column), by month of which date, grouped by which link (optional), and an optional filter. It declares the rollup the way the format's own form does (the same write a conversation makes), then places its chart. (3) Drop the 'saved from its own tab' note. Keep picking existing ones as now. Parity: a conversation already saves a view (arrange_views view:saved) and declares a rollup; adding the block is arrange_views view:dashboard. Say if one of these needs a new write, and if so it needs both halves (D-227). Write a decision row that amends D-521. Anything not decided here (beyond layout inside the panel and wording) is the maintainer's: stop and ask (rule: Maintainer's decisions before briefs). Tests: one step makes a saved view and its block; one step declares a rollup and its block; the made view appears in the rail. Done-test: on a synthetic task format's dashboard, 'Due today' and 'Done by month' made without leaving the dashboard.
