brief: Found in the 0.2.0 review (2026-10-22). The maintainer made a chart 'x' with F2's New chart on the document's dashboard, then looked for it under Decision in the rail to delete it and found nothing: 'i added "x" to decision view and i see nowhere to delete'. A chart is a rollup in the format's declaration. The rail lists only saved views, and no screen deletes a rollup: Remove on a dashboard block leaves the rollup, and only extend_format remove does it. It was removed by hand for the maintainer. Ruled (maintainer, 2026-10-22): list a format's charts in the rail beside its saved views, deletable there too. Do: (1) the rail lists each format's rollups under it beside its saved views (RailFolder, SavedRow's shape), each with a chart glyph rather than the filter glyph, opening its tab; rename and delete where it stands, Delete asking once. (2) Its tab on the format (RollupView) gets Delete too. (3) Deleting a rollup removes its dashboard blocks, as deleting a saved view does (dashboard.test.ts), and renaming follows. (4) A dashboard block's Remove keeps saying the chart stays and names where to delete it. Write a decision row that amends D-521 (the rail lists charts too). Parity: extend_format remove and rename already exist, and the screen half is what is missing (D-227). Anything else not settled here (beyond glyphs, wording and layout) is the maintainer's: stop and ask. Tests: a rollup is listed in the rail; deleting it on screen removes it and its blocks; a block's Remove leaves it. Done-test: make a chart from the dashboard, find it under its format in the rail, and delete it there without a conversation.
