commit: 9862eb9
report: "M53 F4 built at 9862eb9 (work) on main; docs:check green after the landing commit (its only error before was D-527's row, written here).\n\nWhat landed: a dashboard block is resized by dragging its edge - right edge width, bottom edge height, corner both - snapping as it goes to the grid's 4 columns and to rows of 40 px (16 px between), written once on release through setDashboardBlocks; each edge is also a focusable separator the arrow keys move a column/row at a time; dragging an edge never moves the block. A block given a height draws all its rows (to 200) and scrolls inside; a wider saved table shows more columns beside its name (1/2/4/6 at widths 1-4); a board of width 3-4 puts its lanes side by side; a rollup's chart is drawn to the block's height. A block with no size draws exactly as before. Kept as width (1-4) and height (2-20) on format_dashboard_block, migration 065, and as width:/height: lines in a text document's dashboard blocks. Parity: arrange_views view:dashboard size:[{name, width, height}], either alone; show_format view:dashboard draws it and its text names a sized block's size. Decision D-527 (amends D-521). docs/memory.emd's header moved to schema 65 (as U7 did for 64): the text document carries no size lines, so it is what the app's migration would write.\n\nChoices the brief left to the session: the handle's look (a 2 px accent line on the right/bottom edge on hover, a small diagonal mark in the corner on hover/focus, and a '4 columns · 8 rows' tag while dragging), the row unit (40 px), the minimum (1 column, 2 rows) and a maximum of 20 rows.\n\nVerified: dashboard.test.ts (a size kept and read back through arrange_views and through the screen's snapping and write helpers, a text document round-trips it, a block with no size draws and writes as before, refusals); related tests 189 files / 2365 tests green; typecheck and privacy green. In the browser on a synthetic task document: the corner drag of 'Open tasks' landed at 3 columns x 8 rows (710x432 px, the snapped grid exactly), the arrow key took it to 4, and it then showed all 10 open rows scrolling inside instead of 5 and '5 more'; a 4x6 table showed 6 columns, a 4-wide board its lanes side by side, a 4x8 chart fits (its chrome allowance raised from 64 to 88 px after it overflowed by 23 px); sizes held after export and reopen; at a 700 px window 4-wide blocks take both columns with no overflow; no console errors.\n\nNot done: node scripts/ask-cold.mjs ran but all 12 claude -p runs failed with 'Not logged in', so the cold read of the arrange_views description change (one key, size) is not done. check:tours not run (no tour drives a block's edge).\n\nFor the maintainer: the plugin must be rebuilt (npm run build:plugin; done in this checkout, but a running emerald server started before it refuses memory.emd until restarted) and a binary .emd is migrated by the app on open - back up real documents before the new app opens them, as with every migration. To judge: #/formats/<a format>/dashboard - drag a block's right edge, bottom edge and corner; wrong would be a block that does not snap, a drag that moves the block instead, or a size that does not hold after a reload."

