report: "M53 F5 built at e15535b; docs:check green (0 errors), related tests (101), privacy, typecheck and check:tours (10 runs) green. No new decision: D-521 says what a block's title opens and nothing about rows, so nothing it says changed.\n\nWhat landed: on a dashboard (a format's or the document's), a list block's line, a table block's row (every cell; only the first is a Tab stop) and a board block's card are links (react-router Link: Tab reaches, Enter opens) to the row's entry at entryPath + the saved view's address, with route state {from:'dashboard', dashboard}. The entry's back link reads '← Dashboard' and returns to that dashboard; paging and the list beside keep it. A list's tick is a button outside the link and never navigates. The title still opens the view in full. Charts, headline totals, and roadmap/ready blocks open no entry (the brief named list, table and board only). Links are draggable=false, so a drag from a row still moves the block; an edge drag released over a row resizes and opens nothing (checked in the browser).\n\nnav.ts: dashboardState, dashboardEntry, entryCame, entryBack (FormatRows' cameFrom folded into them). A view opened from a dashboard keeps '← Dashboard' on its own band and hands no dashboard state to entries opened from it, as before.\n\nVerified in the dev app on a synthetic task dashboard: clicked a task in a list block, the list beside held the block's 6 open rows (2 of 6), paged to another keeping '← Dashboard', clicked it back to #/formats/task/dashboard; a table date cell and a board card opened their entries; Enter on a focused row opened it; a tick ticked without navigating.\n\nFound along the way: the rail's own entry links (RailFolder) carry no route state, so following one from an entry opened on a dashboard drops '← Dashboard' for '← Task' — as it always did for List and Board. Tests render the dashboard with renderToStaticMarkup and mock the document store, since zustand serves SSR its first state.\n\nTo judge: #/formats/<name>/dashboard (or #/dashboard), click a row in a list block, page, then '← Dashboard'. Wrong would be: the tick opening the entry, the list beside holding every row rather than the block's, or the back link reading the format's name."

