decision: D-472
state: in_progress
brief: From the maintainer, 2026-10-23: a dashboard of the day he is watching must stay current, never hardcoded. Today (D-472, src/domain/format/clock.ts) a filter takes `today`, `before today`, `after today` and `within N days|weeks`, stored as words and worked out on read; but on screen a list's date filter (src/ui/formats/FilterBand.tsx, via columnValues) offers only the dates rows hold, as ticks, so ticking today saves a fixed date and the view is stale tomorrow. Only a dashboard total's conditions (src/ui/formats/dashboard.ts conditionsOf) and the Agenda offer words; a conversation can set them, the screen cannot (D-227). Maintainer's answers, 2026-10-23: (1) new words: `yesterday`, `tomorrow`, `last N days|weeks` (today and the N-1 days before it, the backward twin of `within`), and `this|last|next week`, `this|last|next month`, `this|last|next year`; (2) a date column's filter menu offers the words, old and new, above its ticks, written exactly as a conversation types them (`before today`, never a gloss like Overdue), and a view saved from it keeps the words; (3) which day a week starts on is a DOCUMENT setting, not an app preference, because the plugin and another machine must name the same rows; set on screen in the document's settings and from a conversation (parity, D-227; the document's currency is the nearest precedent), and Monday (ISO) when a document sets none; (4) periods use the local calendar day, the clock `today` already reads. A claim still may not read the clock (CLOCK_REASON). Write a decision row amending D-472. Anything not settled here (beyond the menu's look, and where the week-start control sits in settings) is the maintainer's: stop and ask (rule: Maintainer's decisions before briefs). Tests: each new word's range against a pinned today, with the week starting Monday by default and Sunday when set; the menu writes words and a saved view reads back current on another pinned day; parity for the week-start setting; a text document round-trips it. Done-test: on a synthetic task document, save a list view filtered `due is this week` from the menu, move the pinned day a week on and it holds the new week; set the week start to Sunday from a conversation and the screen agrees.
files: src/domain/format/clock.ts and span.ts (the words and their ranges); src/ui/formats/FilterBand.tsx and src/data/repositories/formatValuesRepository.ts (the menu offers words); src/ui/formats/dashboard.ts (a total's conditions); the document's settings, where its currency is kept, and a migration if the setting needs a column (docs/04-data-model.md); src/plugin/tools/ and docs/plugin.md (the words in tool descriptions; the setting from a conversation); src/parity.test.ts
