### M53 U1
milestone: M53
scope: app
title: A mockup: a lighter entry page, quick add and a list view for tasks
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-514
state: built
brief: Mockup first, as M35 U1 did; the maintainer approves it before U2-U4 build (he said the UI as it is is not nice, so this is his taste to judge, not a driver's). Start by trying the current entry page (src/ui/formats/EntryView.tsx, entryLayout in src/domain/format/view.ts) and the Add flow (entry/new, three steps, every column) on a synthetic task format with ~12 columns (title, state enum, due date, priority, project link, notes markdown, a few optional ones), and say what is clunky. Then draw, in the app's own tokens (src/ui/theme/tokens.css, the rule rows with scope ui): (1) the entry page lighter: a filled entry shows the fields that hold a value plus '+ field' for the rest; hidden fields and how to reveal them; reordering by dragging the field itself or a compact list of names, not a separate arrange mode; whether a long page groups or folds; (2) a new entry that asks for the required fields and the ones the view chose; (3) the list view: one line per row, a done tick (the state enum's done member or a boolean), the title, due relative to today, chips, grouped by a column, collapsible groups; (4) quick add: type a title and Enter at the top of a list or a group, the row taking the values its view implies (the group's member, a 'due today' filter's date). Keep the list beside an open entry (EntryList, which the maintainer likes). Labels name exactly what they cover; make it in place (count click paths). Synthetic data only. Done-test: a mockup file the maintainer has approved, and the decisions it settles written into U2-U4's briefs.
