### M53 U2
milestone: M53
scope: ui
title: Hiding fields on an entry, and reordering that is light
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-517
state: built
brief: "Was Later U-entry-layout, moved into M53 on 2026-10-22. Maintainer, 2026-10-20, after weeks on a real format with many columns: arranging an entry page (moving the fields) is clunky, and a page with many columns feels heavy; some fields should be hidden by the person's choice. Build U1's approved mockup for: (1) a lighter way to reorder, in place of the separate 'Arrange this view' mode and its small handle (EntryView.tsx, setEntryOrder, D-296): drag the field itself, or a compact list of names; (2) hiding a field in the entry view, kept with the view's order in format_view_column and views.md, and the same in arrange_views so a conversation can do it too (parity, D-227); a hidden field is still in the format, the table and every tool, and how its value shows when it holds one is what the mockup settled; (3) grouping or folding a long page, if the mockup kept it. Labels name exactly what they cover; make it in place. Done-test: a field hidden and the page reordered on screen and by arrange_views, each seen by the other; parity.test.ts green; a text document round-trips both.\n\nSETTLED by U1's approved mockup (docs/mockups/m53-u1/tasks.html, approved 2026-10-22; port its markup and words): (a) The Arrange mode goes. One 'Fields' list replaces it, behind the icon where Arrange was (aria-label 'Fields: order, shown, new entry'): every column but the title in this view's order, sectioned by entryLayout's part (Line under the title, Figures, Text), each row a grip, the name in words, 'needed' or 'holds a value', an eye (Shown), and a 'New entry' checkbox (U3 reads it). Drag a row to move it; Alt+Up/Down on a focused row moves it a step. A field moves only within its part, as the order works today, and the list's sections make that plain. (b) A shown field can also be dragged by its label on the page, within its part; its ⋯ menu (where Show as is) adds Move up, Move down and Hide. (c) Hiding is per entry view, kept beside the order in format_view_column's setting string and views.md. A hidden field is not drawn even when it holds a value; the title and a needed (required) column cannot be hidden. 'N hidden' at the end of the entry's Empty line (U3) shows the hidden fields in place, dimmed, with a 'hidden' tag, until the entry is left ('Hide again'). A hidden field stays in the table, every tool and the list view's line. (d) No grouping or folding into sections: hiding empty fields (U3) is what makes a page short; only a long Markdown text folds, after about twelve lines, behind 'Show all N lines'. (e) arrange_views takes hidden and the 'new entry' mark as well as order (parity)."
