### M53 U3
milestone: M53
scope: app
title: A filled entry shows what it holds, and a new one asks for what is needed
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-518
state: built
brief: "Build U1's approved mockup for the entry's empty fields and the new-entry form. On an entry that exists, a column with no value is not drawn; a '+ field' control lists them and adds one in place (the field opens, writes when left, as now). A required column with no value is always drawn and says it is needed. entry/new shows the required columns and the ones the entry view marks to show (or U2's not-hidden ones), with '+ field' for the rest; the draft and Add/Cancel stay. Worked-out columns and checks follow the same rule (shown when they have a value). Mind entryLayout's parts (title, header line, figures, texts, links) so a part with nothing drawn leaves no empty heading. The frame (src/frame) draws the same page read-only. Done-test: on a synthetic task with 12 columns and 4 filled, the page shows 4 plus '+ field'; a new task shows only what is required and chosen; tests in EntryView's suite.\n\nSETTLED by U1's approved mockup (docs/mockups/m53-u1/tasks.html, approved 2026-10-22, choice 1 as A; port its markup and words): (a) Empty fields are offered as ONE LINE OF NAMES at the foot of the entry's left column, after a hairline: the label 'Empty', then '+ <name>' per column that holds no value and is not hidden, one click each; then 'N hidden' at the end of the line (U2). Clicking a name opens that field where it belongs in the order, focused; left empty it folds back into the line. Not a '+ Field' menu (option B, rejected). (b) Labels read as words: underscores become spaces (done_on reads 'done on'), and a unit suffix is dropped from the label (estimate_h reads 'estimate', the h shown on the value). Only the label changes. (c) Two figures or fewer, with no claim to lay them out as a grid, sit in the line under the title instead of a figures part of their own (a lone '3 h' no longer gets a section). (d) entry/new keeps the list beside it (EntryList, with the draft as a row in the group it will land in, 'A new task' until titled), and asks for: the title (focused), every required column, and the columns ticked 'New entry' in U2's Fields list; everything else is on the Empty line. A new entry has no 'Links here'. Nothing about what is missing is said until Add is pressed; then one line in negative names it ('A task needs a title.'). Enter in the title adds. (e) A required enum that nothing implies starts at its first member on a new entry (a new task is inbox): a default the view applies, never a value a model makes; the same rule serves U4's quick add. (f) The list beside an entry gains a '+' (aria 'Add a task') that opens entry/new, so adding from an open entry is two steps, not four."
