report: "M53 U3 built at 9657597 on main. D-518. docs:check green after this landing (its only error before was D-518's missing row).\n\nLANDED: U1's mockup choice A for empty fields. EntryView draws a row's filled columns plus every required one (needed while empty); the rest are the Empty line at the foot ('Empty', '+ name' each, in view order, then U2's 'N hidden' folded in at its end). A name opens the field in place, focused (an enum's menu opens); left empty it folds back; a field being typed in stays drawn until left. Labels are words without a unit suffix (estimate_h reads estimate, h on the value), in the Fields list too. <=2 plain figures sit in the line under the title unless a check / worked-out figure / total / roomy way claims the grid. Worked-out figures and totals drawn only with a value. entry/new: title focused, required + New-entry-ticked columns, rest on the Empty line, no Links here, list kept beside it with the draft as its first marked row ('A new task' until titled), Add never disabled, 'A task needs a title.' only after Add, Enter in the title adds. A required enum starts at its first member (entryDefaults; FormatRows merges it into the blank draft and ignores it for 'Nothing has been filled in yet.'). EntryList '+' (aria 'Add a task') opens entry/new. Read-only (a pack's, the frame) draws the same page with no names to fill.\n\nDEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF: the brief said checks follow the 'shown when they have a value' rule. Checks stay always drawn: unchecked is a verdict, and the timesheet tour highlights an unchecked verdict-hours_paid (its story is 'the claim can't say yet'). Said in D-518.\n\nTOUR: the timesheet tour typed into an empty 'end'; it now clicks empty-end first (new step 19, later steps renumbered; rows.test.ts allows empty-* anchors). check:tours: every tour played (10 runs).\n\nTESTS: new src/ui/formats/EntryView.test.ts (11, the done-test: 12-column task with 4 filled draws exactly those 4 and names the 8 others; a new task draws title, state, due, project with due/project ticked; no Links here; no problem text before Add; hidden beats New entry); view.test.ts +7 for entryLabel, entryNeeds, entryDefaults, entryShown. vitest related over the four touched sources: 179 files / 2196 tests green; typecheck clean; privacy green. Full suite not run (domain change is view.ts helpers only).\n\nBROWSER: dev app with a made-up 12-column task: existing entry drew title/state/due/estimate + Empty line of 8; '+ notes' opened focused and folded back when left empty (focus events had to be dispatched by hand because the pane was hidden); '+ priority' opened its menu; the list '+' opened entry/new with state inbox, title focused, draft row 'A new task' -> typed title; Add empty said 'A task needs a title.'; Enter in the title added and landed on the new row.\n\nLEFT FOR U4: the list has no groups, so the draft row sits first rather than in its group; entryDefaults takes `implied` for quick add. The top bar still says '← Task', not the mockup's '← List' (not in this brief)."

### M53 U4
milestone: M53
scope: engine
title: The list view: one line per row, a done tick, grouped by a column, and quick add
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-519
state: built
brief: "A new view kind, 'list', in VIEW_KINDS (src/domain/format/view.ts), settings in format_view_column and views.md like the board's: 'group' (an enum, a link or a date bucket; none by default), 'done' (the enum member(s) or boolean that tick a row; default the state enum's last member, as agenda's 'done' does), 'line' (columns after the name, shown per D-402's ways). Any format has one at #/formats/<name>/list and in the View select. A row is one line: the tick, the name, the line columns; clicking the name opens the entry with the list beside it. Ticking is update_format_rows's checks and updateRow, as moving a card on the board is. Quick add: a line at the top of the list and of each group, Enter writes a row with the name typed and the values the view implies (the group's member, the address filter's exact values), refusing as record_format_rows does when a required column has no value (it then opens entry/new with what it has). Parity (D-227): show_format view:list draws it (src/plugin/tools/sheet.ts VIEWS, the frame's routes), arrange_views sets group/done/line, and a row added in place is record_format_rows. Follow U1's mockup. Done-test: the synthetic task format as a list grouped by project, ticked and added to in place, in the app and drawn by show_format; parity.test.ts green.\n\nSETTLED by U1's approved mockup (docs/mockups/m53-u1/tasks.html, approved 2026-10-22; port its markup and words): (a) 'List' is a tab in the format's one tab strip beside Table and Board. Under it, the settings sit in place as one 32px row of menus, never a settings screen: 'Group by <column>', 'Ticked when <state is done>', 'Line <columns>', and the address filter's chip when there is one. (b) A row is one 40px line: the tick (a 16px square, filled ink when ticked), the title (opens the entry), then the line's columns right-aligned: an enums column as dot-chips (text with a small dot, no pill), a link's name (left out when grouped by it), and due relative to today, right-aligned: 'today', 'tomorrow', 'Sat, in 2 days' within a week, then '5 Nov'; a late open row reads 'N days late' ('yesterday' for one) in negative, the one colour on the line. Default line: tags, project, due. (c) Group by takes an enum (a group per member), a link (a group per row in the target's order, then 'No <column>'), or a date in buckets: Late, Today, Tomorrow, In the next 7 days, Later, No due date. Group heads are 32px with a chevron, the name and the count of open rows; groups fold (grid-template-rows). Grouped by the column that ticks a row, done is the last group; otherwise each group's ticked rows fold at its foot as 'N done', which opens them. (d) The tick sets the done member; untick restores the member the row held before the tick, else the first member. A ticked row stays in place, struck, for about a second, then sinks into 'N done'. (e) Quick add is a line at the top of the list and of each group whose value is one value (Late, In the next 7 days and Later have none, so no line). Its placeholder names every value the row will take besides its title: 'Add a task · inbox, Garden shed', '… due today'. Enter writes the title, the group's value, the address filter's exact values, and a required enum's first member when nothing implies one (U3's rule); the new row grows into place with a brief accent-soft mark, and the line keeps focus for the next; Esc clears. A required column it still cannot fill opens entry/new with what it has. (f) EntryList, the list beside an open entry, becomes the same list, narrow: the same groups (24px heads), ticks and quick add (one line at the top), the title with due · project under it. Clicking a title in the list view opens the entry with it beside. One list in two widths, so its settings hold in both. (g) New on-screen words, to become term rows when this lands: List, N done, Group by / Ticked when / Line, and quick add's placeholder."
