report: M53 U4 built at 124a17d (D-519). A 'list' view kind: every format has one at #/formats/<name>/list. Settings are words one column holds together (group, line, done <members>), set in place under the List tab by Group by / Ticked when / Line menus, and by arrange_views view:list (whole setting per column; group and done move off the column that held them, keeping its line). Groups: enum members (done last when grouped by the tick's column), a link's rows in the target's order then 'No <col>', or date buckets Late/Today/Tomorrow/In the next 7 days/Later/No <col> date. Each group's ticked rows fold as 'N done'. The tick is the board's move (updateRow through the same checks); untick restores the previous member. Quick add at the top of each one-value group: placeholder names every value ('Add a task · inbox, Garden shed'), Enter writes via stageRows/insertRows (record_format_rows' batch), keeps focus, marks the new row accent-soft; a required column nothing fills opens entry/new with the draft. EntryList is the same list narrow (24px heads, tick, due · link under the title, one quick add at the top, the new-entry draft in the group it will land in); past 1000 rows it draws flat and windowed. The View <select> became the format's tab strip (Table, Board, List, Roadmap, Ready to start, rollups). show_format view:list names each group's rows with their tick; formats prints a **List:** line. Verified: listView.test.ts (11), parity, full suite once, typecheck, check:tours (10 runs), and the browser on a synthetic task document (grouped by project, added, ticked/sank/unticked back to waiting, entry beside the list, draft in No project). Not done: the cold read (scripts/ask-cold.mjs) could not run — the claude CLI here is not logged in; the tool description changes are one clause each in show_format and arrange_views. Left: the entry bar still says '← Task' and goes to the table even when opened from the list (the mockup's '← List'); Line has no word for an empty line (unticking every column gives the default back); Ticked when offers one member, several only through arrange_views; a self-link (blocked_by) is offered as a grouping.

