ed to schema 63 in the work commit (a text document with no saved view changes in nothing else); any emerald plugin process built before d20b5e7 now refuses memory.emd (UNREADABLE) until rebuilt/restarted - npm run build:plugin and restart the emerald server (this landing was written by a fresh build over stdio). Not done: ask-cold.mjs could not run here (the claude CLI is not logged in), so the tool-description changes were not read cold; they add parameters only, no framing. The agenda has no saved views (it is every dated format's).

### M53 U6
milestone: M53
scope: app
title: Charts of a rollup, from one general chart
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-516
state: built
brief: Every chart today is the ledger's (MonthChart, NetTrend, BalanceChart, BalanceLine, AmountHistory, PlanBar, Year's private YearBars and Spark); src/ui/charts/ holds only colours and useWidth. Make one general chart in src/ui/charts/ that takes plain series (labels, one or more series of figures, a unit or currency for the axis): bars and a line, hand-rolled SVG, the theme's tokens and categoryPalette, light and dark, read by a screen reader as a table. RollupView (src/ui/formats/RollupView.tsx) gains a chart beside its table: bars by month, one series per group when the rollup groups by a link. Money stays Money until it is drawn (never a number in the domain). The ledger charts may move onto it where it is a straight swap; none has to. The frame draws a rollup's chart too. Done-test: a rollup on a synthetic format drawn as bars and as a line in the app and the frame; the chart's own tests; no ledger import from src/ui/charts/.
files: src/ui/charts/chart.ts, src/ui/charts/Chart.tsx, src/ui/charts/chart.test.ts, src/ui/charts/categoryPalette.ts, src/ui/formats/rollupChart.ts, src/ui/formats/rollupChart.test.ts, src/ui/formats/RollupView.tsx, src/ui/theme/tokens.css, docs/09-decision-log.md
taken_by: run-milestone driver
started: 2026-10-22
branch: worktree-agent-a55f1f9ab4b315ff9
commit: 5d39450
paths: src/ui/charts/, src/ui/formats/RollupView.tsx
report: M53 U6 built at 5d39450 on worktree-agent-a55f1f9ab4b315ff9. One general chart, src/ui/charts/Chart.tsx over plain data in chart.ts: labels, series of Money / plain figures / a said word / nothing, an axis in a currency or a unit; bars or a line, hand-rolled SVG in the theme tokens, light and dark, the picture aria-hidden and an sr-only table reading every point. RollupView draws its rollup above the table with a Bars/Line toggle, one series per linked row (rollupChart.ts); what the chart cannot hold is said under it. The frame draws it through FormatRows' View menu, unchanged (no new FrameView, so show_format cannot open on a rollup yet). categoryPalette.ts now declares the Category shape it reads instead of importing the ledger's type, so chart.test.ts checks the whole folder imports no ledger. tokens.css gains .fc-grow (bars grow once) and the chart's hover classes. Ledger charts not moved. Verified in the worktree's dev server on a synthetic expense/project document (bars 19 rects, line 4 paths, light and dark) and in the frame stand-in (try-frame) with the same counts. docs:check fails on this branch only for D-516's missing row, which this landing writes. check:tours skipped: no tour passes a rollup view.

### M53 U7
milestone: M53
scope: app
title: Dashboards: one per format and one for the document, made only of views
landed: 2026-10-22
decision: D-521
state: built
brief: A dashboard is an ordered set of blocks, each one of: a saved view (U5) drawn in its kind, compact; a rollup's chart (U6); a headline total (a count, or a sum of a money or number column, under a filter, as format_rows match takes). Nothing else (D-514): no free text, no embeds. One per format at #/formats/<name>/dashboard, and one for the document (its home for a document with no ledger; decide with the maintainer where it sits beside the ledger's Home when both exist). Arranged in place: add a block from the views and rollups the format has, drag to reorder, remove; a block opens its view in full. Kept beside the views (format_view_column or what U5 chose; views.md in a text document). Parity: arrange_views adds, orders and removes blocks; show_format view:dashboard draws it; start_here unchanged. Mockup the dashboard before building (a small one, against U1's look). Done-test: the synthetic task format's dashboard with 'Due today', 'Open by project', a monthly done-count chart and an open count, made on screen and by a conversation, drawn by show_format; a document-wide one with blocks from two formats. Maintainer, 2026-10-22: the mockup (docs/mockups/m53-u7/dashboard.html, 5b7166c) is approved as recommended; port its markup and words. (a) Placement, option 1: the document's dashboard is its own rail item, 'Dashboard' — without a ledger it is first and #/ opens it (today #/ goes to Formats); with the ledger it sits right under Home, and Home stays #/. (b) A format's Dashboard tab comes last in its tab strip, and the format still opens on Table. (c) Storage: a new table format_dashboard_block (migration 064), and a '### <format> dashboard' block in views.md for a text document; not format_view_column (U5's reason: a setting is one word of at most 32 characters).
files: src/data/db/migrations/064_dashboard_block.sql, src/domain/format/view.ts, src/domain/format/document.ts, src/data/repositories/formatViewRepository.ts, src/data/repositories/formatRowRepository.ts (sumColumn), src/ui/formats/dashboard.ts, src/ui/formats/Dashboard.tsx, src/ui/screens/Dashboard.tsx, src/ui/screens/FormatRows.tsx, src/ui/screens/FormatLinkViews.tsx, src/ui/formats/FilterBand.tsx, src/ui/nav.ts, src/ui/NavGlyph.tsx, src/App.tsx, src/frame/routes.tsx, src/frame/host.ts, src/frame/contract.ts, src/plugin/tools/dashboard.ts, src/plugin/tools/views.ts, src/plugin/tools/sheet.ts, fixtures/synthetic/demo/tour_step.format.md, docs/04-data-model.md, docs/plugin.md
blocks: ["M53 U4","M53 U5","M53 U6"]
taken_by: run-milestone driver
started: 2026-10-22
branch: main
commit: 2057542
paths: src/ui/formats/, src/ui/screens/, src/domain/format/view.ts, src/plugin/tools/
report: M53 U7 built at 2057542 (D-521). Dashboards, ported from the approved mockup: a block is a saved view drawn compact in its kind (list: 5 open lines + N more / N done, 2 a group when grouped; table 4 rows; board lanes; roadmap/ready 5 names), a rollup's chart (bars, 150px) or a headline total (count, or sum of a money/integer/real/decimal column, under a filter kept as an address; money per currency); nothing else. Four-column grid (total 1, others 2). Add a block (saved views + rollups, grouped by format on the document's; Headline total made in place with conditions from the saved views, the list's done turned round and date windows; figure live before Add), drag by grip, menu Open in full / Move earlier / Move later / Remove from this dashboard; list ticks work on the dashboard. A block's title opens it in full (saved view at its address, rollup on its tab, total as the list of its rows) with '← Dashboard' back. Placement per the verdict: format's dashboard = last tab after a rule, format still opens on Table; document's = rail 'Dashboard', first and #/ without a ledger, right under Home with one. Storage: format_dashboard_block (migration 064); saved-view rename/delete cascades; deleteFormat clears; text docs write '### <format> dashboard' / '### Document dashboard'. Parity: arrange_views view:dashboard add/order/remove (no format = document's); show_format view:dashboard draws it in the frame and names each block's contents; formats lists a format's blocks; start_here unchanged. 'Dashboard' is now refused as a saved view's name. Done-test: on screen in the browser (task dashboard with Due today, Open by project, done_by_month chart, Open count; the document's with Book and Task blocks plus a book headline total) and by conversation in src/plugin/tools/dashboard.test.ts. Rollup names are snake_case by the declaration's rule, so the chart block is 'done_by_month', not 'Done by month' as the mockup drew it. Tests: full suite green once (one bidi-truncation finding fixed after), typecheck, privacy, docs:check, check:tours green after the custom tour gained a first step clicking Formats (#/ now opens the dashboard). Not done: ask-cold could not run (the claude CLI in its sandbox is not logged in). The engine-only tool text budget rose 56k -> 56.5k after trimming. Servers need a rebuild and restart (schema 64).

